registerFaith({code:'ne',
stories:[
{id:'fgospel',kind:'solo',title:'The Gospel',ne:'सुसमाचार',
sections:[
{id:'gospel',t:'The whole story in short',ne:'सुसमाचार — छोटकरीमा',art:FNE_ART.ovstory,
paras:[
['सुरुमा परमेश्वरले पृथ्वी र त्यसमा भएका सबै थोक बनाउनुभयो। अनि उहाँले मानिसलाई आफ्नै स्वरूपमा बनाउनुभयो — सम्बन्धको लागि, प्रेमको लागि।','Surumaa Parameshwarle prithvi ra tyasmaa bhaekaa sabai thok banaunubhayo. Ani uhaanle maanislaai aaphnai swaroopmaa banaunubhayo — sambandhako laagi, premko laagi.','In the beginning God created the earth and everything in it. And he made human beings in his own image — for relationship, for love.','Genesis 1:26–27'],
['मानिस र परमेश्वरको बीचमा मित्रता थियो। तर मानिसले परमेश्वरको विरुद्धमा विद्रोह गर्ने बाटो रोज्यो — र त्यही विद्रोहले हामीलाई परमेश्वरबाट अलग गर्यो।','Maanis ra Parameshwarko beechmaa mitrataa thiyo. Tara maanisle Parameshwarko biruddhamaa vidroha garne baato rojyo — ra tyahi vidrohale haamilaai Parameshwarbaata alag garyo.','Humanity and God shared friendship. But human beings chose the road of rebellion against God — and that rebellion separated us from him.','Genesis 3'],
['विद्रोह रोज्ने त हामी नै थियौं — तैपनि परमेश्वरले हामीलाई यति प्रेम गर्नुभयो कि उहाँले त्यो भाँचिएको सम्बन्ध निको पारेर फेरि जोड्ने योजना बनाउनुभयो।','Vidroha rojne ta haami nai thiyaun — taipani Parameshwarle haamilaai yati prem garnubhayo ki uhaanle tyo bhaanchieko sambandha niko paarera pheri jodne yojanaa banaunubhayo.','We were the ones who chose to rebel — yet God loved us so much that he made a plan to heal that broken relationship and join it back together.','Genesis 3:15'],
['त्यसैले परमेश्वरले एउटा जाति छान्नुभयो — इस्राएल। अब्राहाम नाम गरेका एक जना साधारण मानिसबाट सुरु भएको त्यो जातिलाई उहाँले प्रतिज्ञा दिनुभयो — तिमीहरूद्वारा संसारका सबै जातिले आशिष् पाउनेछन्। त्यही जातिद्वारा उहाँले सारा संसारमा निको पार्ने काम र मुक्ति ल्याउनुहुनेथियो।','Tyasaile Parameshwarle eutaa jaati chhaannubhayo — Israel. Abrahaam naam garekaa ek janaa saadhaaran maanisbaata suru bhaeko tyo jaatilaai uhaanle pratigyaa dinubhayo — timiharudwaaraa sansaarkaa sabai jaatile aashish paaunechhan. Tyahi jaatidwaaraa uhaanle saaraa sansaarmaa niko paarne kaam ra mukti lyaunuhunethiyo.','So God chose one nation — Israel. It began with a single ordinary man named Abraham, and God promised him: through you, all the peoples of the earth will be blessed. Through this nation God would bring healing and salvation to the whole world.','Genesis 12:1–3'],
['किनभने सयौं वर्षपछि, त्यही जातिबाट, येशू आउनुभयो। उहाँ कन्याबाट जन्मनुभयो; उहाँ परमेश्वरका पुत्र हुनुहुन्छ। उहाँ हामीलाई हाम्रो विद्रोहबाट बचाउन र परमेश्वरसँगको हाम्रो सम्बन्ध निको पार्न आउनुभयो।','Kinabhane sayaun barshapachhi, tyahi jaatibaata, Yeshu aaunubhayo. Uhaan kanyaabaata janmanubhayo; uhaan Parameshwarkaa putra hunuhunchha. Uhaan haamilaai haamro vidrohabaata bachaauna ra Parameshwarsangako haamro sambandha niko paarna aaunubhayo.','Because hundreds of years later, from that very nation, Jesus came. He was born of a virgin; he is the Son of God. He came to save us from our rebellion and to heal our relationship with God.','Matthew 1:18–23 · Luke 19:10'],
['यो यसरी भयो — येशू हाम्रा पापको लागि बलिको रूपमा क्रूसमा मर्नुभयो। अनि तेस्रो दिन उहाँ मृत्युबाट जीवित हुनुभयो — जुन अन्धकारमा हामी मानिसहरू फसेका थियौं, त्यसैलाई उहाँले जित्नुभयो।','Yo yasari bhayo — Yeshu haamraa paapko laagi baliko rupmaa kroosmaa marnubhayo. Ani tesro din uhaan mrityubaata jeewit hunubhayo — jun andhakaarmaa haami maanisharu phasekaa thiyaun, tyasailaai uhaanle jitnubhayo.','It happened like this: Jesus died on the cross as the sacrifice for our sins. And on the third day he rose from the dead — overcoming the very darkness we humans were trapped in.','1 Corinthians 15:3–4'],
['आज येशू जीवित हुनुहुन्छ र परमेश्वरको दाहिने हातपट्टि हुनुहुन्छ। जसले उहाँमाथि विश्वास गरेर उहाँलाई पछ्याउँछ, त्यो परमेश्वरको परिवारमा फर्काइन्छ — परमेश्वरकै सन्तान भएर।','Aaja Yeshu jeewit hunuhunchha ra Parameshwarko daahine haatpatti hunuhunchha. Jasle uhaanmaathi vishwaas garera uhaanlaai pachhyaunchha, tyo Parameshwarko pariwaarmaa pharkaainchha — Parameshwarkai santaan bhaera.','Today Jesus is alive, seated at the right hand of God. And whoever believes in him and follows him is brought home into God’s family — as God’s own child.','Hebrews 12:2 · John 1:12'],
['विश्वास गर्नेहरूलाई परमेश्वरले आफ्नो पवित्र आत्मा दिनुहुन्छ — परमेश्वर आफैँ हामीभित्र बास गर्नुहुन्छ, सान्त्वना दिनुहुन्छ र दिनदिनै बाटो देखाउनुहुन्छ।','Vishwaas garneharulaai Parameshwarle aaphno Pawitra Aatmaa dinuhunchha — Parameshwar aaphain haamibhitra baas garnuhunchha, saantwanaa dinuhunchha ra dindinai baato dekhaunuhunchha.','To those who believe, God gives his Holy Spirit — God himself making his home within us, comforting us and guiding us day by day.','John 14:16–17'],
['र एक दिन येशू फेरि आउनुहुनेछ। उहाँले सबै थोक नयाँ बनाउनुहुनेछ — न आँसु, न मृत्यु — र परमेश्वर आफ्ना मानिसहरूसँग सधैँको लागि बास गर्नुहुनेछ।','Ra ek din Yeshu pheri aaunuhunechha. Uhaanle sabai thok nayaan banaunuhunechha — na aansu, na mrityu — ra Parameshwar aaphnaa maanisharusanga sadhainko laagi baas garnuhunechha.','And one day Jesus will come again. He will make all things new — no more tears, no more death — and God will dwell with his people forever.','Revelation 21:1–4'],
['यही सन्देशले विश्वास गर्ने हरेकलाई निको पार्छ र फेरि जोड्छ — हाम्रो र परमेश्वरको बीचको सङ्गति फर्काइदिन्छ। यही नै सुसमाचार हो — हामीले कमाएको होइन, परमेश्वरले दिनुभएको उपहार।','Yahi sandeshle vishwaas garne hareklaai niko paarchha ra pheri jodchha — haamro ra Parameshwarko beechko sangati pharkaaidinchha. Yahi nai susamaachaar ho — haamile kamaaeko hoina, Parameshwarle dinubhaeko upahaar.','This message brings healing and restoration to everyone who believes it — it gives back the fellowship between us and God. This is the gospel: not something we earn, but a gift God gives.','Romans 1:16 · Ephesians 2:8–9'],
['यो मानिसजातिको लागि परमेश्वरको योजना र उहाँले सारा संसारमा कसरी मुक्ति ल्याउनुभयो भन्ने कुराको सार हो। अब यहाँबाट हामी यही कथा सुरुदेखि, एक-एक घटना गरेर, विस्तारमा हेर्नेछौं।','Yo maanisjaatiko laagi Parameshwarko yojanaa ra uhaanle saaraa sansaarmaa kasari mukti lyaaunubhayo bhanne kuraako saar ho. Aba yahaanbaata haami yahi kathaa surudekhi, ek-ek ghatanaa garera, vistaarmaa hernechhaun.','This is an overview of God’s plan for humanity, and how he brought salvation to the whole world. From here, we will walk through the same story from the beginning — one moment at a time, in detail.']]}]},
{id:'fstory',kind:'arc',title:'God’s Story',ne:'परमेश्वरको कथा',
sections:[
{id:'creation',t:'In the beginning',ne:'सुरुमा',art:FNE_ART.creation,
note:['परमेश्वरलाई हाम्रो खाँचो थिएन — उहाँले हामीलाई चाहनुभयो। मानिस उहाँसँगको मित्रताको लागि बनाइएको हो, र कथा त्यो मित्रता पूर्ण भएको असल संसारबाट सुरु हुन्छ।','Parameshwarlaai haamro khaancho thiena — uhaanle haamilaai chaahanubhayo. Maanis uhaansangako mitrataako laagi banaieko ho, ra kathaa tyo mitrataa purna bhaeko asal sansaarbaata suru hunchha.','God did not need us — he wanted us. Human beings were made for friendship with their Maker, and the story opens in a good world where that friendship is whole.'],
paras:[
['सुरुमा परमेश्वरले आकाश र पृथ्वी बनाउनुभयो। सबै कुरा असल थियो।','Surumaa Parameshwarle aakaash ra prithvi banaunubhayo. Sabai kuraa asal thiyo.','In the beginning God made the heavens and the earth. Everything he made was good.','Genesis 1'],
['परमेश्वरले मानिसलाई आफ्नै स्वरूपमा बनाउनुभयो — पुरुष र स्त्री।','Parameshwarle maanislaai aaphnai swaroopmaa banaunubhayo — purush ra stree.','God made human beings in his own image — male and female.','Genesis 1:27'],
['स्वरूपमा बनाइनुको अर्थ गहिरो थियो — हामीले परमेश्वरको चरित्र र स्वभाव सारा सृष्टिको सामु झल्काउनुपर्थ्यो। बाँकी सृष्टिभन्दा फरक, मानिस उहाँकै प्रतिबिम्ब हुन बनाइएको थियो।','Swaroopmaa banaainuko artha gahiro thiyo — haamile Parameshwarko charitra ra swabhaaw saaraa srishtiko saamu jhalkaunuparthyo. Baanki srishtibhandaa pharak, maanis uhaankai pratibimba huna banaaieko thiyo.','And being made in his image meant something deep: humans were to reflect the character and nature of God to the whole creation. Unlike the rest of what he made, we were made to be his likeness.','Genesis 1:26–28'],
['परमेश्वरले मानिसलाई भन्नुभयो — फल्दै-फुल्दै जाओ, र यस पृथ्वीको हेरचाह गर।','Parameshwarle maanislaai bhannubhayo — phaldai-phuldai jaao, ra yas prithviko herchaah gara.','God told the humans: be fruitful, and take care of this earth.','Genesis 1:28 · 2:15'],
['अदन नाम गरेको एउटा बगैंचामा मानिसहरू परमेश्वरसँगै बस्थे। उहाँ तिनीहरूसँग त्यहीँ हिँड्नुहुन्थ्यो — मानिस र परमेश्वरको बीचमा अटुट सम्बन्ध, मीठो सङ्गति थियो।','Adan naam gareko eutaa bagainchaamaa maanisharu Parameshwarsangai basthe. Uhaan tiniharusanga tyahin hindnuhunthyo — maanis ra Parameshwarko beechmaa atut sambandha, meetho sangati thiyo.','The humans dwelt with God in a garden called Eden. He would walk with them there — an unbroken relationship, sweet fellowship between humanity and God.','Genesis 2:8 · 3:8'],
['बगैंचाको बीचमा एउटा रूख थियो। परमेश्वरले भन्नुभयो — त्यसको फल नखाओ; खायौ भने तिमी मर्नेछौ। किनभने प्रेम गर्नुहुने परमेश्वरले हामीलाई सधैँ रोज्ने ठाउँ दिनुहुन्छ — उहाँसँगको सम्बन्ध चाहन्छौं कि चाहँदैनौं, त्यो हामीले नै रोज्नुपर्छ।','Bagainchaako beechmaa eutaa rukh thiyo. Parameshwarle bhannubhayo — tyasko phal nakhaao; khaayau bhane timi marnechhau. Kinabhane prem garnuhune Parameshwarle haamilaai sadhain rojne thaaun dinuhunchha — uhaansangako sambandha chaahanchhaun ki chaahandainaun, tyo haamile nai rojnuparchha.','In the middle of the garden stood one tree, and God said: do not eat its fruit — if you eat it, you will die. Because the God who loves always leaves us a choice: do we want relationship with him, or not? That choice is ours to make.','Genesis 2:16–17'],
['परमेश्वरले आफ्नो सबै कामलाई हेर्नुभयो र भन्नुभयो — धेरै असल छ। अनि सातौं दिनमा उहाँले विश्राम गर्नुभयो।','Parameshwarle aaphno sabai kaamlaai hernubhayo ra bhannubhayo — dherai asal chha. Ani saataun dinmaa uhaanle vishraam garnubhayo.','God looked at all he had made and said: it is very good. And on the seventh day he rested.','Genesis 1:31 · 2:2–3']]},
{id:'fall',t:'The break',ne:'सङ्गति भाँचियो',art:FNE_ART.fall,
note:['परमेश्वरका मार्गहरूलाई इन्कार गर्ने त मानिसहरू नै थिए — तैपनि परमेश्वरले तिनीहरूलाई बचाउने योजना बनाउनुभयो।','Parameshwarkaa maargaharulaai inkaar garne ta maanisharu nai thie — taipani Parameshwarle tiniharulaai bachaaune yojanaa banaunubhayo.','Even though it was humans who rejected God’s ways, God still made a plan to save them.'],
paras:[
['ती पहिला मानिसहरूका नाम आदम र हव्वा थिए। तर त्यो असल बगैंचामा एक दिन एउटा सर्प आयो — र त्यसले झूट बोल्यो। दुःखको कुरा, आदम र हव्वाले परमेश्वरको वचन छोडेर सर्पकै कुरामा विश्वास गरे — र तिनीहरूले त्यो फल खाए।','Ti pahilaa maanisharukaa naam Aadam ra Hawwaa thie. Tara tyo asal bagainchaamaa ek din eutaa sarpa aayo — ra tyasle jhoot bolyo. Dukhako kuraa, Aadam ra Hawwaale Parameshwarko wachan chhodera sarpakai kuraamaa vishwaas gare — ra tiniharule tyo phal khaae.','The names of those first humans were Adam and Eve. But one day, into that good garden, came a serpent — and it told a lie. Sadly, Adam and Eve let go of God’s word and believed the snake instead — and they ate the fruit.','Genesis 3:1–6'],
['सर्पको झूट यस्तो थियो — यो फल खायौ भने तिमीहरू परमेश्वरजस्तै हुनेछौ। परमेश्वरलाई भरोसा गर्न सकिँदैन; उहाँले तिमीहरूबाट असल कुरा लुकाउँदै हुनुहुन्छ।','Sarpako jhoot yasto thiyo — yo phal khaayau bhane timiharu Parameshwarjastai hunechhau. Parameshwarlaai bharosaa garna sakindaina; uhaanle timiharubaata asal kuraa lukaaundai hunuhunchha.','The lie went like this: eat this fruit, and you will become like God. God cannot be trusted — he is withholding good things from you.','Genesis 3:4–5'],
['फल खानेबित्तिकै तिनीहरूको हृदय दोष र लाजले भरियो — र तिनीहरू लुके। पहिलो पटक मानिस परमेश्वरदेखि डरायो।','Phal khaanebittikai tiniharuko hridaya dosh ra laajle bhariyo — ra tiniharu luke. Pahilo patak maanis Parameshwardekhi daraayo.','The moment they ate, guilt and shame flooded their hearts — and they hid. For the first time, humans were afraid of God.','Genesis 3:7–10'],
['तैपनि परमेश्वरले तिनीहरूलाई खोज्दै आउनुभयो र सोध्नुभयो — तिमी कहाँ छौ? अनि उहाँले आफ्नै हातले तिनीहरूलाई लुगा लगाइदिनुभयो।','Taipani Parameshwarle tiniharulaai khojdai aaunubhayo ra sodhnubhayo — timi kahaan chhau? Ani uhaanle aaphnai haatle tiniharulaai lugaa lagaaidinubhayo.','Yet God came looking for them and asked: where are you? And with his own hands he clothed them.','Genesis 3:9 · 3:21'],
['जब परमेश्वरले सोध्नुभयो, आदमले हव्वालाई दोष दिए, र हव्वाले सर्पलाई। पापले हामीलाई एकअर्काबाट पनि टाढा बनाउँछ।','Jaba Parameshwarle sodhnubhayo, Aadamle Hawwaalaai dosh die, ra Hawwaale sarpalaai. Paaple haamilaai ekarkaabaata pani taadhaa banaunchha.','When God asked what had happened, Adam blamed Eve, and Eve blamed the serpent. Sin pushes us apart from one another too.','Genesis 3:12–13'],
['परमेश्वरको आज्ञा नमान्नु नै पाप हो। पापले मानिस र परमेश्वरको सङ्गति भाँच्यो।','Parameshwarko aagyaa namaannu nai paap ho. Paaple maanis ra Parameshwarko sangati bhaanchyo.','Turning from God’s command — that is sin. And sin broke the fellowship between humanity and God.','Genesis 3:8–10'],
['परमेश्वरले भन्नुभएको कुरा दुःखसाथ पूरा भयो। उहाँले तिनीहरूलाई अदन छोड्न भन्नुभयो — र त्यही दिनदेखि मानिस र परमेश्वरको बीचमा अलगाव आयो। तैपनि उहाँले प्रतिज्ञा दिनुभयो — एक दिन एक जना उद्धारक आउनुहुनेछ।','Parameshwarle bhannubhaeko kuraa dukhasaath puraa bhayo. Uhaanle tiniharulaai Adan chhodna bhannubhayo — ra tyahi dindekhi maanis ra Parameshwarko beechmaa alagaaw aayo. Taipani uhaanle pratigyaa dinubhayo — ek din ek janaa uddhaarak aaunuhunechha.','What God had said would happen, sadly happened. He told them to leave Eden — and from that day there has been a separation between humanity and God. Yet he gave a promise: one day a Rescuer would come.','Genesis 3:15']]},
{id:'spread',t:'Sin spreads',ne:'पाप फैलियो',art:FNE_ART.spread,
note:['पाप एक जना व्यक्तिमै रोकिँदैन — त्यो परिवार र समाजभरि फैलिन्छ। तर खराबी बढ्दै जाँदा पनि परमेश्वरले अनुग्रहमै काम गरिरहनुभयो — उहाँले नोआको परिवारलाई जोगाउनुभयो र संसारलाई नयाँ सुरुवात दिनुभयो।','Paap ek janaa vyaktimai rokindaina — tyo pariwaar ra samaajbhari phailinchha. Tara kharaabi badhdai jaandaa pani Parameshwarle anugrahamai kaam garirahanubhayo — uhaanle Noaako pariwaarlaai jogaunubhayo ra sansaarlaai nayaan suruwaat dinubhayo.','Sin never stays with one person — it spreads through families and whole societies. Yet even as evil grew, God kept acting in grace: he preserved Noah’s family and gave the world a fresh start.'],
paras:[
['पाप संसारभरि फैलियो। मानिसको मन परमेश्वरबाट टाढा भयो।','Paap sansaarbhari phailiyo. Maanisko man Parameshwarbaata taadhaa bhayo.','Sin spread through the whole world, and the human heart drifted far from God.','Genesis 4–6'],
['बगैंचा बाहिरको पहिलो परिवारमै त्यो देखियो — दाजु कयिनले डाहले भरिएर आफ्नै भाइ हाबिललाई मार्यो। कथाको पहिलो मृत्यु नै हत्या थियो।','Bagainchaa baahirako pahilo pariwaarmai tyo dekhiyo — daaju Kayinle daahale bhariera aaphnai bhaai Haabillaai maaryo. Kathaako pahilo mrityu nai hatyaa thiyo.','It showed in the very first family outside the garden: the elder brother, Cain, filled with envy, killed his own brother Abel. The first death in the story was a murder.','Genesis 4:8'],
['मानिसको खराबी देखेर परमेश्वरको हृदय दुख्यो।','Maanisko kharaabi dekhera Parameshwarko hridaya dukhyo.','When God saw the evil of humanity, his heart was grieved.','Genesis 6:5–6'],
['संसार हिंसाले यति भरियो कि परमेश्वरले त्यसलाई ठूलो बाढीले धुने निर्णय गर्नुभयो। तर एक जना विश्वासयोग्य मानिस थिए — नोआ। परमेश्वरले तिनलाई एउटा विशाल जहाज बनाउन लगाउनुभयो।','Sansaar hinsaale yati bhariyo ki Parameshwarle tyaslaai thulo baadhile dhune nirnaya garnubhayo. Tara ek janaa vishwaasyogya maanis thie — Noaa. Parameshwarle tinlaai eutaa vishaal jahaaj banaauna lagaunubhayo.','The world filled with such violence that God resolved to wash it clean with a great flood. But there was one faithful man — Noah. God had him build an enormous boat.','Genesis 6:11–14'],
['तैपनि परमेश्वरले संसारलाई छोड्नुभएन। नोआको परिवारमाथि उहाँले अनुग्रह देखाउनुभयो।','Taipani Parameshwarle sansaarlaai chhodnubhaena. Noaako pariwaarmaathi uhaanle anugraha dekhaunubhayo.','Even so, God did not abandon the world. He showed grace to Noah and his family.','Genesis 6–9'],
['नोआबाट परमेश्वरले संसारलाई नयाँ सुरुवात दिनुभयो — ठीकसँग जिउने एउटा नयाँ मानिस-परिवार। तर मानिसको हृदय भने उस्तै रह्यो। पाप फेरि फैलिन थाल्यो — नयाँ सुरुवातले मात्र पुगेन।','Noaabaata Parameshwarle sansaarlaai nayaan suruwaat dinubhayo — theeksanga jiune eutaa nayaan maanis-pariwaar. Tara maanisko hridaya bhane ustai rahyo. Paap pheri phailina thaalyo — nayaan suruwaatle maatra pugena.','Through Noah God gave the world a fresh start — a new human family meant to live rightly. But the human heart stayed the same. Sin began to spread again — a fresh start alone was not enough.','Genesis 9:20–21 · 11'],
['धेरै पछि मानिसहरू एउटा ठाउँमा भेला भए र आकाशसम्म पुग्ने धरहरा बनाउन थाले — परमेश्वरविना नै ठूलो बन्न। त्यो ठाउँको नाम बाबेल थियो।','Dherai pachhi maanisharu eutaa thaaunmaa bhelaa bhae ra aakaashsamma pugne dharaharaa banaauna thaale — Parameshwarwinaa nai thulo banna. Tyo thaaunko naam Baabel thiyo.','Much later, people gathered in one place and began building a tower to reach the sky — to become great without God. The place was called Babel.','Genesis 11:1–4'],
['बाबेलमा मानिसहरूले आफ्नै नाम ठूलो बनाउन खोजे। तर परमेश्वरको योजना अझै अगाडि बढिरहेको थियो।','Baabelmaa maanisharule aaphnai naam thulo banaauna khoje. Tara Parameshwarko yojanaa ajhai agaadi badhiraheko thiyo.','At Babel people tried to make their own name great. But God’s plan kept moving forward.','Genesis 11'],
['परमेश्वरले तिनीहरू सबैलाई फरक-फरक भाषा बोल्ने बनाउनुभयो — र मानिसहरू सारा पृथ्वीभरि छरिए।','Parameshwarle tiniharu sabailaai pharak-pharak bhaashaa bolne banaunubhayo — ra maanisharu saaraa prithvibhari chharie.','God made them all speak different languages — and so the people scattered across the whole earth.','Genesis 11:8–9']]},
{id:'abraham',t:'A promise to Abraham',ne:'अब्राहामलाई प्रतिज्ञा',art:FNE_ART.abraham,
note:['भाँचिएको संसारको लागि परमेश्वरको जवाफ — एउटा साधारण परिवार। अब्राहामद्वारा सबै जातिले आशिष् पाउने प्रतिज्ञाबाटै सुसमाचार सुरु हुन्छ — र त्यो नेपालसम्म पनि आइपुग्छ।','Bhaanchieko sansaarko laagi Parameshwarko jawaaph — eutaa saadhaaran pariwaar. Abrahaamdwaaraa sabai jaatile aashish paaune pratigyaabaatai susamaachaar suru hunchha — ra tyo Nepaalsamma pani aaipugchha.','God’s answer to a broken world is, surprisingly, one ordinary family. The promise that ALL nations would be blessed through Abraham is where the good news begins — and it reaches Nepal too.'],
paras:[
['ती छरिएका जातिहरूका बीचबाट — नोआकै सन्तानमध्येबाट — परमेश्वरले एक जना मानिसलाई छान्नुभयो — अब्राहाम, ऊर भन्ने शहरका एक साधारण मानिस।','Ti chhariekaa jaatiharukaa beechbaata — Noaakai santaanmadhyebaata — Parameshwarle ek janaa maanislaai chhaannubhayo — Abrahaam, Ur bhanne shaharkaa ek saadhaaran maanis.','From among those scattered peoples — from the line of Noah himself — God chose one man: Abraham, an ordinary man from a city called Ur.','Genesis 11:31 · 12:1'],
['परमेश्वरले अब्राहामलाई बोलाउनुभयो — तिम्रो परिवारद्वारा संसारका सबै जातिले आशिष् पाउनेछन्।','Parameshwarle Abrahaamlaai bolaunubhayo — timro pariwaardwaaraa sansaarkaa sabai jaatile aashish paaunechhan.','God called Abraham: through your family, all the peoples of the earth will be blessed.','Genesis 12:1–3'],
['परमेश्वरले अब्राहामलाई किन छान्नुभयो? उनी अरूभन्दा धर्मी भएकाले होइन। परमेश्वर कृपामा धनी हुनुहुन्छ र मानिसजातिलाई बचाउन चाहनुहुन्थ्यो। हामीले उहाँलाई छोड्ने हरेक कारण दिएका थियौं — तैपनि आफ्नो महान् प्रेम र उदारताको कारण उहाँले हामीलाई छोड्नुभएन।','Parameshwarle Abrahaamlaai kina chhaannubhayo? Uni arubhandaa dharmi bhaekaale hoina. Parameshwar kripaamaa dhani hunuhunchha ra maanisjaatilaai bachaauna chaahanuhunthyo. Haamile uhaanlaai chhodne harek kaaran diekaa thiyaun — taipani aaphno mahaan prem ra udaarataako kaaran uhaanle haamilaai chhodnubhaena.','Why did God choose Abraham? Not because he was more righteous than others. God is rich in mercy, and he wanted to save humanity. We had given him every reason to abandon us — yet because of his great love and generosity, he did not.','Ephesians 2:4 · Deuteronomy 7:7–8'],
['अब्राहामले आफ्नो घर, आफ्नो देश छोडेर हिँडे — कहाँ जाने भन्ने पनि थाहा थिएन। विश्वास भनेको यस्तै हिँडाइ हो।','Abrahaamle aaphno ghar, aaphno desh chhodera hinde — kahaan jaane bhanne pani thaahaa thiena. Vishwaas bhaneko yastai hindaai ho.','Abraham left his home and his country without even knowing where he was going. That walk is what faith looks like.','Hebrews 11:8'],
['एक रात परमेश्वरले उनलाई बाहिर लैजानुभयो र भन्नुभयो — आकाशतिर हेर, र सक्छौ भने ताराहरू गन। तिम्रा सन्तान त्यति नै धेरै हुनेछन्।','Ek raat Parameshwarle unlaai baahira laijaanubhayo ra bhannubhayo — aakaashtira hera, ra sakchhau bhane taaraaharu gana. Timraa santaan tyati nai dherai hunechhan.','One night God led him outside and said: look up and count the stars — if you can. That is how many your descendants will be.','Genesis 15:5'],
['अब्राहामले परमेश्वरलाई विश्वास गरे, र परमेश्वरले उनलाई धर्मी ठहराउनुभयो।','Abrahaamle Parameshwarlaai vishwaas gare, ra Parameshwarle unlaai dharmi thaharaunubhayo.','Abraham trusted God — and God counted him as righteous.','Genesis 15:6'],
['तर एउटा समस्या थियो — अब्राहाम र उनकी पत्नी सारा वृद्ध थिए, र तिनीहरूको कुनै सन्तान थिएन। प्रतिज्ञा असम्भवजस्तो सुनिन्थ्यो। तैपनि ठीक समयमा साराले छोरो जन्माइन् — इसहाक, जसको नामको अर्थ हो हाँसो। परमेश्वरको लागि असम्भव केही रहेनछ।','Tara eutaa samasyaa thiyo — Abrahaam ra unki patni Saaraa vriddha thie, ra tiniharuko kunai santaan thiena. Pratigyaa asambhawjasto suninthyo. Taipani theek samayamaa Saaraale chhoro janmaain — Isahaak, jasko naamko artha ho haanso. Parameshwarko laagi asambhaw kehi rahenachha.','But there was a problem: Abraham and his wife Sarah were old, and they had no child at all. The promise sounded impossible. Yet at just the right time Sarah bore a son — Isaac, whose name means laughter. Nothing, it turned out, is impossible for God.','Genesis 18:10–14 · 21:1–6'],
['यही एउटा परिवारबाट परमेश्वरको उद्धारको कथा अगाडि बढ्यो।','Yahi eutaa pariwaarbaata Parameshwarko uddhaarko kathaa agaadi badhyo.','From this one family, God’s rescue story moved forward.','Genesis 12–50']]},
{id:'exodus',t:'Rescue from Egypt',ne:'मिश्रबाट छुटकारा',art:FNE_ART.exodus,
note:['इस्राएल आफू बलियो भएर स्वतन्त्र भएको होइन — परमेश्वरले अब्राहामको परिवारसँग गर्नुभएको प्रतिज्ञा पूरा गर्नुभयो। उहाँले सुन्नुहुन्छ, काम गर्नुहुन्छ — र उहाँको बाटोमा कुनै साम्राज्य अड्न सक्दैन।','Israel aaphu baliyo bhaera swatantra bhaeko hoina — Parameshwarle Abrahaamko pariwaarsanga garnubhaeko pratigyaa puraa garnubhayo. Uhaanle sunnuhunchha, kaam garnuhunchha — ra uhaanko baatomaa kunai saamraajya adna sakdaina.','Israel did not walk free because they were strong — God kept the promise he had made to Abraham’s family. He hears, he acts, and no empire can stand in his way.'],
paras:[
['समय बित्दै जाँदा अब्राहामको परिवार बढेर ठूलो जाति बन्यो — त्यस जातिको नाम इस्राएल हो। तर तिनीहरू मिश्र भन्ने देशमा पुगे, र त्यहाँका राजाले तिनीहरूलाई कमारा बनाए। चार सय वर्षसम्म तिनीहरूले दुःख पाए। तिनीहरूले परमेश्वरलाई पुकारे — र उहाँले सुन्नुभयो।','Samaya bitdai jaandaa Abrahaamko pariwaar badhera thulo jaati banyo — tyas jaatiko naam Israel ho. Tara tiniharu Mishra bhanne deshmaa puge, ra tyahaankaa raajaale tiniharulaai kamaaraa banaae. Chaar saya barshasamma tiniharule dukha paae. Tiniharule Parameshwarlaai pukaare — ra uhaanle sunnubhayo.','As time passed, Abraham’s family grew into a great people — a people called Israel. But they ended up in a country called Egypt, and its king made them slaves. For four hundred years they suffered. They cried out to God — and he heard.','Exodus 1 · 2:23–25'],
['परमेश्वरले आफ्ना मानिसहरूको दुःख देख्नुभयो, र तिनीहरूलाई मिश्रबाट निकालेर ल्याउन मोशा नाम गरेका एक जना मानिसलाई पठाउनुभयो।','Parameshwarle aaphnaa maanisharuko dukha dekhnubhayo, ra tiniharulaai Mishrabaata nikaalera lyaauna Moshaa naam garekaa ek janaa maanislaai pathaunubhayo.','God saw the suffering of his people, and he sent a man named Moses to lead them out of Egypt.','Exodus 3'],
['मिश्रका राजाले इस्राएलीहरूलाई जान दिन इन्कार गरे। तर धेरै आश्चर्यकर्म र चमत्कारहरूद्वारा परमेश्वरले राजालाई बाध्य पार्नुभयो — र उनले तिनीहरूलाई स्वतन्त्र छोडे।','Mishrakaa raajaale Israeliharulaai jaana dina inkaar gare. Tara dherai aashcharyakarma ra chamatkaarharudwaaraa Parameshwarle raajaalaai baadhya paarnubhayo — ra unle tiniharulaai swatantra chhode.','The king of Egypt refused to let the Israelites go. But through many wonders and miracles God forced him to set them free.','Exodus 7–12'],
['ती आश्चर्यकर्म र चमत्कारहरूले सबै जातिहरूलाई देखाए — परमेश्वर कुनै पनि साम्राज्यभन्दा शक्तिशाली हुनुहुन्छ।','Ti aashcharyakarma ra chamatkaarharule sabai jaatiharulaai dekhaae — Parameshwar kunai pani saamraajyabhandaa shaktishaali hunuhunchha.','Those wonders and miracles showed all the nations that God is more powerful than any empire.','Exodus 9:16'],
['परमेश्वरले तिनीहरूसँग करार बाँध्नुभयो र तिनीहरूकै बीचमा बास गर्नुभयो।','Parameshwarle tiniharusanga karaar baandhnubhayo ra tiniharukai beechmaa baas garnubhayo.','God made a covenant with them and came to dwell right among his people.','Exodus 19–40'],
['करार भनेको साधारण वाचा होइन — विवाहजस्तै दुई पक्षलाई जोड्ने गहिरो प्रतिज्ञा हो। परमेश्वरले भन्नुभयो — म तिमीहरूको परमेश्वर हुनेछु, र तिमीहरू मेरा मानिसहरू हुनेछौ। अनि उहाँले तिनीहरूलाई जिउने तरिकाको निम्ति मार्गदर्शन पनि दिनुभयो।','Karaar bhaneko saadhaaran waachaa hoina — vivaahajastai dui pakshalaai jodne gahiro pratigyaa ho. Parameshwarle bhannubhayo — ma timiharuko Parameshwar hunechhu, ra timiharu meraa maanisharu hunechhau. Ani uhaanle tiniharulaai jiune tarikaako nimti maargadarshan pani dinubhayo.','A covenant is no casual promise — it is a deep, binding pledge that joins two parties, like a marriage. God said: I will be your God, and you will be my people. And he gave them guidance for their whole way of life.','Exodus 6:7 · 19–20'],
['अनि परमेश्वर विश्वासयोग्य रहनुभयो — तिनीहरूले उहाँलाई पछ्याउँदा, उहाँले तिनीहरूलाई चाहिने सबै थोक जुटाइदिनुभयो।','Ani Parameshwar vishwaasyogya rahanubhayo — tiniharule uhaanlaai pachhyaundaa, uhaanle tiniharulaai chaahine sabai thok jutaaidinubhayo.','And God was faithful: as they followed him, he provided everything they needed.','Exodus 16–17'],
['तर परमेश्वरले यति ठूलो विश्वासयोग्यता र कृपा देखाउनुभएर पनि इस्राएलले घरिघरि विद्रोह गर्ने र उहाँको अगुवाइलाई इन्कार गर्ने बाटो रोज्यो। त्यसैले उही चक्र घुमिरह्यो — पाप, परमेश्वरको न्याय र अनुशासन, मानिसहरूको पश्चात्ताप — अनि तिनीहरूलाई फेरि ग्रहण गर्नुहुने परमेश्वरको कृपा।','Tara Parameshwarle yati thulo vishwaasyogyataa ra kripaa dekhaunubhaera pani Israelle gharighari vidroha garne ra uhaanko aguwaailaai inkaar garne baato rojyo. Tyasaile uhi chakra ghumirahyo — paap, Parameshwarko nyaaya ra anushaasan, maanisharuko pashchaattaap — ani tiniharulaai pheri grahan garnuhune Parameshwarko kripaa.','Yet even though God showed such radical faithfulness and mercy, Israel still chose again and again to rebel and reject his leadership. So the same cycle kept turning: sin, God’s judgment and discipline, the people’s repentance — and God’s mercy receiving them back.','Exodus 32 · Numbers 14'],
['मोशाले इस्राएललाई चालीस वर्षसम्म डोर्याए। उनीपछि यहोशू नाम गरेका अगुवाले मानिसहरूलाई डोर्याउन थाले।','Moshaale Israellaai chaalis barshasamma doryaae. Unipachhi Yahoshu naam garekaa aguwaale maanisharulaai doryaauna thaale.','Moses led Israel for forty years. After him, a leader named Joshua began to lead the people.','Deuteronomy 34 · Joshua 1']]},
{id:'kings',t:'Kings and prophets',ne:'राजा र अगमवक्ताहरू',art:FNE_ART.kings,
note:['हरेक राजा असफल हुन्छ — र त्यही नै मुख्य कुरा हो। कथाले हामीलाई अझ असल राजाको प्रतीक्षा गर्न सिकाउँछ — जसको राज्य कहिल्यै सिद्धिँदैन।','Harek raajaa asaphal hunchha — ra tyahi nai mukhya kuraa ho. Kathaale haamilaai ajha asal raajaako pratikshaa garna sikaunchha — jasko raajya kahilyai siddhindaina.','Every king fails — and that is the point. The story is training us to long for a better King, whose kingdom never ends.'],
paras:[
['मिश्रबाट निस्केपछि परमेश्वरले इस्राएललाई प्रतिज्ञा गरिएको देशमा ल्याउनुभयो। त्यहाँ तिनीहरू बसे, र समय बित्दै जाँदा तिनीहरूले भने — अरू जातिहरूका जस्तै हामीलाई पनि राजा चाहिन्छ।','Mishrabaata niskepachhi Parameshwarle Israellaai pratigyaa garieko deshmaa lyaunubhayo. Tyahaan tiniharu base, ra samaya bitdai jaandaa tiniharule bhane — aru jaatiharukaa jastai haamilaai pani raajaa chaahinchha.','After Egypt, God brought Israel into the land he had promised. There they settled — and in time they said: give us a king, like all the other nations have.','Joshua · 1 Samuel 8'],
['इस्राएलका राजाहरूमध्ये सबैभन्दा प्रिय दाऊद थिए। राजा हुनुअघि उनी त एउटा सानो गोठालो केटो मात्र थिए — तर परमेश्वरले उनलाई छान्नुभयो, किनभने उहाँले दाऊदभित्र आफ्नै हृदयअनुसारको मानिस देख्नुभयो।','Israelkaa raajaaharumadhye sabaibhandaa priya Daaud thie. Raajaa hunuaghi uni ta eutaa saano gothaalo keto maatra thie — tara Parameshwarle unlaai chhaannubhayo, kinabhane uhaanle Daaudbhitra aaphnai hridayaanusaarko maanis dekhnubhayo.','The best-loved of Israel’s kings was a man named David. Before he was king he was only a young shepherd boy — but God chose him, because he saw in David a man after his own heart.','1 Samuel 13:14 · 16:7'],
['गोल्यत नाम गरेको एउटा विशाल शत्रु-योद्धाले इस्राएललाई हाँक दियो — तर परमेश्वरले जवान दाऊदलाई त्यसलाई पराजित गर्ने सामर्थ्य दिनुभयो, र इस्राएलले आफ्ना शत्रुहरूमाथि विजय देख्यो।','Golyat naam gareko eutaa vishaal shatru-yoddhaale Israellaai haank diyo — tara Parameshwarle jawaan Daaudlaai tyaslaai paraajit garne saamarthya dinubhayo, ra Israelle aaphnaa shatruharumaathi vijaya dekhyo.','A giant enemy warrior named Goliath defied Israel — but God empowered young David to defeat him, and Israel saw victory over their enemies.','1 Samuel 17'],
['परमेश्वरले दाऊदलाई राजा बनाउनुभयो र प्रतिज्ञा दिनुभयो — तिम्रो वंशबाट एउटा अनन्त राजा आउनुहुनेछ।','Parameshwarle Daaudlaai raajaa banaunubhayo ra pratigyaa dinubhayo — timro wanshabaata eutaa ananta raajaa aaunuhunechha.','God made David king and promised: from your line will come a King whose kingdom never ends.','2 Samuel 7'],
['दाऊदपछि सयौं वर्षसम्म इस्राएलमा धेरै राजाहरूले राज्य गरे। कोही असल थिए — तर धेरैजसो गहिरो पापमा जिए। तिनीहरूले झूटा देवताहरू पुजे, गरिबहरूलाई थिचे, र मानिसहरूलाई पनि परमेश्वरबाट टाढा डोर्याए।','Daaudpachhi sayaun barshasamma Israelmaa dherai raajaaharule raajya gare. Kohi asal thie — tara dheraijaso gahiro paapmaa jie. Tiniharule jhutaa dewataaharu puje, garibharulaai thiche, ra maanisharulaai pani Parameshwarbaata taadhaa doryaae.','After David, many kings ruled Israel over hundreds of years. A few were good — but most lived in deep sin. They worshiped false gods, crushed the poor, and led the people far from God.','1–2 Kings'],
['यो एउटा दुःखलाग्दो चक्र थियो। मानिसहरू केही समय परमेश्वरसँग हिँड्थे; अनि बिस्तारै सम्झौता गर्दै झूटा देवताहरूतिर फर्कन्थे; त्यसले तिनीहरूलाई शत्रुको थिचोमिचोमा पुर्याउँथ्यो; दुःखमा तिनीहरू परमेश्वरलाई पुकार्थे — र उहाँले बचाउनुहुन्थ्यो। तर केही समयपछि फेरि त्यही चक्र दोहोरिन्थ्यो।','Yo eutaa dukhalaagdo chakra thiyo. Maanisharu kehi samaya Parameshwarsanga hindthe; ani bistaarai samjhautaa gardai jhutaa dewataaharutira pharkanthe; tyasle tiniharulaai shatruko thichomichomaa puryaunthyo; dukhamaa tiniharu Parameshwarlaai pukaarthe — ra uhaanle bachaunuhunthyo. Tara kehi samayapachhi pheri tyahi chakra dohorinthyo.','It was a heartbreaking cycle. For a while the people would walk with God; then slowly they would compromise and turn to false gods; that led them into oppression under their enemies; in their misery they would cry out to God — and he would save them. And then, after a while, the same circle would begin again.','Judges 2:11–19'],
['ती राजाहरूकै समयमा परमेश्वरले अगमवक्ताहरू पठाउनुहुन्थ्यो — उहाँले छान्नुभएका मानिसहरू, जसले राजा र जनतासामु परमेश्वरको वचन बोल्थे। तिनीहरूले चेतावनी दिन्थे — पाप छोड, परमेश्वरतिर फर्क — र आशाको सन्देश पनि सुनाउँथे।','Ti raajaaharukai samayamaa Parameshwarle agamwaktaaharu pathaunuhunthyo — uhaanle chhaannubhaekaa maanisharu, jasle raajaa ra janataasaamu Parameshwarko wachan bolthe. Tiniharule chetaawani dinthe — paap chhoda, Parameshwartira pharka — ra aashaako sandesh pani sunaunthe.','And all through the years of those kings, God kept sending prophets — people God chose to speak his words to the kings and to the people. They brought warning — turn from sin, come back to God — and they brought hope.','2 Kings 17:13'],
['अगमवक्ताहरूले आशाको कुरा पनि गरे। तिनीहरूले भने — एक दिन परमेश्वरले आफ्ना मानिसहरूसँग नयाँ करार बाँध्नुहुनेछ, र तिनीहरूको पाप पूर्ण रूपमा क्षमा हुनेछ। अनि तिनीहरूले आउनुहुने परमेश्वरका एक सेवकको बारेमा पनि बताए — जसले मानिसहरूको पाप आफैँमाथि लिएर तिनीहरूको सट्टामा बोक्नुहुनेछ।','Agamwaktaaharule aashaako kuraa pani gare. Tiniharule bhane — ek din Parameshwarle aaphnaa maanisharusanga nayaan karaar baandhnuhunechha, ra tiniharuko paap purna rupmaa kshamaa hunechha. Ani tiniharule aaunuhune Parameshwarkaa ek sewakko baaremaa pani bataae — jasle maanisharuko paap aaphainmaathi liera tiniharuko sattaamaa boknuhunechha.','The prophets also spoke of hope. One day, they said, God would make a new covenant with his people, and their sin would be fully forgiven. And they told of a coming Servant of God who would take the people’s sin upon himself and carry it in their place.','Jeremiah 31 · Isaiah 53'],
['परमेश्वरले अगमवक्ताद्वारा भन्नुभयो — म तिमीहरूलाई नयाँ हृदय दिनेछु, र आफ्नो आत्मा तिमीहरूभित्र राख्नेछु।','Parameshwarle agamwaktaadwaaraa bhannubhayo — ma timiharulaai nayaan hridaya dinechhu, ra aaphno aatmaa timiharubhitra raakhnechhu.','Through the prophets God promised: I will give you a new heart, and I will put my own Spirit within you.','Ezekiel 36:26–27'],
['तर धेरैजसो राजा र जनताले सुनेनन्। अन्त्यमा त्यही पापको फल आयो — शत्रुको सेनाले देश जित्यो, र इस्राएलका मानिसहरूले आफ्नै देश छोड्नुपर्यो। यही नै परमेश्वरको अनुशासन थियो — जसको बारेमा अगमवक्ताहरूले वर्षौंदेखि चेतावनी दिएका थिए।','Tara dheraijaso raajaa ra janataale sunenan. Antyamaa tyahi paapko phal aayo — shatruko senaale desh jityo, ra Israelkaa maanisharule aaphnai desh chhodnuparyo. Yahi nai Parameshwarko anushaasan thiyo — jasko baaremaa agamwaktaaharule barshaundekhi chetaawani diekaa thie.','But most of the kings and the people would not listen. In the end sin bore its fruit: an enemy army conquered the land, and the people of Israel were forced to leave their own country. This was God’s discipline — the discipline the prophets had warned about for years.','2 Kings 17 · 25']]},
{id:'wait',t:'The long wait',ne:'लामो प्रतीक्षा',art:FNE_ART.wait,
note:['हाम्रो कमजोरी र अविश्वासयोग्यताले परमेश्वरको विश्वासयोग्यतालाई रद्द गर्दैन। चुपचाप बितेका चार सय वर्षभरि पनि उहाँ विश्वासयोग्य रहनुभयो — इतिहासकै सबैभन्दा ठूलो आगमनको तयारी गर्दै।','Haamro kamjori ra avishwaasyogyataale Parameshwarko vishwaasyogyataalaai radda gardaina. Chupchaap bitekaa chaar saya barshabhari pani uhaan vishwaasyogya rahanubhayo — itihaaskai sabaibhandaa thulo aagamanko tayaari gardai.','Our weakness and unfaithfulness do not cancel God’s faithfulness. Through four hundred quiet years he stayed faithful — preparing the greatest arrival in history.'],
paras:[
['यसरी अगमवक्ताहरूको चेतावनी पूरा भयो — इस्राएलका मानिसहरू आफ्नो देशबाट टाढा लगिए। तिनीहरूका घर र खेतबारी पछाडि छुटे। सबै आशा हराएजस्तो देखियो।','Yasari agamwaktaaharuko chetaawani puraa bhayo — Israelkaa maanisharu aaphno deshbaata taadhaa lagie. Tiniharukaa ghar ra khetbaari pachhaadi chhute. Sabai aashaa haraaejasto dekhiyo.','So the prophets’ warning came true: the people of Israel were carried far from their own land. Their homes and their fields were left behind. It looked as if all hope was lost.','2 Kings 25'],
['यसैलाई निर्वासन भनिन्छ — बेबिलोन देशको सेनाले यरूशलेम भत्कायो, परमेश्वरको मन्दिर जलायो, र मानिसहरूलाई कैद गरेर आफ्नो देशमा लगे।','Yasailaai nirwaasan bhaninchha — Bebilon deshko senaale Yarushalem bhatkaayo, Parameshwarko mandir jalaayo, ra maanisharulaai kaid garera aaphno deshmaa lage.','This is called the exile: the armies of Babylon tore down Jerusalem, burned God’s temple, and carried the people away captive to Babylon.','2 Kings 25:8–11'],
['निर्वासनमा हुँदा पनि परमेश्वरले तिनीहरूलाई त्याग्नुभएन — तिनीहरू योग्य भएकाले होइन, तर परमेश्वर अत्यन्तै कृपालु हुनुहुन्छ, र उहाँ सारा पृथ्वीमा मुक्ति ल्याउने आफ्नो योजनामा अटल हुनुहुन्थ्यो।','Nirwaasanmaa hundaa pani Parameshwarle tiniharulaai tyaagnubhaena — tiniharu yogya bhaekaale hoina, tara Parameshwar atyantai kripaalu hunuhunchha, ra uhaan saaraa prithvimaa mukti lyaaune aaphno yojanaamaa atal hunuhunthyo.','While they were in exile, God did not abandon them — not because they deserved it, but because God is radically merciful, and he was still committed to bringing salvation to the whole earth.','Jeremiah 29:10–14'],
['इतिहासले एउटा कुरा प्रस्टै देखाइसकेको थियो — हामी मानिसहरू आफ्नै बलले परमेश्वरसँग विश्वासयोग्य भएर हिँड्न सक्दा रहेनछौं; हाम्रो विद्रोह दोहोरिइरह्यो। हामीलाई अर्कै उत्तर चाहिन्थ्यो। परमेश्वरले अगमवक्ताद्वारा त्यही उत्तरको प्रतिज्ञा गर्नुभयो — म तिमीहरूको ढुङ्गाको हृदय निकालेर मासुको हृदय दिनेछु, र मेरो व्यवस्था तिमीहरूकै हृदयमा लेखिदिनेछु।','Itihaasle eutaa kuraa prastai dekhaaisakeko thiyo — haami maanisharu aaphnai balle Parameshwarsanga vishwaasyogya bhaera hindna sakdaa rahenachhaun; haamro vidroha dohoriirahyo. Haamilaai arkai uttar chaahinthyo. Parameshwarle agamwaktaadwaaraa tyahi uttarko pratigyaa garnubhayo — ma timiharuko dhungaako hridaya nikaalera maasuko hridaya dinechhu, ra mero vyawasthaa timiharukai hridayamaa lekhidinechhu.','History had made one thing plain: we humans could not stay faithful to God in our own strength — our rebellion kept repeating. We needed a different answer. And through the prophets God promised exactly that: I will take out your heart of stone and give you a heart of flesh, and I will write my law on your very hearts.','Ezekiel 36:26 · Jeremiah 31:33'],
['अगमवक्ता इजकिएलले एउटा दर्शन देखे — सुकेका हड्डीहरूले भरिएको एउटा बेँसी। परमेश्वरले सोध्नुभयो — के यी हड्डीहरू फेरि जीवित हुन सक्छन्? अनि उहाँको सासले ती हड्डीहरूमा जीवन भरिदियो, र त्यहाँ एउटा ठूलो जमात उभियो। चिन्ह प्रस्ट थियो — मरेतुल्य हृदयलाई पनि परमेश्वरले फेरि जीवित पार्न सक्नुहुन्छ।','Agamwaktaa Ijakielle eutaa darshan dekhe — sukekaa haddiharule bharieko eutaa bensi. Parameshwarle sodhnubhayo — ke yi haddiharu pheri jeewit huna sakchhan? Ani uhaanko saasle ti haddiharumaa jeewan bharidiyo, ra tyahaan eutaa thulo jamaat ubhiyo. Chinha prasta thiyo — maretulya hridayalaai pani Parameshwarle pheri jeewit paarna saknuhunchha.','The prophet Ezekiel saw a vision: a valley full of dry bones. God asked him — can these bones live again? Then God’s own breath filled those bones with life, and a great multitude stood up. The sign was clear: even a heart as good as dead, God can bring back to life.','Ezekiel 37:1–10'],
['निर्वासनमा लगिएकाहरूमध्ये दानिएल नाम गरेका एक जना युवा थिए। त्यो विदेशी देशमा, प्रार्थना गर्न निषेध हुँदा पनि, उनले दिनको तीन पटक झ्याल खोलेर प्रार्थना गरिरहे। सिंहहरूको खोरमा फालिँदा पनि परमेश्वरले उनलाई बचाउनुभयो।','Nirwaasanmaa lagiekaaharumadhye Daaniel naam garekaa ek janaa yuwaa thie. Tyo videshi deshmaa, praarthanaa garna nishedh hundaa pani, unle dinko teen patak jhyaal kholera praarthanaa garirahe. Sinhaharuko khormaa phaalindaa pani Parameshwarle unlaai bachaunubhayo.','Among those carried into exile was a young man named Daniel. In that foreign land, even when prayer was outlawed, he kept opening his window to pray three times a day. Even when he was thrown into a den of lions, God kept him safe.','Daniel 6'],
['सत्तरी वर्षपछि, प्रतिज्ञा अनुसार, परमेश्वरले तिनीहरूलाई आफ्नै देशमा फर्काउनुभयो। तिनीहरूले यरूशलेम शहर र मन्दिर फेरि बनाए। तर हृदयको गहिराइमा सबैले बुझेका थिए — सबैभन्दा ठूलो प्रतिज्ञा अझै पूरा भएको छैन।','Sattari barshapachhi, pratigyaa anusaar, Parameshwarle tiniharulaai aaphnai deshmaa pharkaunubhayo. Tiniharule Yarushalem shahar ra mandir pheri banaae. Tara hridayako gahiraaimaa sabaile bujhekaa thie — sabaibhandaa thulo pratigyaa ajhai puraa bhaeko chhaina.','Seventy years later, just as promised, God brought them back to their own land. They rebuilt the city of Jerusalem and the temple. But deep down everyone knew: the greatest promise had not yet been kept.','Ezra · Nehemiah'],
['तैपनि तिनीहरूले पर्खिरहे — प्रतिज्ञा गरिएको उद्धारक, मसीह, कहिले आउनुहुन्छ?','Taipani tiniharule parkhirahe — pratigyaa garieko uddhaarak, Maseeh, kahile aaunuhunchha?','Still they waited: when would the promised Rescuer — the Messiah — come?','Isaiah 9:6–7'],
['तर त्यो कसरी हुनेछ भन्ने कसैलाई थाहा थिएन। धेरै इस्राएलीहरूले एक जना लडाकु वीरको प्रतीक्षा गरे, जसले तिनीहरूलाई थिचोमिचो गर्नेहरूबाट छुटाउनेछ। तर साँचो उत्तर त्योभन्दा धेरै गहिरो थियो — पापबाटै छुटाउनुहुने उद्धारक। परमेश्वर आफैँ आफ्नो मन्दिरमा फर्कनुहुनेथियो — र मानिसको जीवन र स्वतन्त्रताको लागि आफ्नै ज्यान अर्पण गर्नुहुनेथियो।','Tara tyo kasari hunechha bhanne kasailaai thaahaa thiena. Dherai Israeliharule ek janaa ladaaku veerko pratikshaa gare, jasle tiniharulaai thichomicho garneharubaata chhutaaunechha. Tara saancho uttar tyobhandaa dherai gahiro thiyo — paapbaatai chhutaaunuhune uddhaarak. Parameshwar aaphain aaphno mandirmaa pharkanuhunethiyo — ra maanisko jeewan ra swatantrataako laagi aaphnai jyaan arpan garnuhunethiyo.','But nobody knew how it would happen. Many in Israel waited for a warrior who would deliver them from their oppressors. The true answer ran far deeper — a deliverer who would free them from their sins. God himself would return to his temple — and lay down his own life for the life and freedom of human beings.','Malachi 3:1 · Mark 10:45'],
['चार सय वर्षसम्म सन्नाटा रह्यो। तर परमेश्वरले आफ्नो प्रतिज्ञा बिर्सनुभएको थिएन।','Chaar saya barshasamma sannaataa rahyo. Tara Parameshwarle aaphno pratigyaa birsanubhaeko thiena.','For four hundred years, silence. But God had not forgotten his promise.','Malachi → Matthew']]},
{id:'immanuel',t:'God with us',ne:'इम्मानुएल',art:FNE_ART.immanuel,
note:['सृष्टिकर्ता आफ्नै सृष्टिभित्र पस्नुभयो। येशूमा परमेश्वरले टाढाबाट सहायता पठाउनुभएन — उहाँ आफैँ आउनुभयो।','Srishtikartaa aaphnai srishtibhitra pasnubhayo. Yeshumaa Parameshwarle taadhaabaata sahaayataa pathaunubhaena — uhaan aaphain aaunubhayo.','The Creator stepped inside his own creation. In Jesus, God did not send help from a distance — he came himself.'],
paras:[
['अनि — त्यो लामो, चुपचाप प्रतीक्षापछि — येशू जन्मनुभयो। उहाँलाई अर्को नाम पनि दिइयो — इम्मानुएल, अर्थात् परमेश्वर हामीसँग।','Ani — tyo laamo, chupchaap pratikshaapachhi — Yeshu janmanubhayo. Uhaanlaai arko naam pani diiyo — Immaanuel, arthaat Parameshwar haamisanga.','And then — after that long, silent wait — Jesus was born. He was given another name too: Immanuel, which means God with us.','Matthew 1:23'],
['उहाँको जन्मअघि नै अगमवक्ताहरूले लेखेका थिए — हाम्रा निम्ति एउटा बालक जन्मनुहुनेछ, र उहाँलाई अचम्मको सल्लाहकार, शक्तिशाली परमेश्वर, अनन्तका पिता, शान्तिका राजकुमार भनिनेछ। उहाँ कन्याबाट जन्मनुहुनेछ भनेर पनि लेखिएको थियो — र ठीक त्यसै भयो।','Uhaanko janmaaghi nai agamwaktaaharule lekhekaa thie — haamraa nimti eutaa baalak janmanuhunechha, ra uhaanlaai achammako sallaahakaar, shaktishaali Parameshwar, anantakaa Pitaa, shaantikaa raajkumaar bhaninechha. Uhaan kanyaabaata janmanuhunechha bhanera pani lekhieko thiyo — ra theek tyasai bhayo.','Long before his birth the prophets had written: for us a child will be born, and he will be called Wonderful Counselor, Mighty God, Everlasting Father, Prince of Peace. It was also written that he would be born of a virgin — and that is exactly what happened.','Isaiah 9:6 · 7:14'],
['परमेश्वर आफैँ मानिस बन्नुभयो र हाम्रै बीचमा बस्नुभयो।','Parameshwar aaphain maanis bannubhayo ra haamrai beechmaa basnubhayo.','God himself became human and made his home among us.','John 1:14'],
['येशूले परमेश्वर को हुनुहुन्छ र कस्तो हुनुहुन्छ भनेर पूर्ण रूपमा प्रकट गर्नुभयो। उहाँलाई धेरै नामले चिनिन्छ — परमेश्वरको वचन, देह बन्नुभएको परमेश्वर, परमेश्वरका पुत्र। अनि उहाँ आफैँले भने आफूलाई प्रायः मानिसका पुत्र भन्नुहुन्थ्यो — दानिएल अगमवक्ताको दर्शनबाट आएको नाम, जहाँ सबै जाति र भाषाका मानिसहरूले उहाँको सेवा गर्छन्।','Yeshule Parameshwar ko hunuhunchha ra kasto hunuhunchha bhanera purna rupmaa prakat garnubhayo. Uhaanlaai dherai naamle chininchha — Parameshwarko wachan, deha bannubhaeko Parameshwar, Parameshwarkaa putra. Ani uhaan aaphaile bhane aaphulaai praayah maanisakaa putra bhannuhunthyo — Daaniel agamwaktaako darshanbaata aaeko naam, jahaan sabai jaati ra bhaashaakaa maanisharule uhaanko sewaa garchhan.','Jesus revealed perfectly who God is and what God is like. He is known by many names — the Word of God, God become flesh, the Son of God. And he himself most often used the name Son of Man — a name from the prophet Daniel’s vision, where people of every nation and language serve him.','John 1:1,14 · Daniel 7:13–14'],
['येशू दरबारमा होइन, नासरत भन्ने सानो गाउँमा हुर्कनुभयो। उहाँले काम गर्नुभयो, थकाइ जान्नुभयो, आँसु चिन्नुभयो — हाम्रो जीवन उहाँले भित्रैबाट बुझ्नुहुन्छ।','Yeshu darbaarmaa hoina, Naasarat bhanne saano gaaunmaa hurkanubhayo. Uhaanle kaam garnubhayo, thakaai jaannubhayo, aansu chinnubhayo — haamro jeewan uhaanle bhitraibaata bujhnuhunchha.','Jesus grew up not in a palace but in a small village called Nazareth. He worked, knew tiredness, knew tears — he understands our life from the inside.','Luke 2:39–52 · Hebrews 4:15'],
['येशूले परमेश्वरको राज्यको सुसमाचार सुनाउनुभयो र हराएकाहरूलाई खोज्नुभयो।','Yeshule Parameshwarko raajyako susamaachaar sunaunubhayo ra haraaekaaharulaai khojnubhayo.','Jesus announced the good news of God’s kingdom and went looking for the lost.','Luke 4 · Luke 19:10'],
['यूहन्ना नाम गरेका एक जना अगमवक्ता थिए, जसलाई परमेश्वरले मानिसहरूलाई तयार पार्न पठाउनुभएको थियो। येशूलाई देखेर तिनले कराएर भने — हेर, परमेश्वरको थुमा, जसले संसारको पाप उठाइलानुहुन्छ!','Yuhannaa naam garekaa ek janaa agamwaktaa thie, jaslaai Parameshwarle maanisharulaai tayaar paarna pathaunubhaeko thiyo. Yeshulaai dekhera tinle karaaera bhane — hera, Parameshwarko thumaa, jasle sansaarko paap uthaailaanuhunchha!','There was a prophet named John, sent by God to make the people ready. When John saw Jesus, he cried out: look — the Lamb of God, who takes away the sin of the world!','John 1:29']]},
{id:'crossgs',t:'The cross and the empty tomb',ne:'क्रूस र रित्तो चिहान',art:FNE_ART.cross,
note:['येशूको मृत्यु र पुनरुत्थानले हामी निको भएर परमेश्वरसँगको सङ्गतिमा फर्किन सक्ने बाटो खोलिदियो।','Yeshuko mrityu ra punarutthaanle haami niko bhaera Parameshwarsangako sangatimaa pharkina sakne baato kholidiyo.','Jesus’ death and resurrection made it possible for us to be healed and restored back into fellowship with God.'],
paras:[
['क्रूसको अघिल्लो रात येशूले बगैंचामा प्रार्थना गर्नुभयो। आउन लागेको दुःख उहाँलाई थाहा थियो, र उहाँले बिन्ती गर्नुभयो — पिता, अर्को कुनै बाटो छ भने यो कचौरा मबाट हटाइदिनुहोस् — तैपनि मेरो होइन, तपाईंकै इच्छा पूरा होस्। उहाँको ज्यान कसैले खोसेको होइन — उहाँले प्रेमको कारण आफ्नै खुशीले त्यो बाटो रोज्नुभयो।','Kroosko aghillo raat Yeshule bagainchaamaa praarthanaa garnubhayo. Aauna laageko dukha uhaanlaai thaahaa thiyo, ra uhaanle binti garnubhayo — Pitaa, arko kunai baato chha bhane yo kachauraa mabaata hataaidinuhos — taipani mero hoina, tapaainkai ichchhaa puraa hos. Uhaanko jyaan kasaile khoseko hoina — uhaanle premko kaaran aaphnai khushile tyo baato rojnubhayo.','The night before the cross, Jesus prayed in a garden. He knew the suffering that was coming, and he asked: Father, if there is another way, take this cup from me — yet not my will, but yours be done. No one took his life from him; he chose that road willingly, out of love.','Luke 22:39–44 · John 10:18'],
['भोलिपल्ट उहाँलाई पक्रेर मृत्युदण्ड दिइयो — क्रूसमा टाँगेर, त्यस समयको सबैभन्दा क्रूर सजाय। तर यो सबै परमेश्वरको योजनाभित्रै थियो।','Bholipalta uhaanlaai pakrera mrityudanda diiyo — kroosmaa taangera, tyas samayako sabaibhandaa kroor sajaaya. Tara yo sabai Parameshwarko yojanaabhitrai thiyo.','The next day he was arrested and executed — nailed to a cross, the cruelest punishment of that age. Yet all of it lay inside God’s plan.','Luke 23 · Acts 2:23'],
['क्रूसमा येशूले हाम्रो पाप आफैँमाथि लिनुभयो।','Kroosmaa Yeshule haamro paap aaphainmaathi linubhayo.','On the cross Jesus took our sin upon himself.','Isaiah 53'],
['येशू मर्नुहुँदा मन्दिरको पर्दा माथिदेखि तलसम्म च्यातियो। त्यो पर्दाले मानिसहरूलाई परमेश्वरको उपस्थितिबाट अलग गर्थ्यो — त्यसभित्र जान त वर्षको एक पटक, केवल प्रधान पूजाहारी मात्र सक्थे। अब परमेश्वरकहाँ जाने ढोका सबैका लागि खुला छ।','Yeshu marnuhundaa mandirko pardaa maathidekhi talasamma chyaatiyo. Tyo pardaale maanisharulaai Parameshwarko upasthitibaata alag garthyo — tyasbhitra jaana ta barshako ek patak, kewal pradhaan pujaahaari maatra sakthe. Aba Parameshwarkahaan jaane dhokaa sabaikaa laagi khulaa chha.','When Jesus died, the temple curtain tore from top to bottom. That curtain had separated the people from God’s presence — only the highest priest could go behind it, and only once a year. Now the way into God’s presence stands open to everyone.','Matthew 27:51 · Hebrews 9:7'],
['तेस्रो दिन येशू मृत्युबाट जीवित हुनुभयो। मृत्यु पराजित भयो।','Tesro din Yeshu mrityubaata jeewit hunubhayo. Mrityu paraajit bhayo.','On the third day Jesus rose from the dead. Death itself was defeated.','Luke 24'],
['मानिसलाई आफ्नो पकडमा राख्ने अन्धकारका शक्तिहरूलाई पनि उहाँले त्यहीँ पराजित गर्नुभयो। हामीले न त तिनीहरूले नै बुझेका थिए — क्रूस त सुरुदेखिकै योजना थियो। त्यसले हामी फेरि स्वतन्त्रतामा र परमेश्वरसँगको सम्बन्धमा हिँड्न सक्ने बाटो खोलिदियो।','Maanislaai aaphno pakadmaa raakhne andhakaarkaa shaktiharulaai pani uhaanle tyahin paraajit garnubhayo. Haamile na ta tiniharule nai bujhekaa thie — kroos ta surudekhikai yojanaa thiyo. Tyasle haami pheri swatantrataamaa ra Parameshwarsangako sambandhamaa hindna sakne baato kholidiyo.','There he also defeated the dark powers that held humanity in their grip. Neither we nor they had understood: the cross was the plan from the very beginning. It opened the way for us to walk in freedom and relationship with God once again.','Colossians 2:15 · 1 Corinthians 2:8'],
['अब परमेश्वरकहाँ फर्कने बाटो खुल्यो। भाँचिएको सङ्गति फेरि जोडियो।','Aba Parameshwarkahaan pharkane baato khulyo. Bhaanchieko sangati pheri jodiyo.','Now the way back to God stands open. The broken fellowship is joined again.','Romans 5:1–11'],
['उहाँमा कुनै पाप थिएन — तर हाम्रो पाप उहाँले बोक्नुभयो, ताकि हामी परमेश्वरको अगाडि धर्मी ठहरिन सकौं। यो नै ठूलो साटासाट हो।','Uhaanmaa kunai paap thiena — tara haamro paap uhaanle boknubhayo, taaki haami Parameshwarko agaadi dharmi thaharina sakaun. Yo nai thulo saataasaat ho.','He had no sin of his own — yet he carried ours, so that we could stand righteous before God. This is the great exchange.','2 Corinthians 5:21']]},
{id:'newcreation',t:'New creation',ne:'नयाँ सृष्टि',art:FNE_ART.newcreation,
paras:[
['जीवित हुनुभएपछि येशूले आफ्ना चेलाहरूलाई — अर्थात् उहाँलाई पछ्याउने साथीहरूलाई — पवित्र आत्मा दिनुभयो र संसारभरि पठाउनुभयो।','Jeewit hunubhaepachhi Yeshule aaphnaa chelaaharulaai — arthaat uhaanlaai pachhyaaune saathiharulaai — Pawitra Aatmaa dinubhayo ra sansaarbhari pathaunubhayo.','After he rose, Jesus gave his disciples — the friends who followed him — the Holy Spirit, and sent them out into all the world.','Acts 1–2'],
['पवित्र आत्मा भनेको परमेश्वर आफैँ हुनुहुन्छ — अब उहाँ आफ्ना मानिसहरूभित्र बास गर्नुहुन्छ, सान्त्वना दिनुहुन्छ, र बाटो देखाउनुहुन्छ।','Pawitra Aatmaa bhaneko Parameshwar aaphain hunuhunchha — aba uhaan aaphnaa maanisharubhitra baas garnuhunchha, saantwanaa dinuhunchha, ra baato dekhaunuhunchha.','The Holy Spirit is God himself — now making his home inside his people, comforting them and guiding the way.','John 14:16–17'],
['पहिले मानिसहरू परमेश्वरलाई भेट्न मन्दिर जान्थे। अब अचम्मको कुरा भएको छ — परमेश्वरको आत्मा पाएका उहाँका मानिसहरू नै उहाँको मन्दिर भएका छन्। हामी सँगै भेला भएर उहाँलाई आराधना गर्दा र एकअर्कालाई प्रेम गर्दा, परमेश्वर हामीभित्र र हाम्रै बीचमा बास गर्नुहुन्छ।','Pahile maanisharu Parameshwarlaai bhetna mandir jaanthe. Aba achammako kuraa bhaeko chha — Parameshwarko aatmaa paaekaa uhaankaa maanisharu nai uhaanko mandir bhaekaa chhan. Haami sangai bhelaa bhaera uhaanlaai aaraadhanaa gardaa ra ekarkaalaai prem gardaa, Parameshwar haamibhitra ra haamrai beechmaa baas garnuhunchha.','Before, people went to a temple to meet God. Now something astonishing has happened: God’s own people, filled with his Spirit, ARE his temple. As we gather to worship him and love one another, God dwells within us and among us.','1 Corinthians 3:16'],
['पहिलो विश्वासीहरू सँगै बस्थे — सँगै खान्थे, प्रार्थना गर्थे, र एकअर्कालाई सहायता गर्थे। तिनीहरूले एकअर्कालाई गर्ने प्रेमले हेरिरहेको संसारलाई देखायो — यहाँ केही नयाँ भइरहेको छ।','Pahilo vishwaasiharu sangai basthe — sangai khaanthe, praarthanaa garthe, ra ekarkaalaai sahaayataa garthe. Tiniharule ekarkaalaai garne premle heriraheko sansaarlaai dekhaayo — yahaan kehi nayaan bhairaheko chha.','The first believers lived life together — eating, praying, helping one another. The love they had for one another showed the watching world that something different was happening.','Acts 2:42–47'],
['यो निम्तो इस्राएलमा मात्र रोकिएन — अब सबै जातिहरू परमेश्वरका मानिस बन्न बोलाइएका छन्। एशियाली, अफ्रिकी, पश्चिमी — हरेक जाति र भाषाका मानिसहरू एउटै परिवारमा, भक्ति, प्रेम र आज्ञापालनको जीवनमा येशूलाई सँगसँगै पछ्याउँछन्। येशूको जीवन, मृत्यु र पुनरुत्थानले संसार बदल्यो — एक-एक व्यक्ति गर्दै, हरेकलाई विश्वासयोग्य, दयालु र उदार सृष्टिकर्तासँगको सम्बन्धमा फर्काउँदै।','Yo nimto Israelmaa maatra rokiena — aba sabai jaatiharu Parameshwarkaa maanis banna bolaaiekaa chhan. Eshiyaali, Aphriki, pashchimi — harek jaati ra bhaashaakaa maanisharu eutai pariwaarmaa, bhakti, prem ra aagyaapaalanko jeewanmaa Yeshulaai sangasangai pachhyaunchhan. Yeshuko jeewan, mrityu ra punarutthaanle sansaar badalyo — ek-ek vyakti gardai, hareklaai vishwaasyogya, dayaalu ra udaar srishtikartaasangako sambandhamaa pharkaaundai.','And the invitation did not stop at Israel — now all nations are called to become the people of God. Asian, African, Western — people of every nation and language in one family, following Jesus together in a life of devotion, love and obedience. The life, death and resurrection of Jesus changed the world — one person at a time, each one brought back into relationship with a faithful, kind and generous Creator.','Galatians 3:28 · Revelation 7:9'],
['त्यो सुसमाचार संसारभरि फैलिएको छ। आज नेपालमा धेरै मानिसहरू येशूलाई पछ्याउँछन् — तर धेरैले अझै पछ्याएका छैनन्। त्यसैले परमेश्वरले आफ्नो सुसमाचार सुनाउन नेपालमा मानिसहरू पठाइरहनुभएको छ। कथा अझै लेखिँदैछ।','Tyo susamaachaar sansaarbhari phailieko chha. Aaja Nepaalmaa dherai maanisharu Yeshulaai pachhyaunchhan — tara dheraile ajhai pachhyaaekaa chhainan. Tyasaile Parameshwarle aaphno susamaachaar sunaauna Nepaalmaa maanisharu pathaairahanubhaeko chha. Kathaa ajhai lekhindaichha.','That good news has spread across the world. In Nepal many people follow Jesus today — yet many still do not. So God keeps sending people to Nepal to proclaim his good news. The story is still being written.','Acts 1:8'],
['एक दिन येशू फेरि आउनुहुनेछ। परमेश्वरले नयाँ आकाश र नयाँ पृथ्वी बनाउनुहुनेछ।','Ek din Yeshu pheri aaunuhunechha. Parameshwarle nayaan aakaash ra nayaan prithvi banaunuhunechha.','One day Jesus will come again, and God will make a new heaven and a new earth.','Revelation 21:1'],
['त्यहाँ परमेश्वर आफ्ना मानिसहरूसँग बास गर्नुहुनेछ। न आँसु, न मृत्यु — सङ्गति सधैँको लागि।','Tyahaan Parameshwar aaphnaa maanisharusanga baas garnuhunechha. Na aansu, na mrityu — sangati sadhainko laagi.','There God will dwell with his people. No more tears, no more death — fellowship forever.','Revelation 21:3–4'],
['यो कथा तपाईंको पनि हुन सक्छ। येशूमा विश्वास गर्नुहोस्, र घर फर्कनुहोस्।','Yo kathaa tapaainko pani huna sakchha. Yeshumaa vishwaas garnuhos, ra ghar pharkanuhos.','This story can be yours too. Believe in Jesus, and come home.','John 3:16']]}
]},

{id:'fjesus',kind:'arc',title:'Jesus',ne:'येशू',
overview:{t:'Who is Jesus?',ne:'येशू को हुनुहुन्छ?',art:FNE_ART.ovjesus,
start:['सुरुदेखि हेरौं','From here — his story in detail'],
paras:[
['येशू परमेश्वरका पुत्र हुनुहुन्छ — परमेश्वर आफैँ, हामीजस्तै मानिस बन्नुभयो।','Yeshu Parameshwarkaa putra hunuhunchha — Parameshwar aaphain, haamijastai maanis bannubhayo.','Jesus is the Son of God — God himself, become human like us.','John 1:1,14'],
['उहाँ हामीजस्तै जिउनुभयो — तर पापविना — र आफ्नो जीवनले परमेश्वरको प्रेम देखाउनुभयो।','Uhaan haamijastai jiunubhayo — tara paapwinaa — ra aaphno jeewanle Parameshwarko prem dekhaunubhayo.','He lived as we live — yet without sin — and his whole life showed us the love of God.','Hebrews 4:15'],
['उहाँले आफ्नो ज्यान हाम्रा लागि दिनुभयो र मृत्युलाई जित्नुभयो।','Uhaanle aaphno jyaan haamraa laagi dinubhayo ra mrityulaai jitnubhayo.','He laid down his life for us — and he defeated death.','John 10:11 · Luke 24'],
['आज पनि उहाँ जीवित हुनुहुन्छ र हरेकलाई बोलाउनुहुन्छ — मकहाँ आओ।','Aaja pani uhaan jeewit hunuhunchha ra hareklaai bolaunuhunchha — makahaan aao.','He is alive today, and he calls every person: come to me.','Matthew 11:28'],
['उहाँको बारेमा जान्नु मात्र होइन — उहाँलाई चिन्नु। तलका कथाहरू त्यही निम्तो हुन्।','Uhaanko baaremaa jaannu maatra hoina — uhaanlaai chinnu. Talakaa kathaaharu tyahi nimto hun.','The goal is not just to know about him — it is to know him. The stories below are that invitation.','John 17:3'],
['अब यहाँबाट हामी उहाँको कथा सुरुदेखि हेर्नेछौं — जन्मदेखि रित्तो चिहानसम्म, एक-एक घटना गरेर।','Aba yahaanbaata haami uhaanko kathaa surudekhi hernechhaun — janmadekhi ritto chihaansamma, ek-ek ghatanaa garera.','From here, we will walk through his story from the beginning — from his birth to the empty tomb, one moment at a time.']]},
sections:[
{id:'jbirth',t:'The birth',ne:'जन्म',art:FNE_ART.jbirth,
note:['सबै थोकका राजा दरबारविना, तुरहीविना आउनुभयो। पहिलो साक्षीको रूपमा परमेश्वरले गोठालाहरूलाई रोज्नुभयो — यो राज्य पहिलो रातदेखि नै यसरी चल्छ।','Sabai thokkaa raajaa darbaarwinaa, turahiwinaa aaunubhayo. Pahilo saakshiko rupmaa Parameshwarle gothaalaaharulaai rojnubhayo — yo raajya pahilo raatdekhi nai yasari chalchha.','The King of everything arrived with no palace and no trumpet — and God chose shepherds as the first witnesses. That is how this kingdom works from its very first night.'],
paras:[
['येशू जन्मनुभन्दा सयौं वर्षअघि नै इस्राएलका अगमवक्ताहरूले एक जना आउनुहुनेको बारेमा बताएका थिए — तिनीहरूले उहाँलाई आउनुहुने मसीह भनेर चिने। तिनीहरूले उहाँलाई धेरै नाम दिए — अचम्मको सल्लाहकार, शक्तिशाली परमेश्वर, अनन्तका पिता, शान्तिका राजकुमार — र उहाँ कन्याबाट जन्मनुहुनेछ भनेर लेखे। त्यही भविष्यवाणी अब पूरा हुन लागेको थियो।','Yeshu janmanubhandaa sayaun barshaaghi nai Israelkaa agamwaktaaharule ek janaa aaunuhuneko baaremaa bataaekaa thie — tiniharule uhaanlaai aaunuhune Maseeh bhanera chine. Tiniharule uhaanlaai dherai naam die — achammako sallaahakaar, shaktishaali Parameshwar, anantakaa Pitaa, shaantikaa raajkumaar — ra uhaan kanyaabaata janmanuhunechha bhanera lekhe. Tyahi bhavishyavaani aba puraa huna laageko thiyo.','Hundreds of years before Jesus was born, the prophets of Israel told of someone who would come — they knew him as the coming Messiah. They gave him many names — Wonderful Counselor, Mighty God, Everlasting Father, Prince of Peace — and they wrote that he would be born of a virgin. Now that prophecy was about to come true.','Isaiah 9:6 · 7:14'],
['गब्रिएल स्वर्गदूतले मरियमलाई भने — तिमीले एउटा छोरो जन्माउनेछ्यौ, र उहाँको नाम येशू राख्नू।','Gabriel swargadootle Mariyamlaai bhane — timile eutaa chhoro janmaunechhyau, ra uhaanko naam Yeshu raakhnu.','The angel Gabriel told Mary: you will have a son, and you are to name him Jesus.','Luke 1:26–33'],
['मरियम कुनै रानी थिइनन् — नासरत गाउँकी एउटी साधारण युवती। परमेश्वरले ठूला कामका लागि साधारण मानिसहरूलाई नै रोज्नुहुन्छ।','Mariyam kunai raani thiinan — Naasarat gaaunki eutii saadhaaran yuwati. Parameshwarle thulaa kaamkaa laagi saadhaaran maanisharulaai nai rojnuhunchha.','Mary was no queen — just an ordinary young woman from the village of Nazareth. God loves to choose ordinary people for his greatest work.','Luke 1:26–38'],
['येशू बेथलेहेममा जन्मनुभयो — सानो गाउँ, सानो डुँड। गोठालाहरू पहिलो पाहुना भए।','Yeshu Bethlehemmaa janmanubhayo — saano gaaun, saano dund. Gothaalaaharu pahilo paahunaa bhae.','Jesus was born in Bethlehem — a small town, a humble manger. Shepherds were the first visitors.','Luke 2'],
['टाढा पूर्वबाट ज्योतिषीहरू तारा पछ्याउँदै आए। तिनीहरूले बालकलाई दण्डवत् गरे र बहुमूल्य उपहारहरू चढाए।','Taadhaa purbabaata jyotishiharu taaraa pachhyaaundai aae. Tiniharule baalaklaai dandawat gare ra bahumulya upahaarharu chadhaae.','From the far east, wise men came following a star. They bowed before the child and offered him precious gifts.','Matthew 2:1–11'],
['येशू नामको अर्थ यही हो — उहाँले आफ्ना मानिसहरूलाई तिनीहरूका पापबाट बचाउनुहुनेछ।','Yeshu naamko artha yahi ho — uhaanle aaphnaa maanisharulaai tiniharukaa paapbaata bachaunuhunechha.','The name Jesus carries his mission: he will save his people from their sins.','Matthew 1:21'],
['त्यो रात आकाश स्वर्गदूतहरूले भरियो — सबैभन्दा उच्चमा परमेश्वरलाई महिमा, र पृथ्वीमा शान्ति!','Tyo raat aakaash swargadootharule bhariyo — sabaibhandaa uchchamaa Parameshwarlaai mahimaa, ra prithvimaa shaanti!','That night the sky filled with angels: glory to God in the highest — and on earth, peace!','Luke 2:13–14']]},
{id:'jbaptism',t:'Baptism and the wilderness',ne:'बप्तिस्मा र उजाडस्थान',art:FNE_ART.jbaptism,
note:['येशू हामी उभिने ठाउँमा उभिनुभयो — पापीहरूसँगै पानीमा। अनि हामी लड्ने ठाउँमा दह्रो उभिनुभयो — आदम र इस्राएल असफल भएका हरेक ठाउँमा उहाँले जित्नुभयो।','Yeshu haami ubhine thaaunmaa ubhinubhayo — paapiharusangai paanimaa. Ani haami ladne thaaunmaa dahro ubhinubhayo — Aadam ra Israel asaphal bhaekaa harek thaaunmaa uhaanle jitnubhayo.','Jesus stands where we stand — in the water alongside sinners — and stands firm where we fall, winning in every place Adam and Israel failed.'],
paras:[
['यूहन्ना नदीको छेउमा बसेर मानिसहरूलाई बोलाउँथे — पाप छोडेर परमेश्वरतिर फर्क! नयाँ सुरुवातको चिन्हको रूपमा उनले फर्कनेहरूलाई पानीमा डुबाउँथे — त्यसैलाई बप्तिस्मा भनिन्छ।','Yuhannaa nadiko chheumaa basera maanisharulaai bolaunthe — paap chhodera Parameshwartira pharka! Nayaan suruwaatko chinhako rupmaa unle pharkaneharulaai paanimaa dubaunthe — tyasailaai baptismaa bhaninchha.','John lived by the river, calling people: turn from sin, back to God! As a sign of that new start he would dip the returning ones in the water — that is what baptism means.','Matthew 3:1–6'],
['यूहन्नाले येशूलाई नदीमा बप्तिस्मा दिए। आकाशबाट आवाज आयो — यिनी मेरा प्रिय पुत्र हुन्।','Yuhannaale Yeshulaai nadeemaa baptismaa die. Aakaashbaata aawaaj aayo — yini meraa priya putra hun.','John baptized Jesus in the river, and a voice came from heaven: this is my beloved Son.','Matthew 3:13–17'],
['उजाडस्थानमा शैतानले येशूलाई परीक्षा गर्यो। तर आदमजस्तो होइन — येशूले जित्नुभयो।','Ujaadsthaanmaa shaitaanle Yeshulaai parikshaa garyo. Tara Aadamjasto hoina — Yeshule jitnubhayo.','In the wilderness Satan tested Jesus. But where Adam fell, Jesus stood firm and won.','Matthew 4:1–11'],
['त्यसपछि येशूले साधारण मानिसहरूलाई बोलाउनुभयो — जालहरू छोडेर तिनीहरू उहाँको पछि लागे। बाह्र जना चेला बने।','Tyaspachhi Yeshule saadhaaran maanisharulaai bolaunubhayo — jaalharu chhodera tiniharu uhaanko pachhi laage. Baahra janaa chelaa bane.','Then Jesus called ordinary people — they left their fishing nets and followed him. Twelve became his disciples.','Mark 1:16–20'],
['चालीस दिनसम्म येशूले केही खानुभएन। हरेक परीक्षाको जवाफ उहाँले परमेश्वरको वचनले दिनुभयो — लेखिएको छ।','Chaalis dinsamma Yeshule kehi khaanubhaena. Harek parikshaako jawaaph uhaanle Parameshwarko wachanle dinubhayo — lekhieko chha.','For forty days Jesus ate nothing. And he answered every temptation with the word of God: it is written.','Matthew 4:2–10']]},
{id:'jkingdom',t:'The kingdom announced',ne:'राज्यको सुसमाचार',art:FNE_ART.jkingdom,
note:['परमेश्वरको राज्य नक्साको कुनै ठाउँ होइन — माटो फोरेर उम्रने बीउजस्तै संसारभित्र पस्ने उहाँको असल शासन हो। र त्यसको ढोका पहिले सबैभन्दा असम्भावित मानिसहरूका लागि खुल्छ।','Parameshwarko raajya naksaako kunai thaaun hoina — maato phorera umrane biujastai sansaarbhitra pasne uhaanko asal shaasan ho. Ra tyasko dhokaa pahile sabaibhandaa asambhaawit maanisharukaa laagi khulchha.','The kingdom of God is not a place on a map — it is God’s own good rule breaking in, quiet as a seed pushing up through soil. And its door opens first to the least likely people.'],
paras:[
['येशूले भन्नुभयो — परमेश्वरको राज्य नजिकै आएको छ। फर्केर आओ र सुसमाचारमा विश्वास गर।','Yeshule bhannubhayo — Parameshwarko raajya najikai aaeko chha. Pharkera aau ra susamaachaarmaa vishwaas gara.','Jesus announced: the kingdom of God has come near. Turn around, and believe the good news.','Mark 1:15'],
['उहाँले गरिबहरूलाई, बिरामीहरूलाई र पापीहरूलाई नजिक बोलाउनुभयो।','Uhaanle garibharulaai, biraamiharulaai ra paapiharulaai najik bolaunubhayo.','He called the poor, the sick and the sinners near — the very people others pushed away.','Luke 5:27–32'],
['डाँडामा बसेर उहाँले सिकाउनुभयो — धन्य हुन् आत्मामा गरिब हुनेहरू, किनभने स्वर्गको राज्य तिनीहरूकै हो। धन्य हुन् नम्रहरू। धन्य हुन् शान्ति गराउनेहरू। संसारले जसलाई तल देख्छ, परमेश्वरले तिनीहरूलाई धन्य भन्नुहुन्छ।','Daandaamaa basera uhaanle sikaunubhayo — dhanya hun aatmaamaa garib huneharu, kinabhane swargako raajya tiniharukai ho. Dhanya hun namraharu. Dhanya hun shaanti garaauneharu. Sansaarle jaslaai tala dekhchha, Parameshwarle tiniharulaai dhanya bhannuhunchha.','Sitting on a hillside he taught: blessed are the poor in spirit, for the kingdom of heaven is theirs. Blessed are the humble. Blessed are the peacemakers. The very people the world looks down on, God calls blessed.','Matthew 5:3–9'],
['मानिसहरूले साना बालबालिकालाई येशूकहाँ ल्याए। चेलाहरूले तिनीहरूलाई रोके — तर येशूले भन्नुभयो — बालबालिकालाई मकहाँ आउन देऊ, नरोक। परमेश्वरको राज्य यस्तैहरूको हो।','Maanisharule saanaa baalbaalikaalaai Yeshukahaan lyaae. Chelaaharule tiniharulaai roke — tara Yeshule bhannubhayo — baalbaalikaalaai makahaan aauna deu, naroka. Parameshwarko raajya yastaiharuko ho.','People brought little children to Jesus. His disciples turned them away — but Jesus said: let the children come to me, do not stop them. The kingdom of God belongs to such as these.','Mark 10:13–14'],
['राज्य खेतमा लुकेको धनजस्तै हो — भेट्टाउने मानिसले खुशीले आफ्नो सबै थोक बेचेर त्यो खेत किन्छ।','Raajya khetmaa lukeko dhanjastai ho — bhettaaune maanisle khushile aaphno sabai thok bechera tyo khet kinchha.','The kingdom is like treasure hidden in a field: the one who finds it joyfully sells everything to buy that field.','Matthew 13:44'],
['येशूले भन्नुभयो — परमेश्वरको राज्य रायोको गेडाजस्तै हो। सबैभन्दा सानो बीउ, तर बढेर ठूलो रूख बन्छ, र चराहरूले त्यसका हाँगामा गुँड बनाउँछन्।','Yeshule bhannubhayo — Parameshwarko raajya raayoko gedaajastai ho. Sabaibhandaa saano biu, tara badhera thulo rukh banchha, ra charaaharule tyaskaa haangaamaa gund banaunchhan.','Jesus said: the kingdom of God is like a mustard seed — the smallest of seeds, yet it grows into a great tree, and the birds nest in its branches.','Mark 4:30–32']]},
{id:'jprayer',t:'Jesus teaches prayer',ne:'प्रार्थना',art:FNE_ART.jprayer,
note:['प्रार्थनाको पहिलो शब्दले नै सबै भन्छ — पिता। हामी राजाको दरबारमा होइन, बुबाको काखमा आउँछौं। त्यही ढोका येशूले खोलिदिनुभयो।','Praarthanaako pahilo shabdale nai sabai bhanchha — Pitaa. Haami raajaako darbaarmaa hoina, bubaako kaakhmaa aaunchhaun. Tyahi dhokaa Yeshule kholidinubhayo.','The first word of the prayer says it all — Father. We come not into a king’s court but onto a father’s lap. That is the door Jesus opened.'],
paras:[
['येशू बिहान सबेरै एक्लै प्रार्थना गर्न जानुहुन्थ्यो। चेलाहरूले भने — प्रभु, हामीलाई पनि प्रार्थना गर्न सिकाउनुहोस्।','Yeshu bihaana saberai eklai praarthanaa garna jaanuhunthyo. Chelaaharule bhane — Prabhu, haamilaai pani praarthanaa garna sikaunuhos.','Jesus would go out early in the morning to pray alone. His followers asked: Lord, teach us to pray too.','Mark 1:35 · Luke 11:1'],
['उहाँले सिकाउनुभयो — यसरी प्रार्थना गर: हे हाम्रा स्वर्गीय पिता, तपाईंको नाम पवित्र मानियोस्। तपाईंको राज्य आओस्।','Uhaanle sikaunubhayo — yasari praarthanaa gara: he haamraa swargiya Pitaa, tapaainko naam pawitra maaniyos. Tapaainko raajya aaos.','He taught them: pray like this — our Father in heaven, may your name be honored as holy, may your kingdom come.','Matthew 6:9–10'],
['हामीलाई आजको रोटी दिनुहोस्। हाम्रा पाप क्षमा गर्नुहोस्, जसरी हामीले पनि अरूलाई क्षमा गरेका छौं।','Haamilaai aajako roti dinuhos. Haamraa paap kshamaa garnuhos, jasari haamile pani arulaai kshamaa garekaa chhaun.','Give us today the food we need. Forgive our sins, as we also forgive those who wrong us.','Matthew 6:11–12'],
['हामीलाई परीक्षामा पर्न नदिनुहोस्, तर दुष्टबाट छुटाउनुहोस्। — यति सरल, यति गहिरो। यही प्रार्थना आज पनि संसारभरि येशूका चेलाहरूले गर्छन्।','Haamilaai parikshaamaa parna nadinuhos, tara dushtabaata chhutaaunuhos. — Yati saral, yati gahiro. Yahi praarthanaa aaja pani sansaarbhari Yeshukaa chelaaharule garchhan.','And lead us not into temptation, but deliver us from evil. So simple, so deep. Followers of Jesus around the world still pray this prayer today.','Matthew 6:13'],
['प्रार्थना भनेको लामो भाषण होइन — बुबासँग कुरा गर्नु हो। परमेश्वरले सुन्नुहुन्छ।','Praarthanaa bhaneko laamo bhaashan hoina — bubaasanga kuraa garnu ho. Parameshwarle sunnuhunchha.','Prayer is not a long speech — it is talking with your Father. And God listens.','Matthew 6:7–8'],
['येशूले भन्नुभयो — माग, र तिमीलाई दिइनेछ। खोज, र तिमीले भेट्टाउनेछौ। ढकढक्याऊ, र ढोका खोलिनेछ।','Yeshule bhannubhayo — maaga, ra timilaai diinechha. Khoja, ra timile bhettaaunechhau. Dhakdhakyaau, ra dhokaa kholinechha.','Jesus said: ask, and it will be given to you. Seek, and you will find. Knock, and the door will be opened.','Matthew 7:7']]},
{id:'jmiracles',t:'Power and compassion',ne:'शक्ति र दया',art:FNE_ART.jmiracles,
note:['चमत्कारहरू जादु होइनन् — झलकहरू हुन्। हरेक चङ्गाइ, शान्त भएको आँधी, बढेको रोटी — रोग, भोक र डर नभएको संसारको झ्याल हो।','Chamatkaarharu jaadu hoinan — jhalakharu hun. Harek changaai, shaanta bhaeko aandhi, badheko roti — rog, bhok ra dar nabhaeko sansaarko jhyaal ho.','The miracles are not magic — they are previews. Every healing, every calmed storm, every multiplied loaf is a window into the world as God intends it.'],
paras:[
['येशूले बिरामीलाई निको पार्नुभयो र अन्धालाई देख्ने बनाउनुभयो।','Yeshule biraamilaai niko paarnubhayo ra andhaalaai dekhne banaunubhayo.','Jesus healed the sick and gave the blind their sight.','Matthew 9'],
['एक जना कुष्ठरोगी येशूकहाँ आयो — जसलाई कसैले छुँदैनथ्यो। येशूले हात पसारेर उसलाई छुनुभयो र भन्नुभयो — निको होऊ।','Ek janaa kushtharogi Yeshukahaan aayo — jaslaai kasaile chhundainathyo. Yeshule haat pasaarera uslaai chhunubhayo ra bhannubhayo — niko hou.','A man with leprosy came to Jesus — a man nobody would touch. Jesus reached out his hand, touched him, and said: be healed.','Mark 1:40–42'],
['उहाँले आँधीलाई शान्त पार्नुभयो। चेलाहरूले सोधे — यिनी को हुन्?','Uhaanle aandhilaai shaanta paarnubhayo. Chelaaharule sodhe — yini ko hun?','He calmed a storm with a word. His disciples asked each other: who IS this?','Mark 4:35–41'],
['पाँचवटा रोटी र दुईवटा माछाले उहाँले हजारौंलाई खुवाउनुभयो।','Paanchwataa roti ra duiwataa maachhaale uhaanle hajaraunlaai khuwaunubhayo.','With five loaves and two fish he fed thousands.','John 6:1–14'],
['मरेकी एउटी सानी छोरीको हात समातेर उहाँले भन्नुभयो — छोरी, उठ। र त्यो केटी उठिन्। मृत्यु पनि उहाँको वचन मान्छ।','Marekii eutii saani chhoriko haat samaatera uhaanle bhannubhayo — chhori, utha. Ra tyo keti uthin. Mrityu pani uhaanko wachan maanchha.','Taking the hand of a little girl who had died, he said: child, get up. And she rose. Even death obeys his word.','Mark 5:41–42'],
['उहाँ साधारण मानिसहरूसँग हिँड्नुभयो — माछा मार्नेहरू, पापी भनिएकाहरू, भाँचिएका र बिरामीहरू — र उहाँले तिनीहरूलाई निको पार्नुभयो। भाँचिएका हामीप्रति परमेश्वरको कति गहिरो प्रेम र दया छ भनेर उहाँले नै देखाइदिनुभयो।','Uhaan saadhaaran maanisharusanga hindnubhayo — maachhaa maarneharu, paapi bhaniekaaharu, bhaanchiekaa ra biraamiharu — ra uhaanle tiniharulaai niko paarnubhayo. Bhaanchiekaa haamiprati Parameshwarko kati gahiro prem ra dayaa chha bhanera uhaanle nai dekhaaidinubhayo.','He walked with ordinary people — fishermen, so-called sinners, the broken and the sick — and he made them well. He showed us how deep the love and kindness of God is for us as broken people.','Matthew 9:35–36']]},
{id:'jlostson',t:'The lost son',ne:'हराएको छोरा',art:FNE_ART.jlostson,
note:['दौडिने बुबा नै यस कथाको केन्द्र हो — त्यो संस्कृतिमा इज्जतदार मानिस कहिल्यै दौडिँदैनथे। फर्कने छोरालाई अँगाल्न परमेश्वर आफ्नो इज्जत पनि हेर्नुहुन्न।','Daudine bubaa nai yas kathaako kendra ho — tyo sanskritimaa ijjatdaar maanis kahilyai daudindainathe. Pharkane chhoraalaai angaalna Parameshwar aaphno ijjat pani hernuhunna.','The father RUNNING is the center of this parable — in that culture a dignified man never ran. God sets aside his own dignity to embrace the child who comes home.'],
paras:[
['धार्मिक मानिसहरूले येशूको बारेमा गनगन गरे — यो मानिसले त पापीहरूलाई ग्रहण गर्छ, तिनीहरूसँगै खान्छ! जवाफमा येशूले यो कथा भन्नुभयो — एउटा छोराले बुबाको सम्पत्ति लिएर टाढा गयो र सबै उडायो।','Dhaarmik maanisharule Yeshuko baaremaa gangan gare — yo maanisle ta paapiharulaai grahan garchha, tiniharusangai khaanchha! Jawaaphmaa Yeshule yo kathaa bhannubhayo — eutaa chhoraale bubaako sampatti liera taadhaa gayo ra sabai udaayo.','The religious people grumbled about Jesus: this man welcomes sinners — he even eats with them! In answer, Jesus told this story. A son took his father’s wealth, went far away, and wasted it all.','Luke 15:1–2 · 11–16'],
['टाढा देशमा छोरो यति भोकायो कि सुँगुरको दाना पनि खान तयार भयो। अनि उसले सम्झ्यो — बुबाको घरमा त नोकरहरूले पनि पेटभरि खान्छन्। म फर्किन्छु।','Taadhaa deshmaa chhoro yati bhokaayo ki sungurko daanaa pani khaana tayaar bhayo. Ani usle samjhyo — bubaako gharmaa ta nokarharule pani petbhari khaanchhan. Ma pharkinchhu.','In the far country the son grew so hungry he was ready to eat the pigs’ food. Then he came to his senses: even my father’s servants eat their fill. I will go home.','Luke 15:14–19'],
['छोरो घर फर्कंदा बुबा दौडेर आए र अँगालो हाले।','Chhoro ghar pharkandaa bubaa daudera aae ra angaalo haale.','When the son came home, the father RAN to him and threw his arms around him.','Luke 15:20–24'],
['परमेश्वरको हृदय त्यस्तै छ — फर्कने हरेकलाई उहाँले खुशीसाथ ग्रहण गर्नुहुन्छ।','Parameshwarko hridaya tyastai chha — pharkane hareklaai uhaanle khushisaath grahan garnuhunchha.','That is the heart of God: he joyfully welcomes everyone who comes home.','Luke 15'],
['जेठो छोरो भने रिसायो — म त वर्षौंदेखि तपाईंको सेवा गर्दैछु! बुबाले भने — छोरा, मेरो जे छ, सबै तिम्रै हो। तर तिम्रो भाइ हराएको थियो, अहिले भेट्टाइयो — रमाउनु त पर्छ नि।','Jetho chhoro bhane risaayo — ma ta barshaundekhi tapaainko sewaa gardaichhu! Bubaale bhane — chhoraa, mero je chha, sabai timrai ho. Tara timro bhaai haraaeko thiyo, ahile bhettaaiyo — ramaaunu ta parchha ni.','But the elder son was angry: all these years I have served you! The father said: son, everything I have is yours. But your brother was lost and is found — how could we not celebrate?','Luke 15:25–32']]},
{id:'jsamaritan',t:'The good Samaritan',ne:'असल सामरी',art:FNE_ART.jsamaritan,
note:['येशूले प्रश्न नै उल्टाइदिनुभयो। मेरो प्रेम कसले पाउन योग्य छ होइन — म कसरी असल छिमेकी बन्न सक्छु? अनि उहाँले बाहिरको मानिसलाई नै कथाको नायक बनाउनुभयो।','Yeshule prashna nai ultaaidinubhayo. Mero prem kasle paauna yogya chha hoina — ma kasari asal chhimeki banna sakchhu? Ani uhaanle baahirako maanislaai nai kathaako naayak banaunubhayo.','Jesus flips the question. Not WHO deserves my love — but how can I BE a neighbor? And he makes the outsider the hero of the story.'],
paras:[
['कसैले सोध्यो — मेरो छिमेकी को हो? येशूले कथाले जवाफ दिनुभयो।','Kasaile sodhyo — mero chhimeki ko ho? Yeshule kathaale jawaaph dinubhayo.','Someone asked Jesus: who is my neighbor? He answered with a story.','Luke 10:25–29'],
['यरूशलेमबाट यरीहो जाने बाटो डरलाग्दो थियो — डाँकूहरूले एक जना यात्रुलाई कुटेर, लुटेर आधा मरेको छोडेका थिए।','Yarushalembaata Yariho jaane baato darlaagdo thiyo — daankuharule ek janaa yaatrulaai kutera, lutera aadhaa mareko chhodekaa thie.','The road from Jerusalem down to Jericho was dangerous — robbers had beaten a traveler and left him half dead.','Luke 10:30'],
['एउटा कुरा बुझ्नुपर्छ — त्यस बेला यहूदीहरू र सामरीहरू एकअर्कालाई घृणा गर्थे। सुन्नेहरूका लागि सामरी भनेको शत्रु थियो।','Eutaa kuraa bujhnuparchha — tyas belaa Yahudiharu ra Saamariharu ekarkaalaai ghrinaa garthe. Sunneharukaa laagi Saamari bhaneko shatru thiyo.','One thing to understand: in those days Jews and Samaritans despised each other. To the listeners, a Samaritan meant an enemy.','John 4:9'],
['बाटोमा घाइते मानिसलाई धर्मगुरुहरूले छोडे। तर एक जना सामरीले रोकिएर उसको हेरचाह गरे।','Baatomaa ghaaite maanislaai dharmaguruharule chhode. Tara ek janaa Saamarile rokiera usko herchaah gare.','Religious leaders passed the wounded man by. But a Samaritan — an outsider — stopped and cared for him.','Luke 10:30–35'],
['सामरीले घाउमा तेल र दाखमद्य लगाइदिए, उसलाई आफ्नै गधामा राखेर पौवामा लगे, र खर्च पनि तिरिदिए — फर्किंदा अरू लाग्यो भने म तिर्छु।','Saamarile ghaaumaa tel ra daakhmadhya lagaaidie, uslaai aaphnai gadhaamaa raakhera pauwaamaa lage, ra kharcha pani tiridie — pharkindaa aru laagyo bhane ma tirchhu.','He poured oil and wine on the wounds, set the man on his own donkey, brought him to an inn — and paid, promising: whatever more it costs, I will repay.','Luke 10:34–35'],
['येशूले भन्नुभयो — जाओ, तिमी पनि त्यस्तै गर।','Yeshule bhannubhayo — jaao, timi pani tyastai gara.','Jesus said: go and do the same.','Luke 10:37']]},
{id:'jbuilders',t:'The two builders',ne:'दुई घर बनाउनेहरू',art:FNE_ART.jbuilders,
note:['आफ्नो ठूलो उपदेशको अन्त्यमा येशूले सोध्नुहुन्छ — तिम्रो जीवनको जग के हो? सुन्नु राम्रो हो; गर्नु नै चट्टान हो।','Aaphno thulo updeshako antyamaa Yeshule sodhnuhunchha — timro jeewanko jag ke ho? Sunnu raamro ho; garnu nai chattaan ho.','Jesus ends his great sermon with a question: what is your life built on? Hearing is good — doing is the rock.'],
paras:[
['येशूले भन्नुभयो — मेरो वचन सुनेर पालन गर्ने मानिस चट्टानमाथि घर बनाउने बुद्धिमान् मानिसजस्तै हो।','Yeshule bhannubhayo — mero wachan sunera paalan garne maanis chattaanmaathi ghar banaaune buddhimaan maanisjastai ho.','Jesus said: whoever hears my words and does them is like a wise man who built his house on the rock.','Matthew 7:24'],
['वर्षा आयो, बाढी आयो, हुरी चल्यो — तर त्यो घर ढलेन, किनकि त्यसको जग चट्टानमाथि थियो।','Warshaa aayo, baadhi aayo, huri chalyo — tara tyo ghar dhalena, kinaki tyasko jag chattaanmaathi thiyo.','The rain came, the floods rose, the winds blew — but that house did not fall, because its foundation was on the rock.','Matthew 7:25'],
['तर सुनेर पनि नगर्ने मानिस बालुवामा घर बनाउने मूर्खजस्तै हो — हुरी आउँदा त्यो घर ठूलो गर्जनसँगै ढल्यो।','Tara sunera pani nagarne maanis baaluwaamaa ghar banaaune murkhajastai ho — huri aaundaa tyo ghar thulo garjansangai dhalyo.','But the one who hears and does not act is like a fool who built on sand — when the storm came, that house fell with a great crash.','Matthew 7:26–27'],
['यी दुई घर बाहिरबाट उस्तै देखिन्थे। फरक देखियो — आँधी आएपछि मात्र। जग परीक्षामा मात्र देखिन्छ।','Yi dui ghar baahirbaata ustai dekhinthe. Pharak dekhiyo — aandhi aaepachhi maatra. Jag parikshaamaa maatra dekhinchha.','From the outside the two houses looked the same. The difference showed only when the storm came. Foundations are revealed by testing.','Matthew 7:24–27']]},
{id:'jcross',t:'The cross',ne:'क्रूस',art:FNE_ART.jcross,
note:['क्रूस येशूको सेवामा आइपरेको दुर्घटना थिएन — त्यो नै उहाँको सेवा थियो। कसैले उहाँको ज्यान खोसेन; उहाँले आफैँ दिनुभयो — प्रेमले पूरा मोल खुशीसाथ तिर्यो।','Kroos Yeshuko sewaamaa aaipareko durghatanaa thiena — tyo nai uhaanko sewaa thiyo. Kasaile uhaanko jyaan khosena; uhaanle aaphain dinubhayo — premle puraa mol khushisaath tiryo.','The cross was not an accident that interrupted Jesus’ mission — it WAS the mission. Nobody took his life; he laid it down, love paying the full price willingly.'],
paras:[
['आफ्ना साथीहरूका लागि ज्यान दिनुभन्दा ठूलो प्रेम अरू छैन — अनि येशूले त्यही गर्नुभयो।','Aaphnaa saathiharukaa laagi jyaan dinubhandaa thulo prem aru chhaina — ani Yeshule tyahi garnubhayo.','There is no greater love than to lay down your life for your friends — and that is exactly what Jesus did.','John 15:13'],
['धार्मिक अगुवाहरूको डाहले उहाँलाई मृत्युसम्म पुर्यायो। तर येशूले भन्नुभएको थियो — कसैले मेरो ज्यान खोस्दैन; म आफैँ दिन्छु।','Dhaarmik aguwaaharuko daahale uhaanlaai mrityusamma puryaayo. Tara Yeshule bhannubhaeko thiyo — kasaile mero jyaan khosdaina; ma aaphain dinchhu.','The envy of the religious leaders drove him to his death. But Jesus had already said: no one takes my life from me — I lay it down myself.','Matthew 27:18 · John 10:18'],
['क्रूसमा उहाँले प्रार्थना गर्नुभयो — पिता, यिनीहरूलाई क्षमा गर्नुहोस्।','Kroosmaa uhaanle praarthanaa garnubhayo — Pitaa, yiniharulaai kshamaa garnuhos.','From the cross he prayed: Father, forgive them.','Luke 23:34'],
['मध्यदिनमा तीन घण्टासम्म अन्धकार छायो। हाम्रो पापको सारा भार उहाँमाथि थियो।','Madhyadinmaa tin ghantaasamma andhakaar chhaayo. Haamro paapko saaraa bhaar uhaanmaathi thiyo.','At midday, darkness covered the land for three hours. The whole weight of our sin was upon him.','Matthew 27:45'],
['उहाँ पिताको प्रेम र राज्य प्रकट गर्न आउनुभएको थियो — तैपनि हामीले उहाँलाई इन्कार गर्यौं; मानिसहरूले नै उहाँलाई मारे। तर हामीलाई पनि, हामीले सेवा गर्ने अन्धकारका शक्तिहरूलाई पनि थाहा थिएन — यो त सुरुदेखिकै योजनाको हिस्सा थियो। येशूको मृत्युद्वारा नै परमेश्वरको राज्य स्वर्गमा जस्तै पृथ्वीमा पनि आउँदै थियो।','Uhaan Pitaako prem ra raajya prakat garna aaunubhaeko thiyo — taipani haamile uhaanlaai inkaar garyaun; maanisharule nai uhaanlaai maare. Tara haamilaai pani, haamile sewaa garne andhakaarkaa shaktiharulaai pani thaahaa thiena — yo ta surudekhikai yojanaako hissaa thiyo. Yeshuko mrityudwaaraa nai Parameshwarko raajya swargamaa jastai prithvimaa pani aaundai thiyo.','He had come to reveal the Father’s love and kingdom — yet we rejected him; human beings killed him. But neither we nor the dark forces we obeyed knew this was part of the plan all along. Through Jesus’ death, God’s kingdom was coming on earth as it is in heaven.','Acts 2:23 · 1 Corinthians 2:8'],
['येशूको छेउमा दुई जना डाँकू पनि झुण्ड्याइएका थिए। एउटाले भन्यो — येशू, तपाईं आफ्नो राज्यमा आउनुहुँदा मलाई सम्झनुहोस्। येशूले भन्नुभयो — आजै तिमी मसँग स्वर्गलोकमा हुनेछौ।','Yeshuko chheumaa dui janaa daanku pani jhundyaaiekaa thie. Eutaale bhanyo — Yeshu, tapaain aaphno raajyamaa aaunuhundaa malaai samjhanuhos. Yeshule bhannubhayo — aajai timi masanga swargalokmaa hunechhau.','Two criminals hung beside Jesus. One said: Jesus, remember me when you come into your kingdom. Jesus answered: today you will be with me in paradise.','Luke 23:39–43'],
['उहाँले भन्नुभयो — सिद्धियो। हाम्रो पापको मोल पूरा तिरियो।','Uhaanle bhannubhayo — siddhiyo. Haamro paapko mol puraa tiriyo.','He said: it is finished. The price of our sin was fully paid.','John 19:30']]},
{id:'jrisen',t:'He is risen',ne:'जीवित हुनुहुन्छ',art:FNE_ART.jrisen,
note:['सबै कुरा यही बिहानमा अडिन्छ। चिहान रित्तो भएकोले मृत्यु अब पर्खाल होइन, ढोका हो — र जीवित येशूले आज पनि मानिसहरूलाई नाम काढेर बोलाउनुहुन्छ।','Sabai kuraa yahi bihaanmaa adinchha. Chihaan ritto bhaekole mrityu aba parkhaal hoina, dhokaa ho — ra jeewit Yeshule aaja pani maanisharulaai naam kaadhera bolaunuhunchha.','Everything stands on this morning. Because the tomb is empty, death is no longer a wall but a door — and the risen Jesus still calls people by name.'],
paras:[
['आइतबार बिहान चिहान रित्तो थियो। येशू जीवित हुनुभएको थियो।','Aaitabaar bihaana chihaan ritto thiyo. Yeshu jeewit hunubhaeko thiyo.','On Sunday morning the tomb was empty. Jesus was alive.','Luke 24:1–8'],
['मरियम मग्दलिनी — येशूलाई पछ्याउने एउटी स्त्री — चिहान नजिक रोइरहेकी थिइन्। उनले उहाँलाई चिनिनन् — जबसम्म उहाँले एउटै शब्द भन्नुभयो — मरियम। आफ्नो नाम सुन्नेबित्तिकै उनले चिनिन्।','Mariyam Magdalini — Yeshulaai pachhyaaune euti stree — chihaan najik roirahekii thiin. Unle uhaanlaai chininan — jabasamma uhaanle eutai shabda bhannubhayo — Mariyam. Aaphno naam sunnebittikai unle chinin.','Mary Magdalene — a woman who had followed Jesus — stood weeping near the tomb. She did not recognize him, until he spoke a single word: Mary. The moment she heard her name, she knew.','John 20:14–16'],
['चेला थोमाले भने — नदेखी म विश्वास गर्दिनँ। येशू आउनुभयो र भन्नुभयो — मेरा हातहरू हेर, छोएर हेर। थोमाले भने — मेरा प्रभु, मेरा परमेश्वर!','Chelaa Thomaale bhane — nadekhi ma vishwaas gardinan. Yeshu aaunubhayo ra bhannubhayo — meraa haatharu hera, chhoera hera. Thomaale bhane — meraa Prabhu, meraa Parameshwar!','Thomas said: unless I see, I will not believe. Jesus came to him and said: look at my hands — touch and see. Thomas cried out: my Lord and my God!','John 20:24–29'],
['उहाँको मृत्यु र पुनरुत्थानद्वारा हामी परमेश्वरसँग मिलाइयौं, र मानिसलाई पकडमा राख्ने अन्धकारका शक्तिहरू पराजित भए। त्योभन्दा पनि ठूलो कुरा — अब परमेश्वर आफ्नो आत्माद्वारा हामीभित्रै बास गर्नुहुन्छ। उहाँलाई भेट्न अब मन्दिर जानुपर्दैन; उहाँका मानिसहरू नै उहाँको मन्दिर भएका छन्।','Uhaanko mrityu ra punarutthaandwaaraa haami Parameshwarsanga milaaiyaun, ra maanislaai pakadmaa raakhne andhakaarkaa shaktiharu paraajit bhae. Tyobhandaa pani thulo kuraa — aba Parameshwar aaphno aatmaadwaaraa haamibhitrai baas garnuhunchha. Uhaanlaai bhetna aba mandir jaanupardaina; uhaankaa maanisharu nai uhaanko mandir bhaekaa chhan.','Through his death and resurrection we were reconciled to God, and the dark powers that held humanity in their grip were defeated. And more than that — God now dwells within us by his Spirit. We no longer go to a temple to meet him; his people ARE his temple.','Colossians 2:15 · 1 Corinthians 3:16'],
['उहाँले चेलाहरूलाई भन्नुभयो — जाओ, सबै जातिहरूलाई मेरा चेला बनाओ। म सधैँ तिमीहरूसँग छु।','Uhaanle chelaaharulaai bhannubhayo — jaao, sabai jaatiharulaai meraa chelaa banaao. Ma sadhain timiharusanga chhu.','He told his followers: go, make disciples of all nations — and remember, I am with you always.','Matthew 28:18–20'],
['येशूको जीवन, मृत्यु र पुनरुत्थानले संसार बदल्यो — एक-एक व्यक्ति गर्दै। आज पनि उहाँ जीवित हुनुहुन्छ, र उहाँले तपाईंलाई बोलाउनुहुन्छ।','Yeshuko jeewan, mrityu ra punarutthaanle sansaar badalyo — ek-ek vyakti gardai. Aaja pani uhaan jeewit hunuhunchha, ra uhaanle tapaainlaai bolaunuhunchha.','The life, death and resurrection of Jesus changed the world — one person at a time. He is alive today — and he is calling you.','Revelation 3:20']]}
]},

{id:'facts',kind:'arc',title:'Jesus’ Followers',ne:'येशूका चेलाहरू',
overview:{t:'The church in short',ne:'मण्डली — छोटकरीमा',art:FNE_ART.ovacts,
start:['सुरुदेखि हेरौं','From here — the whole story in detail'],
paras:[
['येशू मृत्युबाट जीवित हुनुभयो — र उहाँको कथा त्यहीँ सकिएन। उहाँ पिताकहाँ फर्कनुभयो, र दश दिनपछि परमेश्वरको आत्मा उहाँका चेलाहरूभित्र वास गर्न आउनुभयो।','Yeshu mrityubaata jivit hunubhayo — ra uhaanko kathaa tyahin sakiena. Uhaan Pitaakahaan pharkanubhayo, ra dash dinpachhi Parameshwarko Aatmaa uhaankaa chelaaharubhitra baas garna aaunubhayo.','Jesus rose from the dead — and his story did not end there. He returned to the Father, and ten days later God’s Spirit came to live inside his followers.'],
['साधारण मानिसहरू — जालहारीहरू, महिलाहरू, कर उठाउनेहरू — नयाँ किसिमको परिवार बने: सँगै खाने, सँगै प्रार्थना गर्ने, आफूसँग भएको बाँड्ने।','Saadhaaran maanisharu — jaalahaariharu, mahilaaharu, kar uthaauneharu — nayaan kisimko pariwaar bane: sangai khaane, sangai praarthanaa garne, aaphusanga bhaeko baandne.','Ordinary people — fishermen, women, tax collectors — became a new kind of family: eating together, praying together, sharing what they had.'],
['उनीहरूलाई सताइयो, तितरबितर पारियो, कतिलाई मारियो पनि। तर सन्देशलाई जति थिचियो, त्यति नै टाढा फैलियो।','Uniharulaai sataaiyo, titarbitar paariyo, katilaai maariyo pani. Tara sandeshlaai jati thichiyo, tyati nai taadhaa phailiyo.','They were persecuted, scattered, even killed. But the more the message was pressed down, the further it spread.'],
['मण्डलीको सबैभन्दा डरलाग्दो शत्रुले समेत येशूलाई भेट्यो र उहाँको सन्देशवाहक बन्यो। सिमाना एकपछि अर्को गर्दै खुल्दै गए — सुसमाचार हरेक जातिको लागि थियो।','Mandaliko sabaibhandaa darlaagdo shatrule samet Yeshulaai bhetyo ra uhaanko sandeshwaahak banyo. Simaanaa ekpachhi arko gardai khuldai gae — susamaachaar harek jaatiko laagi thiyo.','Even the fiercest enemy of the church met Jesus and became his messenger. Border after border opened: the good news was for every nation.'],
['एउटै पुस्ताभित्र त्यो सन्देश यरूशलेमबाट साम्राज्यको राजधानीसम्म पुग्यो — सेनाले होइन, साक्षीहरूले बोकेर।','Eutai pustaabhitra tyo sandesh Yarushalembaata saamraajyako raajdhaanisamma pugyo — senaale hoina, saakshiharule bokera.','Within one generation the message had traveled from Jerusalem to the capital of the empire — carried not by armies but by witnesses.'],
['अनि त्यो अघि बढिरह्यो — पहाड र समुद्र पार गर्दै, शताब्दीपछि शताब्दी — तपाईंको देशसम्म नपुगुन्जेल। यही त्यो कथा हो।','Ani tyo aghi badhirahyo — pahaad ra samudra paar gardai, shataabdipachhi shataabdi — tapaainko deshsamma napugunjel. Yahi tyo kathaa ho.','And it kept going — across mountains and oceans, century after century, until it reached your country too. This is that story.']]},
sections:[
{id:'await',t:'Wait for the gift',ne:'वरदान पर्खनुहोस्',art:FNE_ART.await,
note:['मण्डलीको कथा काम गरेर होइन, पर्खेर र प्रार्थना गरेर सुरु हुन्छ। परमेश्वरको काम हाम्रो बलले होइन — उहाँकै वरदानबाट सुरु हुन्छ।','Mandaliko kathaa kaam garera hoina, parkhera ra praarthanaa garera suru hunchha. Parameshwarko kaam haamro balle hoina — uhaankai waradaanbaata suru hunchha.','The story of the church begins not with action but with waiting and prayer. God’s work starts with God’s gift — not with our strength.'],
paras:[
['जीवित भएपछि चालीस दिनसम्म येशू आफ्ना साथीहरूलाई भेटिरहनुभयो — उनीहरूसँग खानुभयो, परमेश्वरको राज्यको बारेमा सिकाउनुभयो। उहाँ साँच्चै जीवित हुनुहुन्थ्यो।','Jivit bhaepachhi chaalis dinsamma Yeshu aaphnaa saathiharulaai bhetirahanubhayo — uniharusanga khaanubhayo, Parameshwarko raajyako baaremaa sikaaunubhayo. Uhaan saanchai jivit hunuhunthyo.','For forty days after he rose, Jesus kept meeting his friends — eating with them, teaching them about God’s kingdom. He was unmistakably alive.','Acts 1:3'],
['उहाँले एउटा प्रतिज्ञा र एउटा काम दिनुभयो — पवित्र आत्मा नआउन्जेल यरूशलेममा पर्खनू; त्यसपछि तिमीहरू मेरा साक्षी हुनेछौ — यो सहरमा, छिमेकी देशमा, र पृथ्वीको अन्तिम छेउसम्म।','Uhaanle eutaa pratigyaa ra eutaa kaam dinubhayo — Pavitra Aatmaa naaunjel Yarushalemmaa parkhanu; tyaspachhi timiharu meraa saakshi hunechhau — yo saharmaa, chhimeki deshmaa, ra prithviko antim chheusamma.','He gave them a promise and a task: wait in Jerusalem until the Holy Spirit comes upon you — then you will be my witnesses, in this city, in the next country, and to the very ends of the earth.','Acts 1:4–8'],
['अनि उनीहरूले हेर्दाहेर्दै उहाँ माथि उचालिनुभयो, र बादलले उहाँलाई ढाक्यो। दुई स्वर्गदूतले भने — यही येशू फेरि फर्केर आउनुहुनेछ, जसरी जानुभएको देख्यौ, त्यसरी नै।','Ani uniharule herdaaherdai uhaan maathi uchaalinubhayo, ra baadalle uhaanlaai dhaakyo. Dui swargadutle bhane — yahi Yeshu pheri pharkera aaunuhunechha, jasari jaanubhaeko dekhyau, tyasari nai.','Then, as they watched, he was taken up, and a cloud hid him from their eyes. Two angels stood beside them: this same Jesus will come back, the same way you saw him go.','Acts 1:9–11'],
['साक्षी भनेको आफूले देखेको कुरा बताउने मानिस मात्र हो। योजना यत्ति नै थियो — सेना होइन, पैसा होइन, केवल उहाँलाई चिन्ने मानिसहरू।','Saakshi bhaneko aaphule dekheko kuraa bataaune maanis maatra ho. Yojanaa yatti nai thiyo — senaa hoina, paisaa hoina, kewal uhaanlaai chinne maanisharu.','A witness is simply someone who tells what they have seen. That was the whole plan — no army, no money, just people who knew him.'],
['त्यसैले करिब एक सय बीस जना माथिल्लो कोठामा सँगै पर्खिबसे — पुरुष र महिला, उहाँकी आमा मरियम पनि — र उनीहरूले प्रार्थना गरिरहे।','Tyasaile karib ek saya bis janaa maathillo kothaamaa sangai parkhibase — purush ra mahilaa, uhaanki aamaa Mariyam pani — ra uniharule praarthanaa garirahe.','So about a hundred and twenty of them waited together in an upstairs room — men and women, his mother Mary among them — and they prayed.','Acts 1:12–14']]},
{id:'pentecost',t:'Wind and fire',ne:'हावा र आगो',art:FNE_ART.pentecost,
note:['बाबेलमा भाषाहरू छरिए; पेन्तिकोसमा परमेश्वर ती सबै भाषाहरूमा बोल्नुहुन्छ। परमेश्वरको परिवारमा हरेक मातृभाषाको लागि ठाउँ छ — तपाईंको भाषाको लागि पनि।','Baabelmaa bhaashaaharu chharie; Pentikosmaa Parameshwar ti sabai bhaashaaharumaa bolnuhunchha. Parameshwarko pariwaarmaa harek maatribhaashaako laagi thaaun chha — tapaainko bhaashaako laagi pani.','Babel scattered the languages; at Pentecost God speaks through all of them. God’s family has room for every mother tongue — including yours.'],
paras:[
['पेन्तिकोस भन्ने कटनीको चाडको लागि यरूशलेम भरिएको थियो — हरेक देशबाट आएका मानिसहरूले।','Pentikos bhanne kataniko chaadko laagi Yarushalem bhariyeko thiyo — harek deshbaata aaekaa maanisharule.','Jerusalem was crowded for the harvest festival called Pentecost, with visitors from every land.','Acts 2:1,5'],
['अचानक हुरी चलेजस्तो आवाजले घर भरियो, र आगोका साना जिब्राजस्ता ज्वालाहरू हरेकमाथि बसे। सबै जना पवित्र आत्माले भरिए।','Achaanak huri chalejasto aawaajle ghar bhariyo, ra aagokaa saanaa jibraajastaa jwaalaaharu harekmaathi base. Sabai janaa Pavitra Aatmaale bharie.','Suddenly a sound like a rushing wind filled the house, and what looked like small flames of fire rested on each of them. All of them were filled with the Holy Spirit.','Acts 2:2–4'],
['उनीहरू आफूले कहिल्यै नसिकेका भाषाहरूमा बोल्न थाले — र ती आगन्तुकहरूले, हरेकले आ-आफ्नै मातृभाषामा, परमेश्वरका महान् कामहरूको बयान सुने।','Uniharu aaphule kahilyai nasikekaa bhaashaaharumaa bolna thaale — ra ti aagantukharule, harekle aa-aaphnai maatribhaashaamaa, Parameshwarkaa mahaan kaamharuko bayaan sune.','They began to speak in languages they had never learned — and the visitors heard, each in their own mother tongue, the great things God has done.','Acts 2:4–11'],
['परमेश्वरलाई मानिसहरूसँग उनीहरूकै भाषामा बोल्न मन पर्छ — मुटुको भाषा, आमाको भाषा। आज पनि उहाँ त्यसै गर्नुहुन्छ।','Parameshwarlaai maanisharusanga uniharukai bhaashaamaa bolna man parchha — mutuko bhaashaa, aamaako bhaashaa. Aaja pani uhaan tyasai garnuhunchha.','God loves to speak to people in their own language — heart-language, mother tongue. He still does.'],
['अनि पत्रुस — एक समय येशूलाई इन्कार गरेको त्यही जालहारी — उभिएर सारा कथा सुनाए: तिमीहरूले उहाँलाई मार्‍यौ; परमेश्वरले उहाँलाई जीवित पार्नुभयो; उहाँ नै प्रभु हुनुहुन्छ। सुन्नेहरूको मुटु छियो — अब हामी के गरौं?','Ani Patrus — ek samaya Yeshulaai inkaar gareko tyahi jaalahaari — ubhiera saaraa kathaa sunaae: timiharule uhaanlaai maaryau; Parameshwarle uhaanlaai jivit paarnubhayo; uhaan nai Prabhu hunuhunchha. Sunneharuko mutu chhiyo — aba haami ke garaun?','Then Peter — the fisherman who had once denied Jesus — stood up and told the whole story: you killed him; God raised him; he is Lord. The listeners were cut to the heart: what should we do?','Acts 2:14–37'],
['परमेश्वरतिर फर्क र बप्तिस्मा लेओ, पत्रुसले भने, र तिमीहरूले पनि त्यही वरदान पाउनेछौ। त्यो दिन करिब तीन हजार मानिसले विश्वास गरे। मण्डली जन्मियो।','Parameshwartira pharka ra baptismaa leo, Patrusle bhane, ra timiharule pani tyahi waradaan paaunechhau. Tyo din karib tin hajaar maanisle vishwaas gare. Mandali janmiyo.','Turn back to God and be baptized, Peter said, and you will receive the same gift. That day about three thousand people believed. The church was born.','Acts 2:38–41']]},
{id:'together',t:'Life together',ne:'सँगसँगैको जीवन',art:FNE_ART.together,
note:['पहिलो मण्डली शक्ति वा चलाख योजनाले होइन, देखिने प्रेमले बढ्यो। हेर्नेहरूले भने — हेर त, यिनीहरूले एक-अर्कालाई कति प्रेम गर्छन्!','Pahilo mandali shakti waa chalaakh yojanaale hoina, dekhine premle badhyo. Herneharule bhane — her ta, yiniharule ek-arkaalaai kati prem garchhan!','The first church grew not through power or clever plans, but through love that could be seen. Watching them, people said: see how they love one another!'],
paras:[
['नयाँ विश्वासीहरू चार कुरामा लागिरहे: प्रेरितहरूको शिक्षा, सङ्गति, सँगै रोटी भाँच्ने काम, र प्रार्थना।','Nayaan vishwaasiharu chaar kuraamaa laagirahe: preritharuko shikshaa, sangati, sangai roti bhaanchne kaam, ra praarthanaa.','The new believers devoted themselves to four things: the apostles’ teaching, fellowship, breaking bread together, and prayer.','Acts 2:42'],
['उनीहरू खुसी मनले एक-अर्काको घरमा खान्थे। कसैलाई खाँचो नपरोस् भनेर आफूसँग भएको बेचेर बाँड्थे।','Uniharu khusi manle ek-arkaako gharmaa khaanthe. Kasailaai khaancho naparos bhanera aaphusanga bhaeko bechera baandthe.','They ate in each other’s homes with glad hearts. They sold what they could spare so that no one among them was in need.','Acts 2:44–46'],
['धनी र गरिब, पुरुष र महिला, स्थानीय र परदेशी — सबै एउटै भान्सामा बसे। रगतको होइन, येशूको परिवार।','Dhani ra garib, purush ra mahilaa, sthaaniya ra pardeshi — sabai eutai bhaansaamaa base. Ragatko hoina, Yeshuko pariwaar.','Rich and poor, men and women, locals and foreigners sat at one table — a family not of blood, but of Jesus.'],
['यही सँगसँगैको जीवनलाई मण्डली भनिन्छ। मण्डली कहिल्यै भवन थिएन — येशूका भएका, एक-अर्काका भएका मानिसहरू नै मण्डली हुन्।','Yahi sangsangaiko jivanlaai mandali bhaninchha. Mandali kahilyai bhawan thiena — Yeshukaa bhaekaa, ek-arkaakaa bhaekaa maanisharu nai mandali hun.','This life together is called the church. The church was never a building; it is people who belong to Jesus, belonging to each other.'],
['र दिनदिनै छिमेकीहरूले हेरिरहे — र दिनदिनै परमेश्वरले उनीहरूको सङ्ख्यामा अरू थपिदिनुभयो।','Ra dindinnai chhimekiharule herirahe — ra dindinnai Parameshwarle uniharuko sankhyaamaa aru thapidinubhayo.','And day by day their neighbors watched — and day by day, God added more people to their number.','Acts 2:47']]},
{id:'boldness',t:'In the name of Jesus',ne:'येशूको नाममा',art:FNE_ART.boldness,
note:['साहस तालिम वा पदबाट आएन। येशूलाई चिनेकोबाट आयो — आज पनि त्यहीँबाट नै आउँछ।','Saahas taalim waa padbaata aaena. Yeshulaai chinekobaata aayo — aaja pani tyahinbaata nai aaunchha.','Courage did not come from training or position. It came from knowing Jesus — the same place it comes from today.'],
paras:[
['मन्दिरको ढोकामा जन्मदेखि नै हिँड्न नसक्ने एक जना मानिस बस्थ्यो। उसले पत्रुस र यूहन्नासँग पैसा माग्यो।','Mandirko dhokaamaa janmadekhi nai hindna nasakne ek janaa maanis basthyo. Usle Patrus ra Yuhannaasanga paisaa maagyo.','At the temple gate sat a man who had never walked. He asked Peter and John for money.','Acts 3:1–3'],
['सुन र चाँदी त मसँग छैन, पत्रुसले भने, तर जे छ, त्यही दिन्छु — नासरतका येशू ख्रीष्टको नाममा, उठ र हिँड। अनि ऊ उठ्यो — हिँड्दै, उफ्रँदै, परमेश्वरको प्रशंसा गर्दै।','Sun ra chaandi ta masanga chhaina, Patrusle bhane, tara je chha, tyahi dinchhu — Naasaratkaa Yeshu Khristko naammaa, uth ra hind. Ani u uthyo — hinddai, uphrandai, Parameshwarko prashansaa gardai.','Silver and gold I do not have, Peter said, but what I have I give you: in the name of Jesus Christ of Nazareth, stand up and walk. And he did — walking, and leaping, and praising God.','Acts 3:6–8'],
['धार्मिक अधिकारीहरूले उनीहरूलाई पक्रे र आदेश दिए — फेरि कहिल्यै यो नाम नलिनू।','Dhaarmik adhikaariharule uniharulaai pakre ra aadesh die — pheri kahilyai yo naam nalinu.','The religious authorities arrested them and ordered them: never speak this name again.','Acts 4:1–3,18'],
['पत्रुस र यूहन्नाले जवाफ दिए — परमेश्वरको भन्दा तपाईंहरूको कुरा मान्नु ठीक हो कि होइन, आफैँ विचार गर्नुहोस् — हामीले देखेका र सुनेका कुरा नबोली बस्नै सक्दैनौं।','Patrus ra Yuhannaale jawaaph die — Parameshwarko bhandaa tapaainharuko kuraa maannu thik ho ki hoina, aaphain vichaar garnuhos — haamile dekhekaa ra sunekaa kuraa naboli basnai sakdainaun.','Peter and John answered: judge for yourselves whether it is right to obey you rather than God — we cannot stop speaking about what we have seen and heard.','Acts 4:19–20'],
['सभा छक्क पर्‍यो — यिनीहरू त साधारण, नपढेका मानिस थिए। तर उनीहरू येशूसँग बसेका थिए।','Sabhaa chhakka paryo — yiniharu ta saadhaaran, napadhekaa maanis thie. Tara uniharu Yeshusanga basekaa thie.','The council was astonished: these were ordinary, unschooled men — but they had been with Jesus.','Acts 4:13']]},
{id:'scattered',t:'Scattered seed',ne:'छरिएको बीउ',art:FNE_ART.scattered,
note:['मण्डलीको सबैभन्दा अँध्यारो दिन नै त्यसको सबैभन्दा फराकिलो ढोका बन्यो। परमेश्वरले सतावटलाई समेत रोपाइँमा बदल्न सक्नुहुन्छ।','Mandaliko sabaibhandaa andhyaaro din nai tyasko sabaibhandaa pharaakilo dhokaa banyo. Parameshwarle sataawatlaai samet ropaainmaa badalna saknuhunchha.','The church’s darkest day became its widest door. God can turn even persecution into planting.'],
paras:[
['सबैले सन्देशलाई स्वागत गरेनन्। अनुग्रह र शक्तिले भरिएका स्तिफनस नाम गरेका एक विश्वासीलाई सभाको अगाडि घिसारेर लगियो।','Sabaile sandeshlaai swaagat garenan. Anugraha ra shaktile bhariekaa Stiphanas naam garekaa ek vishwaasilaai sabhaako agaadi ghisaarera lagiyo.','Not everyone welcomed the message. A believer named Stephen — full of grace and power — was dragged before the council.','Acts 6:8–12'],
['उनले परमेश्वरका जनको सारा कथा सुनाए, र अन्त्यमा भने — तिमीहरूले त्यो धर्मी जनलाई धोका दियौ र मार्‍यौ।','Unle Parameshwarkaa janko saaraa kathaa sunaae, ra antyamaa bhane — timiharule tyo dharmi janlaai dhokaa diyau ra maaryau.','He told them the whole story of God’s people, and then he said: you have betrayed and murdered the Righteous One.','Acts 7:51–52'],
['उनीहरूले उनलाई ढुङ्गाले हाने। मर्दै गर्दा उनले आफ्ना प्रभुले जस्तै प्रार्थना गरे — प्रभु, यो पाप यिनीहरूको विरुद्धमा नगन्नुहोस्। येशूको लागि मर्ने उनी पहिलो भए।','Uniharule unlaai dungaale haane. Mardai gardaa unle aaphnaa Prabhule jastai praarthanaa gare — Prabhu, yo paap yiniharuko biruddhamaa nagannuhos. Yeshuko laagi marne uni pahilo bhae.','They stoned him. As he died he prayed like his Lord: Lord, do not hold this sin against them. He was the first to die for Jesus.','Acts 7:59–60'],
['त्यही दिनदेखि ठूलो सतावट सुरु भयो, र विश्वासीहरू यरूशलेमबाट तितरबितर भए। अन्त्य आएजस्तो देखियो।','Tyahi dindekhi thulo sataawat suru bhayo, ra vishwaasiharu Yarushalembaata titarbitar bhae. Antya aaejasto dekhiyo.','A great persecution broke out that day, and the believers were scattered from Jerusalem. It looked like the end.','Acts 8:1'],
['तर जहाँ-जहाँ छरिए, त्यहाँ-त्यहाँ उनीहरूले सन्देश पनि लगे — र सहरपिच्छे नयाँ मण्डलीहरू उम्रन थाले। छरिएको बीउ मर्दैन; उम्रन्छ।','Tara jahaan-jahaan chharie, tyahaan-tyahaan uniharule sandesh pani lage — ra saharpichchhe nayaan mandaliharu umrana thaale. Chharieko biu mardaina; umranchha.','But wherever they were scattered, they carried the message with them — and new churches sprang up in town after town. Scattered seed does not die; it grows.','Acts 8:4']]},
{id:'damascus',t:'The enemy becomes a brother',ne:'शत्रु भाइ बन्छ',art:FNE_ART.damascus,
note:['येशूको पहुँचभन्दा बाहिर कोही छैन — मण्डलीको सबैभन्दा ठूलो शत्रु पनि छैन। धम्की ओकल्ने मानिस प्रेमका पत्रहरू लेख्ने मानिस बन्यो।','Yeshuko pahunchbhandaa baahira kohi chhaina — mandaliko sabaibhandaa thulo shatru pani chhaina. Dhamki okalne maanis premkaa patraharu lekhne maanis banyo.','Nobody is beyond the reach of Jesus — not even the church’s worst enemy. The man breathing threats became the man writing letters of love.'],
paras:[
['मण्डलीको सबैभन्दा कडा सिकारी शाऊल नाम गरेको एक जवान थियो। ऊ घर-घर पसेर विश्वासीहरूलाई झ्यालखानामा घिसार्थ्यो — स्तिफनसको हत्यामा पनि ऊ सहमत थियो।','Mandaliko sabaibhandaa kadaa sikaari Shaaul naam gareko ek jawaan thiyo. U ghar-ghar pasera vishwaasiharulaai jhyaalkhaanaamaa ghisaarthyo — Stiphanasko hatyaamaa pani u sahamat thiyo.','The fiercest hunter of the church was a young man named Saul. He went house to house, dragging believers to prison — and he approved of Stephen’s death.','Acts 8:1,3'],
['दमस्कस जाने बाटोमा अचानक स्वर्गबाट एउटा ज्योति उसको वरिपरि चम्क्यो, र ऊ भुइँमा लोट्यो। एउटा आवाज आयो — शाऊल, शाऊल, तिमी मलाई किन सताउँछौ?','Damaskas jaane baatomaa achaanak swargabaata eutaa jyoti usko waripari chamkyo, ra u bhuinmaa lotyo. Eutaa aawaaj aayo — Shaaul, Shaaul, timi malaai kina sataaunchhau?','On the road to Damascus a light from heaven suddenly flashed around him, and he fell to the ground. A voice said: Saul, Saul, why do you persecute me?','Acts 9:3–4'],
['प्रभु, तपाईं को हुनुहुन्छ? उसले सोध्यो। म येशू हुँ, जसलाई तिमी सताउँछौ।','Prabhu, tapaain ko hunuhunchha? Usle sodhyo. Ma Yeshu hun, jaslaai timi sataaunchhau.','Who are you, Lord? he asked. I am Jesus, whom you are persecuting.','Acts 9:5'],
['ध्यान दिनुहोस् — येशूले मेरा मानिसहरू भन्नुभएन — मलाई भन्नुभयो। उहाँका जनलाई छुने कुराले उहाँलाई नै छुन्छ।','Dhyaan dinuhos — Yeshule meraa maanisharu bhannubhaena — malaai bhannubhayo. Uhaankaa janlaai chhune kuraale uhaanlaai nai chhunchha.','Notice: Jesus did not say “my people” — he said ME. Whatever touches his people touches him.'],
['अन्धा भएको शाऊललाई डोर्‍याएर सहरभित्र लगियो। हननिया नाम गरेका एक विश्वासी — उसदेखि डराउँदा डराउँदै पनि — आए, उसमाथि हात राखे र भने — भाइ शाऊल। उसका आँखा फेरि देख्ने भए, र उसले बप्तिस्मा लियो।','Andhaa bhaeko Shaaullaai doryaaera saharbhitra lagiyo. Hananiyaa naam garekaa ek vishwaasi — usdekhi daraaundaa daraaundai pani — aae, usmaathi haat raakhe ra bhane — bhaai Shaaul. Uskaa aankhaa pheri dekhne bhae, ra usle baptismaa liyo.','Blinded, Saul was led into the city. A believer named Ananias — though terrified of him — came, laid his hands on him and said: Brother Saul. His sight returned, and he was baptized.','Acts 9:8–18'],
['सिकारी सन्देशवाहक बन्यो। उसलाई आज हामी पावल भनेर चिन्छौं — जसले सुसमाचारलाई अरू कसैले भन्दा टाढासम्म पुर्‍यायो।','Sikaari sandeshwaahak banyo. Uslaai aaja haami Paawal bhanera chinchhaun — jasle susamaachaarlaai aru kasaile bhandaa taadhaasamma puryaayo.','The hunter became a messenger. We know him today as Paul — who would carry the good news further than anyone.','Acts 9:20–22']]},
{id:'cornelius',t:'No outsiders anymore',ne:'अब कोही पराई छैन',art:FNE_ART.cornelius,
note:['अब कोही पराई रहेन। कुनै जाति, कुनै थर, कुनै वर्ग परमेश्वरको नजिक अर्कोभन्दा छैन — ढोका सबैका लागि उत्तिकै खुला, उत्तिकै नजिक छ।','Aba kohi paraai rahena. Kunai jaati, kunai thar, kunai warga Parameshwarko najik arkobhandaa chhaina — dhokaa sabaikaa laagi uttikai khulaa, uttikai najik chha.','There are no outsiders left. No nation, no clan, no caste stands closer to God than another — the door is equally open, and equally near.'],
paras:[
['त्यो बेला धेरैले सुसमाचार एउटै जातिको मात्र हो भन्ठान्थे। परमेश्वरले ढोका चौडा खोल्न लाग्नुभएको थियो।','Tyo belaa dheraile susamaachaar eutai jaatiko maatra ho bhanthaanthe. Parameshwarle dhokaa chaudaa kholna laagnubhaeko thiyo.','In those days many believed the good news belonged to one nation only. God was about to open the door wide.'],
['कर्नेलियस नाम गरेका एक रोमी सैनिक अफिसर — परमेश्वरको भय मान्ने एक परदेशी — ले दर्शनमा स्वर्गदूत देखे: पत्रुसलाई बोलाऊ।','Karneliyas naam garekaa ek Romi sainik aphisar — Parameshwarko bhaya maanne ek pardeshi — le darshanmaa swargadut dekhe: Patruslaai bolaau.','A Roman army officer named Cornelius — a foreigner who feared God — saw an angel in a vision: send for Peter.','Acts 10:1–5'],
['उता पत्रुसले चाहिँ हरेक किसिमका पशु भएको दर्शन देखे, र सुने — परमेश्वरले शुद्ध पार्नुभएकोलाई अशुद्ध नभन। तीन पटकसम्म।','Utaa Patrusle chaahin harek kisimkaa pashu bhaeko darshan dekhe, ra sune — Parameshwarle shuddha paarnubhaekolaai ashuddha nabhana. Tin pataksamma.','Meanwhile Peter saw a vision of every kind of animal, and heard: do not call unclean what God has made clean. Three times.','Acts 10:9–16'],
['कर्नेलियसका दूतहरूले ढोका ढक्ढक्याउँदा पत्रुसले बुझे — र गए। परदेशीको घरभित्र पस्नु उनको रीतिविरुद्ध थियो — तापनि उनी भित्र पसे।','Karneliyaskaa dutharule dhokaa dhakdhakyaaundaa Patrusle bujhe — ra gae. Pardeshiko gharbhitra pasnu unko ritiviruddha thiyo — taapani uni bhitra pase.','When Cornelius’s messengers knocked, Peter understood — and went. It was against all custom for him to enter a foreigner’s house — and he went in.','Acts 10:17–29'],
['पत्रुसले येशूको बारेमा बोल्दाबोल्दै पवित्र आत्मा सुन्ने सबैमाथि ओर्लनुभयो — ती परदेशीहरूमाथि, ठीक सुरुमा उनीहरूमाथि जस्तै।','Patrusle Yeshuko baaremaa boldaaboldai Pavitra Aatmaa sunne sabaimaathi orlanubhayo — ti pardeshiharumaathi, thik surumaa uniharumaathi jastai.','While Peter was still speaking about Jesus, the Holy Spirit fell on everyone listening — on the foreigners, exactly as on them at the beginning.','Acts 10:44–47'],
['पत्रुसले भने — अब म साँच्चै बुझ्दछु: परमेश्वरले पक्षपात गर्नुहुन्न, तर उहाँतिर फर्कने हरेक जातिका मानिसलाई स्वागत गर्नुहुन्छ।','Patrusle bhane — aba ma saanchai bujhdachhu: Parameshwarle pakshapaat garnuhunna, tara uhaantira pharkane harek jaatikaa maanislaai swaagat garnuhunchha.','Peter said: now I truly understand — God shows no favoritism, but welcomes people from every nation who turn to him.','Acts 10:34–35']]},
{id:'sent',t:'Sent out',ne:'पठाइएका',art:FNE_ART.sent,
note:['मण्डली भनेको पठाइएको जन हो। एन्टिओखियादेखि आजसम्म ढाँचा उही छ — प्रार्थना गर, पठाऊ, जाऊ, रोप — अनि घर चिठी लेख।','Mandali bhaneko pathaaieko jan ho. Entiokhiyaadekhi aajasamma dhaanchaa uhi chha — praarthanaa gara, pathaau, jaau, ropa — ani ghar chithi lekha.','The church is a sent people. From Antioch until now the pattern is the same: pray, send, go, plant — and write home.'],
paras:[
['एन्टिओखिया सहरमा — जहाँ विश्वासीहरूलाई पहिलो पटक ख्रीष्टियान भनियो — मण्डली प्रार्थना र उपवासमा थियो।','Entiokhiyaa saharmaa — jahaan vishwaasiharulaai pahilo patak Khristiyaan bhaniyo — mandali praarthanaa ra upawaasmaa thiyo.','In the city of Antioch — where believers were first called Christians — the church was praying and fasting.','Acts 11:26 · 13:1–2'],
['पवित्र आत्माले भन्नुभयो — बारनाबास र शाऊललाई मैले बोलाएको कामको लागि अलग गर। मण्डलीले उनीहरूमाथि हात राखेर पठाइदियो।','Pavitra Aatmaale bhannubhayo — Baarnaabaas ra Shaaullaai maile bolaaeko kaamko laagi alag gara. Mandalile uniharumaathi haat raakhera pathaaidiyo.','The Holy Spirit said: set apart for me Barnabas and Saul, for the work I have called them to. The church laid hands on them and sent them off.','Acts 13:2–3'],
['यसरी यात्राहरू सुरु भए — सहरपिच्छे उनीहरूले येशूको कथा सुनाए, र पछाडि विश्वासीहरूका नयाँ परिवारहरू छोडे।','Yasari yaatraaharu suru bhae — saharpichchhe uniharule Yeshuko kathaa sunaae, ra pachhaadi vishwaasiharukaa nayaan pariwaarharu chhode.','So began the journeys: city after city, they told the story of Jesus, and left behind new families of believers.','Acts 13–14'],
['हरेक बाटोमा कठिनाइ थियो — गिल्ला, ढुङ्गा, झ्यालखाना। पावलले पछि लेखे — परमेश्वरको राज्यमा पस्न हामी धेरै कष्टबाट भएर जानुपर्छ।','Harek baatomaa kathinaai thiyo — gillaa, dungaa, jhyaalkhaanaa. Paawalle pachhi lekhe — Parameshwarko raajyamaa pasna haami dherai kashtabaata bhaera jaanuparchha.','There was hardship on every road — mockery, stoning, prison. Paul later wrote: we must go through many troubles to enter God’s kingdom.','Acts 14:19–22'],
['ती नयाँ मण्डलीहरूको नजिक रहन पावलले चिठीहरू लेखे — येशूले यति भरिएका चिठीहरू, जुन हामी आज पनि बाइबलकै अंशको रूपमा पढ्छौं।','Ti nayaan mandaliharuko najik rahana Paawalle chithiharu lekhe — Yeshule yati bhariekaa chithiharu, jun haami aaja pani Baibalkai anshako rupmaa padhchhaun.','To stay close to the young churches, Paul wrote them letters — letters so full of Jesus that we still read them today, as part of the Bible itself.']]},
{id:'chains',t:'Chains cannot stop it',ne:'साङ्लाले रोक्न सक्दैन',art:FNE_ART.chains,
note:['प्रेरितको पुस्तक आधा पाइलामै टुङ्गिन्छ — सन्देशवाहकमाथि साङ्लो छ, सन्देशमाथि छैन। त्यसको अन्तिम दृश्य छैन, किनभने कथा सकिएकै थिएन।','Preritko pustak aadhaa paailaamai tunginchha — sandeshwaahakmaathi saanglo chha, sandeshmaathi chhaina. Tyasko antim drishya chhaina, kinabhane kathaa sakiekai thiena.','The book of Acts ends mid-stride — chains on the messenger, none on the message. It has no closing scene, because the story was not over.'],
paras:[
['फिलिप्पी सहरमा पावल र उनका साथी सिलासलाई लट्ठीले पिटियो र झ्यालखानाको सबैभन्दा भित्री कोठामा थुनियो — खुट्टा ठिँगुरामा कसेर।','Philippi saharmaa Paawal ra unkaa saathi Silaaslaai latthile pitiyo ra jhyaalkhaanaako sabaibhandaa bhitri kothaamaa thuniyo — khuttaa thinguraamaa kasera.','In the city of Philippi, Paul and his friend Silas were beaten with rods and locked in the innermost cell, their feet in stocks.','Acts 16:22–24'],
['मध्यरातमा उनीहरू प्रार्थना गर्दै र परमेश्वरको भजन गाउँदै थिए — र अरू कैदीहरू सुनिरहेका थिए।','Madhyaraatmaa uniharu praarthanaa gardai ra Parameshwarko bhajan gaaundai thie — ra aru kaidiharu sunirahekaa thie.','At midnight they were praying and singing to God — and the other prisoners were listening.','Acts 16:25'],
['अचानक भुइँचालोले झ्यालखाना हल्लायो; हरेक ढोका खुल्यो, हरेकको साङ्लो फुस्क्यो।','Achaanak bhuinchaalole jhyaalkhaanaa hallaayo; harek dhokaa khulyo, harekko saanglo phuskyo.','Suddenly an earthquake shook the prison; every door flew open, every chain came loose.','Acts 16:26'],
['आफ्नै ज्यान लिन लागेको जेलरले चिच्यायो — बाँच्नको लागि मैले के गर्नुपर्छ? प्रभु येशूमा विश्वास गर, उनीहरूले भने, र तिमी बाँच्नेछौ — तिमी र तिम्रो घराना। त्यही रात उसले उनीहरूका घाउ धोइदियो, र ऊ र उसको सारा परिवारले बप्तिस्मा लियो।','Aaphnai jyaan lina laageko jelarle chichyaayo — baanchnako laagi maile ke garnuparchha? Prabhu Yeshumaa vishwaas gara, uniharule bhane, ra timi baanchnechhau — timi ra timro gharaanaa. Tyahi raat usle uniharukaa ghaau dhoidiyo, ra u ra usko saaraa pariwaarle baptismaa liyo.','The jailer, about to take his own life, cried out: what must I do to be saved? Believe in the Lord Jesus, they answered, and you will be saved — you and your household. That night he washed their wounds, and he and his whole family were baptized.','Acts 16:27–34'],
['वर्षौंपछि पावल साम्राज्यको राजधानी रोम पुगे — कैदीको रूपमा। तापनि सिपाहीको पहरामा बसेको आफ्नै भाडाको घरबाट उनले सबैलाई स्वागत गरे र खुलमखुला, कुनै रोकावटविना, येशूको बारेमा बताइरहे।','Warshaunpachhi Paawal saamraajyako raajdhaani Rom puge — kaidiko rupmaa. Taapani sipaahiko paharaamaa baseko aaphnai bhaadaako gharbaata unle sabailaai swaagat gare ra khulamkhulaa, kunai rokaawatvinaa, Yeshuko baaremaa bataairahe.','Years later Paul reached Rome, the capital of the empire — as a prisoner. Yet from his own rented house, under guard, he welcomed everyone and told them about Jesus, openly and without hindrance.','Acts 28:16,30–31']]},
{id:'ends',t:'To the ends of the earth',ne:'पृथ्वीको छेउसम्म',art:FNE_ART.ends,
note:['तपाईंले यी कथाहरू यो भाषामा पढ्न सक्नुको कारण नै यही हो — कसैले ती यहाँसम्म बोकेर ल्यायो। त्यो दौड तपाईंसम्म आइपुगेको छ; निम्तो तपाईंकै हो।','Tapaainle yi kathaaharu yo bhaashaamaa padhna saknuko kaaran nai yahi ho — kasaile ti yahaansamma bokera lyaayo. Tyo daud tapaainsamma aaipugeko chha; nimto tapaainkai ho.','This is why you can read these stories in this language at all — someone carried them here. The relay has reached you; the invitation is yours.'],
paras:[
['तिमीहरू मेरा साक्षी हुनेछौ, येशूले भन्नुभएको थियो — पृथ्वीको अन्तिम छेउसम्म। र उनीहरू भए — अनि उनीहरूले बताएकाहरू पनि, अनि तिनीहरूपछिकाहरू पनि।','Timiharu meraa saakshi hunechhau, Yeshule bhannubhaeko thiyo — prithviko antim chheusamma. Ra uniharu bhae — ani uniharule bataaekaaharu pani, ani tiniharupachhikaaharu pani.','You will be my witnesses, Jesus had said — to the very ends of the earth. And they were — and so were the ones they told, and the ones after them.','Acts 1:8'],
['सन्देशले मरुभूमि, पहाड र समुद्रहरू पार गर्‍यो। त्यो भाषापछि भाषामा अनुवाद हुँदै गयो — किनभने परमेश्वर मातृभाषामा बोल्नुहुन्छ।','Sandeshle marubhumi, pahaad ra samudraharu paar garyo. Tyo bhaashaapachhi bhaashaamaa anuwaad hundai gayo — kinabhane Parameshwar maatribhaashaamaa bolnuhunchha.','The message crossed deserts and mountains and oceans. It was translated into language after language — because God speaks mother tongues.'],
['शताब्दीपछि शताब्दी साधारण साक्षीहरूले त्यो बोकिरहे — व्यापारी, आमा, शिक्षक, किसान — एक दिन त्यो नेपालसम्म नआइपुगुन्जेल।','Shataabdipachhi shataabdi saadhaaran saakshiharule tyo bokirahe — byaapaari, aamaa, shikshak, kisaan — ek din tyo Nepaalsamma naaipugunjel.','Century after century, ordinary witnesses carried it on — traders, mothers, teachers, farmers — until one day it reached Nepal too.'],
['आज नेपालका येशूका चेलाहरू भेला हुन्छन्, प्रार्थना गर्छन् र आफ्ना छिमेकीलाई प्रेम गर्छन् — त्यही माथिल्लो कोठामा सुरु भएको परिवारकै अंश।','Aaja Nepaalkaa Yeshukaa chelaaharu bhelaa hunchhan, praarthanaa garchhan ra aaphnaa chhimekilaai prem garchhan — tyahi maathillo kothaamaa suru bhaeko pariwaarkai ansha.','Today, followers of Jesus in Nepal gather, pray and love their neighbors — part of the same family that began in that upstairs room.'],
['यूहन्नालाई कथाको अन्त्य देखाइयो — गन्नै नसकिने भीड, हरेक जाति, कुल, वंश र भाषाबाट, परमेश्वरको सामु सँगै उभिएको। त्यो तस्बिरमा तपाईंकै जातिको कोही छ।','Yuhannaalaai kathaako antya dekhaaiyo — gannai nasakine bhid, harek jaati, kul, wansha ra bhaashaabaata, Parameshwarko saamu sangai ubhieko. Tyo tasbirmaa tapaainkai jaatiko kohi chha.','John was shown the end of the story: a crowd no one could count, from every nation, tribe, people and language, standing together before God. Someone from your people is in that picture.','Revelation 7:9'],
['प्रेरितको पुस्तक साँच्चै कहिल्यै सकिएन। उही आत्माले अझै भर्नुहुन्छ, उही येशूले अझै बोलाउनुहुन्छ, र उही कथा अझै लेखिँदैछ — सायद, अब, तपाईंमा।','Preritko pustak saanchai kahilyai sakiena. Uhi Aatmaale ajhai bharnuhunchha, uhi Yeshule ajhai bolaaunuhunchha, ra uhi kathaa ajhai lekhindaichha — saayad, aba, tapaainmaa.','The book of Acts never really ended. The same Spirit still fills, the same Jesus still calls, and the same story is still being written — perhaps, next, in you.']]}
]},

{id:'flives',kind:'collection',title:'People God Used',ne:'परमेश्वरले प्रयोग गर्नुभएका मानिसहरू',
overview:{t:'Ordinary people, faithful God',ne:'साधारण मानिस, विश्वासयोग्य परमेश्वर',art:FNE_ART.ovlives,
start:['यूसुफबाट सुरु गरौं','Eight lives, one faithful God'],
paras:[
['परमेश्वरको कथाले सारा यात्रा दस पाइलामा सुनायो — तर बाइबलका केही उत्कृष्ट जीवनहरूलाई हतारमा छोड्नुपर्‍यो। यो सङ्ग्रहले बिस्तारै, एक-एक गरेर तिनै कथाहरू सुनाउँछ।','Parameshwarko kathaale saaraa yaatraa das paailaamaa sunaayo — tara Baibalkaa kehi utkrishta jivanharulaai hataarmaa chhodnuparyo. Yo sangrahale bistaarai, ek-ek garera tinai kathaaharu sunaaunchha.','God’s Story told the whole sweep in ten steps — but it had to hurry past some of the best lives in the Bible. This collection slows down and tells them one by one.'],
['यी वीरहरूका कथा होइनन्। यी साधारण, कमजोरी भएका मानिसहरूका कथा हुन् — र तिनीहरूलाई प्रयोग गर्नुहुने विश्वासयोग्य परमेश्वरको कथा।','Yi virharukaa kathaa hoinan. Yi saadhaaran, kamjori bhaekaa maanisharukaa kathaa hun — ra tiniharulaai prayog garnuhune vishwaasyogya Parameshwarko kathaa.','These are not stories of heroes. They are stories of ordinary, flawed people — and of the faithful God who used them.'],
['धोका पाएको एक भाइ। एउटा गोठालो केटो। एक विदेशी विधवा। झ्यालमा प्रार्थना गर्ने एक निर्वासित। कोही पनि ठूला देखिँदैनथे — तर हरेकको ठूलो अर्थ थियो।','Dhokaa paaeko ek bhaai. Eutaa gothaalo keto. Ek videshi vidhawaa. Jhyaalmaa praarthanaa garne ek nirwaasit. Kohi pani thulaa dekhindainathe — tara harekko thulo artha thiyo.','A betrayed brother. A shepherd boy. A foreign widow. An exile praying at his window. None of them looked important — every one of them mattered.'],
['यहाँको हरेक कथा एकै बसाइमा पूरा हुन्छ। जुनसुकै क्रममा पढ्नुहोस् — हरेकले एउटै परमेश्वरको फरक-फरक पक्ष देखाउँछ।','Yahaanko harek kathaa ekai basaaimaa puraa hunchha. Junsukai kramamaa padhnuhos — harekle eutai Parameshwarko pharak-pharak paksha dekhaaunchha.','Each story here is complete in one sitting. Read them in any order — each one shows a different side of the same God.'],
['अनि यी सबैले अगाडितिर औंल्याउँछन्: हरेक उद्धार, हरेक क्षमा, हरेक विश्वासको पाइला — येशूमा आएको महान् उद्धारको सानो तस्बिर हो।','Ani yi sabaile agaaditira aunlyaaunchhan: harek uddhaar, harek kshamaa, harek vishwaasko paailaa — Yeshumaa aaeko mahaan uddhaarko saano tasbir ho.','And they all point forward: every rescue, every forgiveness, every faithful step is a small picture of the great rescue that came in Jesus.']
]},
sections:[
{id:'joseph',t:'Joseph — sold by his brothers',ne:'यूसुफ — दाजुहरूले बेचेका',art:FNE_ART.joseph,
note:['बीस वर्षका खाल्डा र झ्यालखानाहरू — एउटै पनि खेर गएन। परमेश्वरले त्यही समयभर उद्धार बुनिरहनुभएको थियो। अरूले हानिको निम्ति विचार गरेको कुरालाई परमेश्वरले भलाइको निम्ति प्रयोग गर्न सक्नुहुन्छ।','Bis warshakaa khaaldaa ra jhyaalkhaanaaharu — eutai pani kher gaena. Parameshwarle tyahi samayabhar uddhaar bunirahanubhaeko thiyo. Arule haaniko nimti vichaar gareko kuraalaai Parameshwarle bhalaaiko nimti prayog garna saknuhunchha.','Twenty years of pits and prisons, and not one wasted — God was weaving rescue the whole time. What others intend for harm, God can intend for good.'],
paras:[
['याकूबका बाह्र छोरा थिए, र तिनले यूसुफलाई सबैभन्दा धेरै माया गर्थे — तिनलाई एउटा राम्रो लबेदा नै बनाइदिए। दाजुहरूले त्यो देखे, र डाह बढ्दै घृणा बन्यो।','Yaakubkaa baahra chhoraa thie, ra tinle Yusuphlaai sabaibhandaa dherai maayaa garthe — tinlaai eutaa raamro labedaa nai banaaidie. Daajuharule tyo dekhe, ra daah badhdai ghrinaa banyo.','Jacob had twelve sons, and he loved Joseph the most — he even gave him a beautiful robe. His brothers saw it, and jealousy grew into hatred.','Genesis 37:3–4'],
['एक दिन, घरदेखि टाढा, दाजुहरूले यूसुफलाई समाते, सुक्खा खाल्डोमा फ्याँके, र बीस चाँदीका सिक्कामा व्यापारीहरूलाई बेचिदिए। तिनी सत्र वर्षका थिए।','Ek din, ghardekhi taadhaa, daajuharule Yusuphlaai samaate, sukkhaa khaaldomaa phyaanke, ra bis chaandikaa sikkaamaa byaapaariharulaai bechidie. Tini satra warshakaa thie.','One day, far from home, the brothers seized Joseph, threw him into a dry pit, and sold him to traders for twenty pieces of silver. He was seventeen.','Genesis 37:23–28'],
['मिश्रमा यूसुफ कमारा बने — तापनि परमप्रभु तिनीसँग हुनुहुन्थ्यो, र तिनका मालिकले समेत त्यो देखे। तर मालिककी पत्नीले तिनको बारेमा झूट बोलिन्, र निर्दोष यूसुफ झ्यालखानामा परे।','Mishramaa Yusuph kamaaraa bane — taapani Paramprabhu tinisanga hunuhunthyo, ra tinkaa maalikle samet tyo dekhe. Tara maalikki patnile tinko baaremaa jhut bolin, ra nirdosh Yusuph jhyaalkhaanaamaa pare.','In Egypt Joseph became a slave — yet the LORD was with him, and even his master saw it. Then the master’s wife lied about him, and he was thrown into prison, innocent.','Genesis 39'],
['पहिले खाल्डो, अनि झ्यालखाना — वर्षौंसम्म। तर कथाले चार पटक भन्छ: परमप्रभु यूसुफसँग हुनुहुन्थ्यो। परमेश्वरको साथ सधैं उद्धारजस्तो देखिँदैन।','Pahile khaaldo, ani jhyaalkhaanaa — warshaunsamma. Tara kathaale chaar patak bhanchha: Paramprabhu Yusuphsanga hunuhunthyo. Parameshwarko saath sadhain uddhaarjasto dekhindaina.','The pit, then prison — year after year. But the story says it four times: the LORD was with Joseph. God’s presence does not always look like rescue.','Genesis 39:21,23'],
['झ्यालखानामा यूसुफले सपनाहरूको अर्थ खोले — र वर्षौंपछि, स्वयं फारोले कसैले बुझाउन नसक्ने सपना देखे। यूसुफलाई कालकोठरीबाट ल्याइयो, र परमेश्वरले तिनलाई अर्थ दिनुभयो: सात वर्ष सहकाल, त्यसपछि सात वर्ष अनिकाल।','Jhyaalkhaanaamaa Yusuphle sapanaaharuko artha khole — ra warshaunpachhi, swayam Phaarole kasaile bujhaauna nasakne sapanaa dekhe. Yusuphlaai kaalkotharibaata lyaaiyo, ra Parameshwarle tinlaai artha dinubhayo: saat warsha sahakaal, tyaspachhi saat warsha anikaal.','In prison Joseph interpreted dreams — and years later, Pharaoh himself had a dream nobody could explain. Joseph was brought from the dungeon, and God gave him the meaning: seven years of plenty, then seven of famine.','Genesis 41'],
['एकै दिनमा यूसुफ कैदीबाट सारा मिश्रका शासक बने, फारोपछिका दोस्रो — भोकमरीमा परेको संसार बाँचोस् भनेर अन्न जम्मा गर्दै।','Ekai dinmaa Yusuph kaidibaata saaraa Mishrakaa shaasak bane, Phaaropachhikaa dosro — bhokmarimaa pareko sansaar baanchos bhanera anna jammaa gardai.','In one day Joseph rose from prisoner to ruler of all Egypt, second only to Pharaoh — storing grain so a starving world could live.','Genesis 41:39–43'],
['अनिकालले तिनका दाजुहरूलाई अन्न किन्न मिश्रसम्म पुर्‍यायो — र तिनीहरूले नचिनेका शासकको सामु शिर झुकाए। जब यूसुफले आखिरमा आफ्नो चिनारी दिए, तिनीहरू त्रसित भए। तर तिनी रोए, र भने: तिमीहरूले मेरो हानि गर्ने विचार गर्‍यौ, तर परमेश्वरले त्यसलाई भलाइको निम्ति विचार गर्नुभयो — धेरैका ज्यान बचाउनलाई। तिनले तिनीहरूलाई क्षमा गरे, र सारा परिवारलाई सुरक्षित ठाउँमा ल्याए।','Anikaalle tinkaa daajuharulaai anna kinna Mishrasamma puryaayo — ra tiniharule nachinekaa shaasakko saamu shir jhukaae. Jaba Yusuphle aakhirmaa aaphno chinaari die, tiniharu trasit bhae. Tara tini roe, ra bhane: timiharule mero haani garne vichaar garyau, tara Parameshwarle tyaslaai bhalaaiko nimti vichaar garnubhayo — dherakaa jyaan bachaaunlaai. Tinle tiniharulaai kshamaa gare, ra saaraa pariwaarlaai surakshit thaaunmaa lyaae.','The famine drove his brothers to Egypt to buy grain — and they bowed before the ruler they did not recognize. When Joseph finally revealed himself, they were terrified. But he wept, and said: you intended to harm me, but God intended it for good — to save many lives. He forgave them, and brought the whole family home to safety.','Genesis 45:4–8 · 50:20']
]},
{id:'moses',t:'Moses — the reluctant deliverer',ne:'मोशा — हिचकिचाउने उद्धारक',art:FNE_ART.moses,
note:['मोशाका हरेक बहानाको जवाफ एउटै थियो — म तँसँग हुनेछु। परमेश्वरले बोलाउनुहुँदा योग्यता होइन, उहाँकै उपस्थिति नै उत्तर हो।','Moshaakaa harek bahaanaako jawaaph eutai thiyo — ma tansanga hunechhu. Parameshwarle bolaaunuhundaa yogyataa hoina, uhaankai upasthiti nai uttar ho.','To every excuse Moses made, the answer was the same: I will be with you. When God calls, the answer is not our ability but his presence.'],
paras:[
['मिश्रमा इस्राएलीहरू कमारा थिए, र फारोले हरेक नवजात छोरालाई मार्ने हुकुम दिएका थिए। एउटी आमाले आफ्नो बालकलाई टोकरीमा राखेर नील नदीमा बगाइन् — र फारोकी छोरीले नै त्यो बालकलाई भेट्टाइन् र हुर्काइन्। उसको नाम मोशा रह्यो।','Mishramaa Israeliharu kamaaraa thie, ra Phaarole harek nawajaat chhoraalaai maarne hukum diekaa thie. Euti aamaale aaphno baalaklaai tokarimaa raakhera Nil nadimaa bagaain — ra Phaaroki chhorile nai tyo baalaklaai bhettaain ra hurkaain. Usko naam Moshaa rahyo.','In Egypt the Israelites were slaves, and Pharaoh had ordered every newborn son killed. One mother laid her baby in a basket on the Nile — and it was Pharaoh’s own daughter who found him and raised him. His name was Moses.','Exodus 1–2'],
['दरबारमा हुर्केका मोशा एक दिन आफ्नै जातिको रक्षा गर्न खोज्दा एक मिश्रीलाई मारे — र भागेर मरुभूमिमा गए। चालीस वर्षसम्म तिनी त्यहाँ गोठालो भएर बसे। राजकुमार अब कोही थिएनन्।','Darbaarmaa hurkekaa Moshaa ek din aaphnai jaatiko rakshaa garna khojdaa ek Mishrilaai maare — ra bhaagera marubhumimaa gae. Chaalis warshasamma tini tyahaan gothaalo bhaera base. Raajkumaar aba kohi thienan.','Raised in the palace, Moses one day killed an Egyptian while defending his own people — and fled to the desert. For forty years he lived there as a shepherd. The prince was nobody now.','Exodus 2:11–15'],
['त्यहीँ, बलिरहेको तर नजल्ने पोथ्राबाट, परमेश्वरले तिनलाई बोलाउनुभयो — मेरा जनको दुःख मैले देखेको छु। जा, तिनीहरूलाई निकालेर ल्या। मोशाले सोधे — म को हुँ र? परमेश्वरले जवाफ दिनुभयो — म तँसँग हुनेछु।','Tyahin, balirahiko tara najalne pothraabaata, Parameshwarle tinlaai bolaaunubhayo — meraa janko dukha maile dekheko chhu. Jaa, tiniharulaai nikaalera lyaa. Moshaale sodhe — ma ko hun ra? Parameshwarle jawaaph dinubhayo — ma tansanga hunechhu.','There, from a bush that burned but was not consumed, God called him: I have seen the suffering of my people. Go, and bring them out. Moses asked — who am I? God answered — I will be with you.','Exodus 3'],
['मोशाले बहाना बनाए — म बोल्नमा सिपालु छैन; अरू कसैलाई पठाउनुहोस्। तर परमेश्वरले भन्नुभयो — मुख कसले बनायो? म तेरो मुखसँग हुनेछु। परमेश्वरलाई वाक्पटु मानिस चाहिँदैन — तयार हुने मानिस चाहिन्छ।','Moshaale bahaanaa banaae — ma bolnamaa sipaalu chhaina; aru kasailaai pathaaunuhos. Tara Parameshwarle bhannubhayo — mukh kasle banaayo? Ma tero mukhsanga hunechhu. Parameshwarlaai waakpatu maanis chaahindaina — tayaar hune maanis chaahinchha.','Moses made excuses — I am not good with words; send someone else. But God said: who made the mouth? I will be with your mouth. God does not need eloquent people — he needs willing ones.','Exodus 4:10–13'],
['अनि त्यही हिचकिचाउने गोठालोले फारोको सामु उभिएर परमेश्वरका वचन बोले, आफ्ना जनलाई समुद्र पार गराए, र चालीस वर्षसम्म मरुभूमिमा तिनीहरूलाई डोर्‍याए — तिनीहरूका निम्ति परमेश्वरसँग अनुरोध गर्दै, तिनीहरूका गनगन सहँदै।','Ani tyahi hichkichaaune gothaalole Phaaroko saamu ubhiera Parameshwarkaa wachan bole, aaphnaa janlaai samudra paar garaae, ra chaalis warshasamma marubhumimaa tiniharulaai doryaae — tiniharukaa nimti Parameshwarsanga anurodh gardai, tiniharukaa gangan sahandai.','And that same hesitant shepherd stood before Pharaoh speaking God’s words, led his people through the sea, and guided them forty years in the wilderness — pleading with God for them, bearing their grumbling.','Exodus 14 · 32:11–14'],
['परमेश्वरले मोशासँग साथीसँग बोलेझैं आमनेसामने बोल्नुहुन्थ्यो। यात्राको अन्त्यमा तिनले नबो डाँडाबाट प्रतिज्ञाको देश हेरे — र परमेश्वरकै साथमा बिदा भए।','Parameshwarle Moshaasanga saathisanga bolejhaain aamnesaamne bolnuhunthyo. Yaatraako antyamaa tinle Nabo daandaabaata pratigyaako desh here — ra Parameshwarkai saathmaa bidaa bhae.','God would speak with Moses face to face, as a man speaks with his friend. At the journey’s end he looked over the promised land from Mount Nebo — and departed in God’s own presence.','Exodus 33:11 · Deuteronomy 34']]},
{id:'ruth',t:'Ruth — the outsider who stayed',ne:'रूथ — नछोड्ने विदेशी',art:FNE_ART.ruth,
note:['रूथसँग न देश थियो, न धन, न भविष्य — केवल अटल प्रेम थियो। त्यही सामान्य विश्वासयोग्यतालाई परमेश्वरले राजाहरूको र स्वयं येशूको वंश बनाउनुभयो।','Ruthsanga na desh thiyo, na dhan, na bhavishya — kewal atal prem thiyo. Tyahi saamaanya vishwaasyogyataalaai Parameshwarle raajaaharuko ra swayam Yeshuko wansha banaaunubhayo.','Ruth had no country, no money, no future — only stubborn love. And that ordinary faithfulness God wove into the line of kings, and of Jesus himself.'],
paras:[
['अनिकालका दिनमा नाओमी नाम गरेकी एक इस्राएली स्त्री परिवारसहित मोआब देशमा बसाइँ सरिन्। त्यहाँ उनका पति र दुवै छोरा मरे। उनीसँग रहे केवल दुई विदेशी बुहारीहरू।','Anikaalkaa dinmaa Naomi naam gareki ek Israeli stri pariwaarsahit Moab deshmaa basaain sarin. Tyahaan unkaa pati ra duwai chhoraa mare. Unisanga rahe kewal dui videshi buhaariharu.','In days of famine an Israelite woman named Naomi moved with her family to the land of Moab. There her husband and both her sons died. All she had left were two foreign daughters-in-law.','Ruth 1:1–5'],
['रित्तिएर घर फर्कंदा नाओमीले बुहारीहरूलाई भनिन् — आ-आफ्ना घर फर्केर जाओ। एउटी गइन्। तर रूथले नाओमीलाई समातेर भनिन् — तपाईं जहाँ जानुहुन्छ, म त्यहीँ जान्छु। तपाईंका जन मेरा जन हुनेछन्, तपाईंका परमेश्वर मेरा परमेश्वर।','Rittiera ghar pharkandaa Naomile buhaariharulaai bhanin — aa-aaphnaa ghar pharkera jaao. Euti gain. Tara Ruthle Naomilaai saamaatera bhanin — tapaain jahaan jaanuhunchha, ma tyahin jaanchhu. Tapaainkaa jan meraa jan hunechhan, tapaainkaa Parameshwar meraa Parameshwar.','Going home empty, Naomi told her daughters-in-law: return to your own homes. One went. But Ruth held on to Naomi and said: where you go, I will go. Your people will be my people, and your God my God.','Ruth 1:16–17'],
['बेथलेहेममा गरिब र विधवा भएर रूथले नाओमीलाई खुवाउन खेतमा छोडिएका अन्नका बाला बटुल्न थालिन् — दिनभरि, घामैभरि। उनको विश्वासयोग्यताको चर्चा सारा नगरमा फैलियो।','Bethlehemmaa garib ra vidhawaa bhaera Ruthle Naomilaai khuwaauna khetmaa chhodiekaa annakaa baalaa batulna thaalin — dinbhari, ghaamaibhari. Unko vishwaasyogyataako charchaa saaraa nagarmaa phailiyo.','In Bethlehem, poor and widowed, Ruth went gleaning leftover grain in the fields to feed Naomi — all day, under the sun. Word of her faithfulness spread through the whole town.','Ruth 2:2–12'],
['त्यो खेत बोअज नाम गरेका एक असल मानिसको थियो। तिनले रूथलाई भने — तिमीले आफ्नी सासूको निम्ति गरेका सबै कुरा मैले सुनेको छु। परमप्रभुले तिमीलाई पूरा इनाम दिऊन् — जसका पखेटामुनि तिमी शरण लिन आयौ।','Tyo khet Boaj naam garekaa ek asal maanisko thiyo. Tinle Ruthlaai bhane — timile aaphni saasuko nimti garekaa sabai kuraa maile suneko chhu. Paramprabhule timilaai puraa inaam diun — jaskaa pakhetaamuni timi sharan lina aayau.','The field belonged to a good man named Boaz. He told Ruth: I have heard all you have done for your mother-in-law. May the LORD reward you fully — under whose wings you have come to take refuge.','Ruth 2:11–12'],
['इस्राएलमा एउटा सुन्दर चलन थियो — हराएको परिवारलाई फिर्ता किन्ने नातेदार, अर्थात् उद्धार गर्ने नातेदार। बोअजले त्यही भूमिका लिए: तिनले रूथलाई विवाह गरे, र रित्तिएकी नाओमीको काखमा फेरि एक नाति खेल्न थाल्यो।','Israelmaa eutaa sundar chalan thiyo — haraaeko pariwaarlaai phirtaa kinne naatedaar, arthaat uddhaar garne naatedaar. Boajle tyahi bhumikaa lie: tinle Ruthlaai viwaaha gare, ra rittieki Naomiko kaakhmaa pheri ek naati khelna thaalyo.','Israel had a beautiful custom — a relative who buys back a ruined family, a redeeming kinsman. Boaz took that role: he married Ruth, and a grandson played again in empty-handed Naomi’s lap.','Ruth 4:9–17'],
['त्यो नातिको नाम ओबेद थियो — दाऊद राजाका हजुरबुबा। मोआबकी त्यो विदेशी विधवा येशूकै वंशावलीमा उभिइन्। परमेश्वरको परिवारमा बाहिरका मानिसका लागि सधैं ठाउँ थियो।','Tyo naatiko naam Obed thiyo — Daaud raajaakaa hajurbubaa. Moabki tyo videshi vidhawaa Yeshukai wanshaawalimaa ubhiin. Parameshwarko pariwaarmaa baahirakaa maaniskaa laagi sadhain thaaun thiyo.','That grandson was Obed — grandfather of King David. The foreign widow from Moab stands in the family line of Jesus himself. God’s family always had room for outsiders.','Ruth 4:17 · Matthew 1:5']]},
{id:'david',t:'David — a heart after God',ne:'दाऊद — परमेश्वरको मनको मानिस',art:FNE_ART.david,
note:['परमेश्वरको मनको मानिस भनेको पापै नगर्ने मानिस होइन — पाप देखाइदिँदा नुहेर फर्कने मानिस हो। दाऊदको महानता तिनको वीरता होइन, तिनको पश्चात्ताप थियो।','Parameshwarko manko maanis bhaneko paapai nagarne maanis hoina — paap dekhaaidindaa nuhera pharkane maanis ho. Daaudko mahaantaa tinko virtaa hoina, tinko pashchaattaap thiyo.','A man after God’s heart is not a man who never sins — it is a man who bows and turns when his sin is shown to him. David’s greatness was not his courage but his repentance.'],
paras:[
['परमेश्वरले शमूएल अगमवक्तालाई नयाँ राजा अभिषेक गर्न यिशैको घरमा पठाउनुभयो। सात जना छोराहरू अगाडि आए — तर परमेश्वरले भन्नुभयो — मानिसले बाहिरी रूप हेर्छ, परमप्रभुले हृदय हेर्नुहुन्छ। अन्तिममा बोलाइए कान्छा — भेडा चराइरहेका दाऊद।','Parameshwarle Shamuel agamwaktaalaai nayaan raajaa abhishek garna Yishaiko gharmaa pathaaunubhayo. Saat janaa chhoraaharu agaadi aae — tara Parameshwarle bhannubhayo — maanisle baahiri rup herchha, Paramprabhule hridaya hernuhunchha. Antimmaa bolaaie kaanchhaa — bhedaa charaairahekaa Daaud.','God sent the prophet Samuel to Jesse’s house to anoint a new king. Seven sons passed by — but God said: people look at the outside; the LORD looks at the heart. Last of all they called the youngest — David, out keeping the sheep.','1 Samuel 16:6–13'],
['गोठालो केटो हुँदा नै दाऊदले ठूला कुरा सिकिसकेका थिए — सिंह र भालुबाट बगाल जोगाउँदा तिनले जानेका थिए: बचाउनुहुने परमप्रभु नै हुनुहुन्छ। त्यसैले गोल्यत नामको ऐरावतका सामु पनि तिनी डराएनन्।','Gothaalo keto hundaa nai Daaudle thulaa kuraa sikisakekaa thie — sinha ra bhaalubaata bagaal jogaaundaa tinle jaanekaa thie: bachaaunuhune Paramprabhu nai hunuhunchha. Tyasaile Golyat naamko airaawatkaa saamu pani tini daraaenan.','As a shepherd boy David had already learned the great lesson — protecting the flock from lion and bear, he knew: it is the LORD who saves. So even before the giant named Goliath, he was not afraid.','1 Samuel 17:34–37'],
['राजा भएपछि दाऊदले परमेश्वरको सन्दुक यरूशलेम ल्याए — र सारा शक्ति लगाएर परमप्रभुको सामु नाचे। तिनले भजनहरू लेखे जुन आज पनि संसारभरि गाइन्छन् — परमप्रभु मेरा गोठाला हुनुहुन्छ।','Raajaa bhaepachhi Daaudle Parameshwarko sanduk Yarushalem lyaae — ra saaraa shakti lagaaera Paramprabhuko saamu naache. Tinle bhajanharu lekhe jun aaja pani sansaarbhari gaainchhan — Paramprabhu meraa gothaalaa hunuhunchha.','As king, David brought God’s ark to Jerusalem — and danced before the LORD with all his might. He wrote songs still sung around the world today: the LORD is my shepherd.','2 Samuel 6:14 · Psalm 23'],
['तर दाऊद ठूलो पापमा पनि फसे — अर्काकी पत्नी बतशेबालाई लिए, र त्यो लुकाउन उनका पति मारिने बन्दोबस्त गरे। परमेश्वरले नातान अगमवक्तालाई पठाउनुभयो, र नातानले राजाकै सामु भने — त्यो मानिस तपाईं नै हुनुहुन्छ।','Tara Daaud thulo paapmaa pani phase — arkaaki patni Batshebaalaai lie, ra tyo lukaauna unkaa pati maarine bandobasta gare. Parameshwarle Naataan agamwaktaalaai pathaaunubhayo, ra Naataanle raajaakai saamu bhane — tyo maanis tapaain nai hunuhunchha.','But David also fell into great sin — he took another man’s wife, Bathsheba, and arranged her husband’s death to hide it. God sent the prophet Nathan, who said to the king’s face: you are the man.','2 Samuel 11–12:7'],
['दाऊद रिसाएनन्, बहाना बनाएनन्। तिनले भने — मैले परमप्रभुको विरुद्धमा पाप गरेको छु। तिनले लेखे — हे परमेश्वर, ममा शुद्ध हृदय सृजनुहोस्। परमेश्वरले क्षमा गर्नुभयो — तर पापका पीडादायी फलहरू परिवारमा वर्षौंसम्म रहे।','Daaud risaaenan, bahaanaa banaaenan. Tinle bhane — maile Paramprabhuko biruddhamaa paap gareko chhu. Tinle lekhe — he Parameshwar, mamaa shuddha hridaya srijanuhos. Parameshwarle kshamaa garnubhayo — tara paapkaa pidaadaayi phalharu pariwaarmaa warshaunsamma rahe.','David did not rage or make excuses. He said: I have sinned against the LORD. He wrote: create in me a clean heart, O God. God forgave him — yet the painful fruit of that sin stayed in his family for years.','2 Samuel 12:13 · Psalm 51'],
['परमेश्वरले दाऊदलाई एउटा प्रतिज्ञा दिनुभयो — तेरो वंशबाट एक राजा आउनुहुनेछ जसको राज्य कहिल्यै टुङ्गिनेछैन। सहस्र वर्षपछि, दाऊदकै सहर बेथलेहेममा, त्यो राजा जन्मनुभयो।','Parameshwarle Daaudlaai eutaa pratigyaa dinubhayo — tero wanshabaata ek raajaa aaunuhunechha jasko raajya kahilyai tunginechhaina. Sahasra warshapachhi, Daaudkai sahar Bethlehemmaa, tyo raajaa janmanubhayo.','And God gave David a promise: from your line will come a King whose kingdom will never end. A thousand years later, in David’s own town of Bethlehem, that King was born.','2 Samuel 7:12–16 · Luke 2:4']]},
{id:'elijah',t:'Elijah — fire and a whisper',ne:'एलिया — आगो र मधुर आवाज',art:FNE_ART.elijah,
note:['आगो झार्ने परमेश्वरले नै थाकेको सेवकलाई रोटी र निद्रा दिनुहुन्छ, र आँधीमा होइन, मधुर आवाजमा बोल्नुहुन्छ। जलेर थाकेकाहरूप्रति परमेश्वर कोमल हुनुहुन्छ।','Aago jhaarne Parameshwarle nai thaakeko sewaklaai roti ra nidraa dinuhunchha, ra aandhimaa hoina, madhur aawaajmaa bolnuhunchha. Jalera thaakekaaharuprati Parameshwar komal hunuhunchha.','The same God who sends fire gives his worn-out servant bread and sleep, and speaks not in the storm but in a whisper. God is gentle with the burned out.'],
paras:[
['इस्राएलका राजा र रानीले जनतालाई बाल नामको मूर्ति पुज्न डोर्‍याएका थिए। तब एलिया अगमवक्ता राजाको सामु उभिएर बोले — मैले सेवा गर्ने परमप्रभु जीवित हुनुभएझैं, यी वर्षहरूमा मेरो वचनविना पानी पर्नेछैन।','Israelkaa raajaa ra raanile janataalaai Baal naamko murti pujna doryaaekaa thie. Taba Eliyaa agamwaktaa raajaako saamu ubhiera bole — maile sewaa garne Paramprabhu jivit hunubhaejhaain, yi warshaharumaa mero wachanvinaa paani parnechhaina.','Israel’s king and queen were leading the people to worship an idol called Baal. Then the prophet Elijah stood before the king and said: as surely as the LORD I serve lives, there will be no rain these years except at my word.','1 Kings 17:1'],
['अनिकालका ती वर्षहरूमा परमेश्वरले एलियालाई अनौठा तरिकाले पालनुभयो — खोलाको पानी, र बिहान-बेलुका रोटी ल्याइदिने कागहरू। पछि एक गरिब विधवाको पीठो र तेल कहिल्यै सकिएन।','Anikaalkaa ti warshaharumaa Parameshwarle Eliyaalaai anauthaa tarikaale paalnubhayo — kholaako paani, ra bihaan-belukaa roti lyaaidine kaagharu. Pachhi ek garib vidhawaako pitho ra tel kahilyai sakiena.','Through those famine years God kept Elijah in strange ways — a brook for water, and ravens bringing bread morning and evening. Later, a poor widow’s flour and oil that never ran out.','1 Kings 17:2–16'],
['अनि कर्मेल डाँडामा ठूलो सामना भयो — एकातिर बालका साढे चार सय अगमवक्ता, अर्कोतिर एक्लै एलिया। जुन परमेश्वरले आगोद्वारा जवाफ दिनुहुन्छ, उहाँ नै परमेश्वर हुनुहुन्छ। बालको वेदी चुपचाप रह्यो — तर परमप्रभुको आगो आकाशबाट झर्‍यो, र सारा जनताले घोप्टो परेर भने: परमप्रभु नै परमेश्वर हुनुहुन्छ!','Ani Karmel daandaamaa thulo saamanaa bhayo — ekaatira Baalkaa saadhe chaar saya agamwaktaa, arkotira eklai Eliyaa. Jun Parameshwarle aagodwaaraa jawaaph dinuhunchha, uhaan nai Parameshwar hunuhunchha. Baalko wedi chupchaap rahyo — tara Paramprabhuko aago aakaashbaata jharyo, ra saaraa janataale ghopto parera bhane: Paramprabhu nai Parameshwar hunuhunchha!','Then came the great showdown on Mount Carmel — four hundred fifty prophets of Baal on one side, Elijah alone on the other. The God who answers by fire, he is God. Baal’s altar stayed silent — but the fire of the LORD fell from heaven, and all the people fell on their faces: the LORD, he is God!','1 Kings 18:20–39'],
['तर भोलिपल्टै रानीको धम्कीले एलिया प्राण जोगाउन भागे। मरुभूमिमा एक बोटमुनि बसेर तिनले प्रार्थना गरे — पुग्यो, हे परमप्रभु, मेरो प्राण लिनुहोस्। विजयको भोलिपल्ट परमेश्वरका सेवक पनि यति थाकेका हुन सक्छन्।','Tara bholipaltai raaniko dhamkile Eliyaa praan jogaauna bhaage. Marubhumimaa ek botmuni basera tinle praarthanaa gare — pugyo, he Paramprabhu, mero praan linuhos. Vijayako bholipalta Parameshwarkaa sewak pani yati thaakekaa huna sakchhan.','Yet the very next day, at the queen’s threat, Elijah ran for his life. In the desert he sat under a bush and prayed: it is enough, LORD — take my life. Even God’s servants can be that exhausted the day after a victory.','1 Kings 19:1–4'],
['परमेश्वरले तिनलाई हप्काउनुभएन। उहाँले तिनलाई सुत्न दिनुभयो, र स्वर्गदूतद्वारा दुई पटक तातो रोटी खुवाउनुभयो — उठेर खा; बाटो तँलाई ज्यादै लामो छ। पहिले आराम र भोजन, अनि मात्र अर्ती।','Parameshwarle tinlaai hapkaaunubhaena. Uhaanle tinlaai sutna dinubhayo, ra swargadutdwaaraa dui patak taato roti khuwaaunubhayo — uthera khaa; baato tanlaai jyaadai laamo chha. Pahile aaraam ra bhojan, ani maatra arti.','God did not scold him. He let him sleep, and twice fed him warm bread by an angel — get up and eat; the journey is too much for you. First rest and food; only then a word.','1 Kings 19:5–8'],
['अनि होरेब डाँडामा ठूलो आँधी आयो, भूकम्प आयो, आगो आयो — तर परमप्रभु तीमा हुनुहुन्नथ्यो। त्यसपछि आयो एउटा शान्त, मधुर आवाज। परमेश्वरले एलियालाई नयाँ काम, एक सहयोगी, र एउटा भेद दिनुभयो — बालको सामु घुँडा नटेकेका सात हजार अझै छन्। तँ कहिल्यै एक्लो थिइनस्।','Ani Horeb daandaamaa thulo aandhi aayo, bhukampa aayo, aago aayo — tara Paramprabhu timaa hunuhunnathyo. Tyaspachhi aayo eutaa shaanta, madhur aawaaj. Parameshwarle Eliyaalaai nayaan kaam, ek sahayogi, ra eutaa bhed dinubhayo — Baalko saamu ghundaa natekekaa saat hajaar ajhai chhan. Tan kahilyai eklo thiinas.','Then on Mount Horeb came a great wind, an earthquake, a fire — but the LORD was not in them. After them came a still, gentle whisper. God gave Elijah new work, a companion, and a secret: seven thousand have never bowed to Baal. You were never alone.','1 Kings 19:11–18']]},
{id:'daniel',t:'Daniel — faithful in exile',ne:'दानिएल — निर्वासनमा विश्वासयोग्य',art:FNE_ART.daniel,
note:['दानिएलको रहस्य सङ्कटको घडीमा थिएन — खुला झ्यालको दैनिक बानीमा थियो। सिंहको खोरको साहस दिनहुँको प्रार्थनाबाट बन्छ।','Daanielko rahasya sankatko gharimaa thiena — khulaa jhyaalko dainik baanimaa thiyo. Sinhako khorko saahas dinhunko praarthanaabaata banchha.','Daniel’s secret was not found in the moment of crisis — it was built at the open window, day by day. Lions’-den courage is made of daily prayer.'],
paras:[
['यरूशलेम ढल्दा बाबेलले उत्कृष्ट जवानहरूलाई कैद गरेर लग्यो — तिनीहरूमध्ये एक थिए दानिएल। नयाँ नाम, नयाँ भाषा, राजाको भोजन — सबैले तिनलाई बाबेलकै बनाउन खोज्यो। तर दानिएलले आफ्नो हृदयमा अठोट गरे: म आफूलाई बिटुलो पार्नेछैनँ।','Yarushalem dhaldaa Baabelle utkrishta jawaanharulaai kaid garera lagyo — tiniharumadhye ek thie Daaniel. Nayaan naam, nayaan bhaashaa, raajaako bhojan — sabaile tinlaai Baabelkai banaauna khojyo. Tara Daanielle aaphno hridayamaa athot gare: ma aaphulaai bitulo paarnechhainan.','When Jerusalem fell, Babylon carried off its best young men — among them Daniel. New name, new language, the king’s food — everything was designed to make him Babylonian. But Daniel resolved in his heart: I will not defile myself.','Daniel 1:3–8'],
['तिनी विद्रोही भएनन् — उत्कृष्ट भए। हरेक काममा राजाका सबै सल्लाहकारभन्दा दस गुणा सक्षम। परमेश्वरले तिनलाई सपना र दर्शनको अर्थ खोल्ने बुद्धि दिनुभयो, र दानिएल विदेशी दरबारमै उच्च पदमा पुगे।','Tini vidrohi bhaenan — utkrishta bhae. Harek kaammaa raajaakaa sabai sallaahkaarbhandaa das gunaa saksham. Parameshwarle tinlaai sapanaa ra darshanko artha kholne buddhi dinubhayo, ra Daaniel videshi darbaarmai uchcha padmaa puge.','He did not rebel — he excelled. In every matter he proved ten times better than all the king’s advisers. God gave him wisdom to interpret dreams and visions, and Daniel rose high in a foreign court.','Daniel 1:17–20'],
['तिनका तीन साथीलाई राजाको सुनको मूर्तिलाई ढोग्न आदेश भयो — नत्र दन्किरहेको भट्टी। तिनीहरूले जवाफ दिए — हाम्रा परमेश्वरले हामीलाई बचाउन सक्नुहुन्छ। तर बचाउनुभएन भने पनि, हामी तपाईंको मूर्तिलाई ढोग्नेछैनौं। भट्टीभित्र चौथो आकृति हिँडिरहेको देखियो — र तिनीहरू एक रौं पनि नखहरिई निस्के।','Tinkaa tin saathilaai raajaako sunko murtilaai dhogna aadesh bhayo — natra dankiraheko bhatti. Tiniharule jawaaph die — haamraa Parameshwarle haamilaai bachaauna saknuhunchha. Tara bachaaunubhaena bhane pani, haami tapaainko murtilaai dhognechhainaun. Bhattibhitra chautho aakriti hindiraheko dekhiyo — ra tiniharu ek raun pani nakhahari-i niske.','His three friends were ordered to bow to the king’s golden statue — or face the blazing furnace. They answered: our God is able to save us. But even if he does not, we will not bow. Inside the furnace a fourth figure was seen walking — and they came out without even a singed hair.','Daniel 3:16–27'],
['वर्षौंपछि, ईर्ष्यालु अधिकारीहरूले नयाँ कानुन बनाए — तीस दिनसम्म राजाबाहेक कसैसँग प्रार्थना गर्ने जो कोही सिंहको खोरमा फालिनेछ। दानिएलले के गरे? सधैंझैं गरे — दिनको तीन पटक, यरूशलेमतिर फर्केको झ्याल खोलेर, घुँडा टेकी परमेश्वरलाई धन्यवाद दिए।','Warshaunpachhi, irshyaalu adhikaariharule nayaan kaanun banaae — tis dinsamma raajaabaahek kasaisanga praarthanaa garne jo kohi sinhako khormaa phaalinechha. Daanielle ke gare? Sadhainjhaain gare — dinko tin patak, Yarushalemtira pharkeko jhyaal kholera, ghundaa teki Parameshwarlaai dhanyawaad die.','Years later, jealous officials crafted a new law: for thirty days, anyone praying to anyone but the king would be thrown to the lions. What did Daniel do? What he had always done — three times a day, at his window open toward Jerusalem, he knelt and gave thanks to God.','Daniel 6:6–10'],
['राजाले निकै चाहेर पनि आफ्नै कानुन उल्टाउन सकेनन्, र दानिएल सिंहको खोरमा फालिए। बिहान सबेरै राजा दौडेर आए र कराए — के तिम्रा परमेश्वरले तिमीलाई बचाउन सक्नुभयो? खोरबाट आवाज आयो — मेरा परमेश्वरले आफ्ना दूत पठाएर सिंहका मुख थुनिदिनुभयो।','Raajaale nikai chaahera pani aaphnai kaanun ultaauna sakenan, ra Daaniel sinhako khormaa phaalie. Bihaan saberai raajaa daudera aae ra karaae — ke timraa Parameshwarle timilaai bachaauna saknubhayo? Khorbaata aawaaj aayo — meraa Parameshwarle aaphnaa dut pathaaera sinhakaa mukh thunidinubhayo.','The king, though he badly wanted to, could not undo his own law, and Daniel was thrown to the lions. At first light the king ran to the den and cried: has your God been able to save you? A voice rose from the den: my God sent his angel and shut the lions’ mouths.','Daniel 6:16–22'],
['दानिएल बुढेसकालसम्म विदेशी सम्राटहरूको सेवामा रहे — तर घुँडा भने सधैं एउटै परमेश्वरका अगाडि मात्र टेके। मन्दिरविनाको देशमा तिनको शान्त, दैनिक विश्वासयोग्यताले सम्राटहरूलाई नै भन्न लगायो — दानिएलका परमेश्वर नै जीवित परमेश्वर हुनुहुन्छ।','Daaniel budheskaalsamma videshi samraatharuko sewaamaa rahe — tara ghundaa bhane sadhain eutai Parameshwarkaa agaadi maatra teke. Mandirvinaako deshmaa tinko shaanta, dainik vishwaasyogyataale samraatharulaai nai bhanna lagaayo — Daanielkaa Parameshwar nai jivit Parameshwar hunuhunchha.','Daniel served foreign emperors into old age — but his knees bowed to one God only. In a land without a temple, his quiet daily faithfulness made emperors themselves declare: the God of Daniel is the living God.','Daniel 6:25–27']]},
{id:'jonah',t:'Jonah — the runaway prophet',ne:'योना — भाग्ने अगमवक्ता',art:FNE_ART.jonah,
note:['योनाको पुस्तक अगमवक्ताको सफलतामा होइन, परमेश्वरको प्रश्नमा टुङ्गिन्छ — किनभने त्यो प्रश्न हामीतिर फर्केको छ: के हाम्रो दया पनि परमेश्वरको जति फराकिलो छ?','Yonaako pustak agamwaktaako saphaltaamaa hoina, Parameshwarko prashnamaa tunginchha — kinabhane tyo prashna haamitira pharkeko chha: ke haamro dayaa pani Parameshwarko jati pharaakilo chha?','The book of Jonah ends not with the prophet’s success but with God’s question — because the question turns toward us: is our mercy as wide as God’s?'],
paras:[
['परमेश्वरले योना अगमवक्तालाई भन्नुभयो — निनवे जा, त्यो ठूलो सहरका मानिसहरूलाई चेतावनी दे। तर निनवे त इस्राएलका निर्दयी शत्रुहरूको राजधानी थियो। योना उठे — र ठीक उल्टो दिशाको जहाज चढे।','Parameshwarle Yonaa agamwaktaalaai bhannubhayo — Ninawe jaa, tyo thulo saharkaa maanisharulaai chetaawani de. Tara Ninawe ta Israelkaa nirdayi shatruharuko raajdhaani thiyo. Yonaa uthe — ra thik ulto dishaako jahaaj chadhe.','God told the prophet Jonah: go to Nineveh, that great city, and warn its people. But Nineveh was the capital of Israel’s cruelest enemies. Jonah got up — and boarded a ship going in exactly the opposite direction.','Jonah 1:1–3'],
['समुद्रमा यस्तो आँधी उठ्यो कि जहाज नै टुक्रिन लाग्यो। योनाले नाविकहरूलाई भने — दोष मेरो हो; मलाई समुद्रमा फालिदेओ। तिनीहरूले फाले — र समुद्र शान्त भयो। अनि परमप्रभुले एउटा ठूलो माछा पठाउनुभयो, जसले योनालाई निल्यो।','Samudramaa yasto aandhi uthyo ki jahaaj nai tukrina laagyo. Yonaale naawikharulaai bhane — dosh mero ho; malaai samudramaa phaalideo. Tiniharule phaale — ra samudra shaanta bhayo. Ani Paramprabhule eutaa thulo maachhaa pathaaunubhayo, jasle Yonaalaai nilyo.','At sea a storm rose so fierce the ship began to break apart. Jonah told the sailors: the fault is mine — throw me into the sea. They did — and the sea grew calm. And the LORD sent a great fish, which swallowed Jonah.','Jonah 1:4–17'],
['माछाको पेटभित्र, समुद्रको गहिराइबाट, योनाले प्रार्थना गरे — मैले पुकारेँ, र तपाईंले सुन्नुभयो। उद्धार परमप्रभुबाट नै आउँछ। तीन दिनपछि माछाले योनालाई सुक्खा जमिनमा उगेलिदियो।','Maachhaako petbhitra, samudrako gahiraaibaata, Yonaale praarthanaa gare — maile pukaaren, ra tapaainle sunnubhayo. Uddhaar Paramprabhubaata nai aaunchha. Tin dinpachhi maachhaale Yonaalaai sukkhaa jaminmaa ugelidiyo.','Inside the fish, from the depths of the sea, Jonah prayed: I called, and you heard me. Salvation comes from the LORD. After three days the fish spat Jonah out onto dry land.','Jonah 2'],
['अनि परमप्रभुको वचन योनाकहाँ दोस्रो पटक आयो — निनवे जा। यसपालि तिनी गए। तिनको छोटो चेतावनी सुनेर त्यो विशाल सहर — राजादेखि सर्वसाधारणसम्म — पापबाट फर्कियो। र परमेश्वरले तिनीहरूलाई नाश गर्नुभएन।','Ani Paramprabhuko wachan Yonaakahaan dosro patak aayo — Ninawe jaa. Yaspaali tini gae. Tinko chhoto chetaawani sunera tyo vishaal sahar — raajaadekhi sarwasaadhaaransamma — paapbaata pharkiyo. Ra Parameshwarle tiniharulaai naash garnubhaena.','Then the word of the LORD came to Jonah a second time: go to Nineveh. This time he went. At his short warning that vast city — from the king to the least — turned from its sin. And God did not destroy them.','Jonah 3'],
['तर योना खुसी भएनन् — रिसाए। मलाई थाहा थियो, तिनले परमेश्वरलाई भने — तपाईं अनुग्रही र दयालु हुनुहुन्छ भनेर! त्यसैले त म भागेको थिएँ। तिनी सहरबाहिर बसेर हेर्न थाले — सायद अझै आगो बर्सिन्छ कि।','Tara Yonaa khusi bhaenan — risaae. Malaai thaahaa thiyo, tinle Parameshwarlaai bhane — tapaain anugrahi ra dayaalu hunuhunchha bhanera! Tyasaile ta ma bhaageko thien. Tini saharbaahira basera herna thaale — saayad ajhai aago barsinchha ki.','But Jonah was not glad — he was furious. I knew it, he told God — I knew you are gracious and merciful! That is exactly why I ran. He sat down outside the city and watched — in case fire might still fall.','Jonah 4:1–5'],
['परमेश्वरले एउटा बोट उमारेर योनालाई छहारी दिनुभयो — योना खुसी भए। भोलिपल्ट बोट ओइलायो — योना फेरि मर्न चाहने गरी रिसाए। तब परमेश्वरले सोध्नुभयो — एउटा बोटको निम्ति तँलाई यति माया लाग्छ भने, के मलाई त्यो ठूलो सहरको माया नलागोस् — जहाँ एक लाख बीस हजारभन्दा बढी मानिस छन्? पुस्तक त्यही प्रश्नमा टुङ्गिन्छ।','Parameshwarle eutaa bot umaarera Yonaalaai chhahaari dinubhayo — Yonaa khusi bhae. Bholipalta bot oilaayo — Yonaa pheri marna chaahane gari risaae. Taba Parameshwarle sodhnubhayo — eutaa botko nimti tanlaai yati maayaa laagchha bhane, ke malaai tyo thulo saharko maayaa nalaagos — jahaan ek laakh bis hajaarbhandaa badhi maanis chhan? Pustak tyahi prashnamaa tunginchha.','God grew a plant to shade Jonah — and Jonah was glad. Next day the plant withered — and Jonah was angry enough to die again. Then God asked: you care this much about one plant — should I not care about that great city, with more than a hundred and twenty thousand people in it? The book ends on that question.','Jonah 4:6–11']]},
{id:'esther',t:'Esther — for such a time as this',ne:'एस्तर — यस्तै समयको लागि',art:FNE_ART.esther,
note:['एस्तरको साहस एक वाक्यमा अटाउँछ — मरे मरुँला। परमेश्वरले तपाईंलाई जुन ठाउँमा राख्नुभएको छ, सायद त्यो पनि यस्तै समयको निम्ति हो।','Estarko saahas ek waakyamaa ataaunchha — mare marunlaa. Parameshwarle tapaainlaai jun thaaunmaa raakhnubhaeko chha, saayad tyo pani yastai samayako nimti ho.','Esther’s courage fits in one sentence: if I perish, I perish. And the place where God has put you — perhaps that too is for such a time as this.'],
paras:[
['निर्वासनमा छरिएका यहूदीहरूमध्ये फारसी साम्राज्यमा एक अनाथ केटी थिइन् — एस्तर, जसलाई तिनका दाजुका छोरा पर्ने नातेदार मोर्दकैले छोरीझैं हुर्काएका थिए। अनौठो घटनाक्रमबाट एस्तर त्यही साम्राज्यकी रानी बनिन् — आफू यहूदी हुँ भन्ने कुरा कसैलाई नभनीकन।','Nirwaasanmaa chhariekaa Yahudiharumadhye Phaarasi saamraajyamaa ek anaath keti thiin — Estar, jaslaai tinkaa daajukaa chhoraa parne naatedaar Mordakaile chhorijhaain hurkaaekaa thie. Anautho ghatanaakrambaata Estar tyahi saamraajyaki raani banin — aaphu Yahudi hun bhanne kuraa kasailaai nabhanikana.','Among the Jews scattered in exile lived an orphan girl in the Persian empire — Esther, raised like a daughter by her relative Mordecai. Through a strange turn of events Esther became queen of that very empire — telling no one she was a Jew.','Esther 2:5–17'],
['दरबारका शक्तिशाली अधिकारी हामानले मोर्दकैसँगको रिसमा साम्राज्यभरिका सबै यहूदीलाई एकै दिनमा नाश गर्ने राजकीय आदेश जारी गराए। मिति तोकियो। जाति नै मेटिने भयो।','Darbaarkaa shaktishaali adhikaari Haamaanle Mordakaisangako rismaa saamraajyabharikaa sabai Yahudilaai ekai dinmaa naash garne raajkiya aadesh jaari garaae. Miti tokiyo. Jaati nai metine bhayo.','Haman, a powerful court official, in his rage against Mordecai obtained a royal decree to destroy all the Jews of the empire in a single day. The date was set. A whole people faced erasure.','Esther 3:8–13'],
['मोर्दकैले एस्तरलाई खबर पठाए — राजाको सामु गएर आफ्ना जनका लागि बिन्ती गर। तर नबोलाई राजाको सामु जानेलाई मृत्युदण्ड हुन्थ्यो। मोर्दकैले थपे — को जान्दछ, सायद यस्तै समयको निम्ति पो तिमी दरबारमा पुगेकी छ्यौ कि?','Mordakaile Estarlaai khabar pathaae — raajaako saamu gaera aaphnaa jankaa laagi binti gara. Tara nabolaai raajaako saamu jaanelaai mrityudanda hunthyo. Mordakaile thape — ko jaandachha, saayad yastai samayako nimti po timi darbaarmaa pugeki chhyau ki?','Mordecai sent word to Esther: go before the king and plead for your people. But to approach the king unsummoned meant death. Mordecai added: who knows — perhaps you have come to the palace for such a time as this?','Esther 4:8–14'],
['एस्तरले जवाफ फर्काइन् — तीन दिनसम्म मेरो निम्ति उपवास बस। अनि म राजाकहाँ जानेछु, जुन नियमविरुद्ध छ — र मरे मरुँला। डर नभएर होइन — डरभन्दा ठूलो कुराको निम्ति तिनी अघि बढिन्।','Estarle jawaaph pharkaain — tin dinsamma mero nimti upawaas basa. Ani ma raajaakahaan jaanechhu, jun niyamviruddha chha — ra mare marunlaa. Dar nabhaera hoina — darbhandaa thulo kuraako nimti tini aghi badhin.','Esther sent back her answer: fast for me three days. Then I will go to the king, though it is against the law — and if I perish, I perish. Not because she felt no fear — she moved forward for something bigger than fear.','Esther 4:15–16'],
['राजाले एस्तरलाई ग्रहण गरे। दुई भोजको धैर्यपूर्ण योजनापछि तिनले खोलिन् — कसैले मलाई र मेरा जनलाई नाश गर्न आदेश किनेको छ। म पनि यहूदी हुँ। षड्यन्त्र उल्टियो: हामान ढले, र मोर्दकै उठे, र यहूदीहरूले आफ्नो रक्षा गर्ने अधिकार पाए। जाति बाँच्यो।','Raajaale Estarlaai grahan gare. Dui bhojko dhairyapurna yojanaapachhi tinle kholin — kasaile malaai ra meraa janlaai naash garna aadesh kineko chha. Ma pani Yahudi hun. Shadyantra ultiyo: Haamaan dhale, ra Mordakai uthe, ra Yahudiharule aaphno rakshaa garne adhikaar paae. Jaati baanchyo.','The king received Esther. After a patient plan of two banquets she revealed it: someone has bought a decree to destroy me and my people. I too am a Jew. The plot overturned: Haman fell, Mordecai rose, and the Jews were granted the right to defend themselves. The people lived.','Esther 7–8'],
['एस्तरको पुस्तकभरि एउटा अनौठो कुरा छ — परमेश्वरको नाम एक पटक पनि लेखिएको छैन। तर हरेक संयोग, हरेक समय-मिलान, हरेक साहसमा उहाँकै हात प्रस्टै देखिन्छ। कहिलेकाहीं परमेश्वर मौन रहनुहुन्छ — तर कहिल्यै अनुपस्थित हुनुहुन्न।','Estarko pustakbhari eutaa anautho kuraa chha — Parameshwarko naam ek patak pani lekhieko chhaina. Tara harek sanyog, harek samaya-milaan, harek saahasmaa uhaankai haat prastai dekhinchha. Kahilekaahin Parameshwar mauna rahanuhunchha — tara kahilyai anupasthit hunuhunna.','There is something strange about the book of Esther — God’s name is never written in it, not once. Yet his hand is plain in every coincidence, every perfect timing, every act of courage. Sometimes God is silent — but he is never absent.','Esther 9:20–22']]}
]},

{id:'fmeet',kind:'collection',title:'Meeting Jesus',ne:'येशूसँगको भेट',
overview:{t:'People he met, stories he told',ne:'उहाँले भेट्नुभएका मानिसहरू, उहाँले भन्नुभएका कथाहरू',art:FNE_ART.ovmeet,
start:['निकोदेमसबाट सुरु गरौं','Ten meetings, one Jesus'],
paras:[
['येशूको कथाले उहाँको सारा जीवन पछ्यायो — जन्म, शिक्षा, मृत्यु, पुनरुत्थान। यो सङ्ग्रह अझ नजिक उभिन्छ, आँखाको तहमा: उहाँले एक-एक गरी भेट्नुभएका मानिसहरू, र उहाँले भन्नुभएका कथाहरू।','Yeshuko kathaale uhaanko saaraa jeewan pachhyaayo — janma, shikshaa, mrityu, punarutthaan. Yo sangraha ajha najik ubhinchha, aankhaako tahmaa: uhaanle ek-ek gari bhetnubhaekaa maanisharu, ra uhaanle bhannubhaekaa kathaaharu.','The Jesus story followed his whole life — born, teaching, dying, rising. This collection stands closer, at eye level: the people he met one at a time, and the stories he told.'],
['मानिससँग उहाँ कहिल्यै हतारमा हुनुहुन्नथ्यो। एक जना शिक्षक रातको अँध्यारोमा आए। एउटी स्त्रीले मध्याह्नमा इनारमा उहाँलाई भेटिन्। एक जना कर उठाउने उहाँलाई हेर्न मात्र रूखमा चढे। तीमध्ये हरेक बदलिएर घर फर्के।','Maanissanga uhaan kahilyai hataarmaa hunuhunnathyo. Ek janaa shikshak raatko andhyaaromaa aae. Euti striile madhyaahnmaa inaarmaa uhaanlaai bhetin. Ek janaa kar uthaaune uhaanlaai herna maatra rukhmaa chadhe. Teemadhye harek badaliera ghar pharke.','He was never in a hurry with a person. A teacher came to him after dark. A woman met him at a well at midday. A tax collector climbed a tree just to see him go past. Every one of them went home changed.'],
['अनि उहाँले कथाहरूमा सिकाउनुभयो — किसान, गोठाला, नोकर र हराएका कुराहरूका बारेमा। साधारण कथाहरू, जुन जोसुकैले घर लैजान र वर्षौंसम्म सोच्न सक्थ्यो।','Ani uhaanle kathaaharumaa sikaaunubhayo — kisaan, gothaalaa, nokar ra haraaekaa kuraaharukaa baaremaa. Saadhaaran kathaaharu, jun josukaile ghar laijaana ra barshaunsamma sochna sakthyo.','And he taught in stories — about farmers, shepherds, servants and lost things. Ordinary stories anyone could carry home and think about for years.'],
['यहाँको हरेक कथा आफैमा पूरा छ; जुनसुकै क्रममा पढ्नुहोस्। सँगै तिनले एउटै प्रश्नको जवाफ दिइरहन्छन्: परमेश्वर वास्तवमा कस्तो हुनुहुन्छ?','Yahaanko harek kathaa aaphaimaa puraa chha; junsukai kramamaa padhnuhos. Sangai tinle eutai prashnako jawaaph diirahanchhan: Parameshwar waastawamaa kasto hunuhunchha?','Each one here is complete on its own; read them in any order. Together they keep answering the same question: what is God actually like?'],
['जवाफ हरेक पटक उस्तै आउँछ। उहाँ मानिसहरूलाई खोज्न आउनुहुन्छ। उहाँ तिनीहरूदेखि लाज मान्नुहुन्न। र सबैले पछिल्लो सम्झेको मानिस पटक-पटक उहाँको टेबलमा पुगिरहन्छ।','Jawaaph harek patak ustai aaunchha. Uhaan maanisharulaai khojna aaunuhunchha. Uhaan tiniharudekhi laaj maannuhunna. Ra sabaile pachhillo samjheko maanis patak-patak uhaanko teblamaa pugirahanchha.','The answer comes back the same every time. He comes looking for people. He is not ashamed of them. And the last person anyone expected keeps ending up at his table.']]},
sections:[
{id:'nicodemus',t:'Nicodemus — the visitor at night',ne:'निकोदेमस — रातको पाहुना',art:FNE_ART.nicodemus,
note:['निकोदेमसले आफ्नो सारा जीवन कसरी असल हुने भनेर अध्ययन गर्दै बिताएका थिए। येशूले उनलाई भन्नुभयो — तिमीलाई त्यस्तो कुरा चाहिन्छ जुन तिमी हासिल गर्न सक्दैनौ; जन्म, र जन्म त पाइने कुरा हो।','Nikodemasle aaphno saaraa jeewan kasari asal hune bhanera adhyayan gardai bitaaekaa thie. Yeshule unlaai bhannubhayo — timilaai tyasto kuraa chaahinchha jun timi haasil garna sakdainau; janma, ra janma ta paaine kuraa ho.','Nicodemus had spent his whole life studying how to be good enough. Jesus told him he needed something he could not achieve — a birth, and a birth is something you receive.'],
paras:[
['निकोदेमस व्यवस्थाका आदरणीय शिक्षक र शासक परिषद्का सदस्य थिए। उनी रातमा येशूकहाँ आए — सायद कसैले नदेखोस् भनेर। उनले नम्रतापूर्वक सुरु गरे — गुरुज्यू, हामी जान्दछौं, परमेश्वर तपाईंसँग हुनुहुन्छ।','Nikodemas byawasthaakaa aadarniya shikshak ra shaasak parishadkaa sadasya thie. Uni raatmaa Yeshukahaan aae — saayad kasaile nadekhos bhanera. Unle namrataapurwak suru gare — gurujyu, haami jaandachhaun, Parameshwar tapaainsanga hunuhunchha.','Nicodemus was a respected teacher of the law and a member of the ruling council. He came to Jesus at night — perhaps so that no one would see him. He began politely: teacher, we know God is with you.','John 3:1–2'],
['येशूले नम्र जवाफ दिनुभएन। उहाँले भन्नुभयो — कोही नयाँ गरी नजन्मेसम्म परमेश्वरको राज्य देख्न सक्दैन।','Yeshule namra jawaaph dinubhaena. Uhaanle bhannubhayo — kohi nayaan gari najanmesamma Parameshwarko raajya dekhna sakdaina.','Jesus did not answer politely. He said: unless a person is born again, they cannot see the kingdom of God.','John 3:3'],
['निकोदेमस अलमलमा परे। हुर्केको मानिस कसरी जन्मन सक्छ? के ऊ फेरि आमाभित्र पस्न सक्छ? उनी विद्वान् थिए, तर त्यस दिन उनले केही बुझेनन्।','Nikodemas alamalmaa pare. Hurkeko maanis kasari janmana sakchha? Ke u pheri aamaabhitra pasna sakchha? Uni widwaan thie, tara tyas din unle kehi bujhenan.','Nicodemus was baffled. How can a grown man be born? Can he enter his mother again? He was a scholar, and for once he understood nothing.','John 3:4'],
['येशूले बुझाउनुभयो — पहिलो जन्मले तिमीलाई शरीर दिन्छ; यो दोस्रो जन्म आत्माबाट हो। यो बतास जस्तै हो — तिमी त्यसको आवाज सुन्छौ, त्यसले हल्लाएको देख्छौ, तर त्यो कहाँबाट आउँछ र कहाँ जान्छ, तिमी नियन्त्रण गर्न सक्दैनौ।','Yeshule bujhaaunubhayo — pahilo janmale timilaai sharir dinchha; yo dosro janma Aatmaabaata ho. Yo bataas jastai ho — timi tyasko aawaaj sunchhau, tyasle hallaaeko dekhchhau, tara tyo kahaanbaata aaunchha ra kahaan jaanchha, timi niyantran garna sakdainau.','Jesus explained: the first birth gives you a body; this second birth is of the Spirit. It is like the wind — you hear it and see what it moves, but you cannot control where it comes from or where it goes.','John 3:5–8'],
['अनि येशूले त्यो वाक्य भन्नुभयो जुन अरू लगभग सबैभन्दा टाढा पुगेको छ — परमेश्वरले संसारलाई यति धेरै प्रेम गर्नुभयो कि आफ्ना एक मात्र पुत्र दिनुभयो, ताकि उहाँमाथि विश्वास गर्ने कोही पनि नाश नहोस्, तर कहिल्यै नसकिने जीवन पाओस्।','Ani Yeshule tyo waakya bhannubhayo jun aru lagbhag sabaibhandaa taadhaa pugeko chha — Parameshwarle sansaarlaai yati dherai prem garnubhayo ki aaphnaa ek maatra putra dinubhayo, taaki uhaanmaathi wishwaas garne kohi pani naash nahos, tara kahilyai nasakine jeewan paaos.','Then Jesus said the sentence that has travelled further than almost any other: God loved the world so much that he gave his only Son, so that whoever believes in him would not perish but have life that never ends.','John 3:16'],
['त्यो रात निकोदेमस चुपचाप गए। तर उनी अझै दुई पटक देखा पर्छन् — परिषद्अगाडि येशूको पक्षमा बोल्दै, र अन्तमा, उहाँलाई गाड्न मसला बोकेर। कुनै-कुनै जन्म पूरा हुन समय लाग्छ।','Tyo raat Nikodemas chupchaap gae. Tara uni ajhai dui patak dekhaa parchhan — parishadagaadi Yeshuko pakshamaa boldai, ra antamaa, uhaanlaai gaadna masalaa bokera. Kunai-kunai janma puraa huna samaya laagchha.','Nicodemus went away quiet that night. But he appears twice more — defending Jesus before the council, and at the end, carrying spices to bury him. Some births take a while to finish.','John 7:50–51 · 19:39']]},
{id:'well',t:'The woman at the well',ne:'इनारमा भेटिएकी स्त्री',art:FNE_ART.well,
note:['उहाँले पहिले उनीसँग पानी माग्नुभयो। कहिलेकाहीं कसैसम्म पुग्ने बाटो भनेको उसलाई केही दिनु होइन, बरु उसबाट केही लिनु हो।','Uhaanle pahile unisanga paani maagnubhayo. Kahilekaahin kasaisamma pugne baato bhaneko uslaai kehi dinu hoina, baru usbaata kehi linu ho.','He asked her for water first. Sometimes the way to reach a person is not to offer them something, but to let them give you something.'],
paras:[
['येशू सामरिया हुँदै यात्रा गर्दै हुनुहुन्थ्यो — यहूदीहरूले टार्ने क्षेत्र, किनकि ती दुई जातिले शताब्दीयौंदेखि एकअर्कालाई घृणा गर्दै आएका थिए। मध्याह्नमा थाकेर उहाँ एउटा पुरानो इनारको छेउमा बस्नुभयो।','Yeshu Saamariyaa hundai yaatraa gardai hunuhunthyo — yahudiharule taarne kshetra, kinaki tee dui jaatile shataabdiyaundekhi ekarkaalaai ghrinaa gardai aaekaa thie. Madhyaahnmaa thaakera uhaan eutaa puraano inaarko chheumaa basnubhayo.','Jesus was travelling through Samaria — a region Jews avoided, for the two peoples had despised each other for centuries. Tired at midday, he sat down beside an old well.','John 4:3–6'],
['एउटी सामरी स्त्री पानी भर्न आइन्। मध्याह्न पानी भर्ने बेला होइन — अरू स्त्रीहरू बिहान सबेरै आउँथे। उनी एक्लै आइन्, गर्मीमा, जब त्यहाँ कोही हुँदैनथ्यो।','Euti saamari strii paani bharna aain. Madhyaahn paani bharne belaa hoina — aru striiharu bihaan saberai aaunthe. Uni eklai aain, garmimaa, jaba tyahaan kohi hundainathyo.','A Samaritan woman came to draw water. Midday is the wrong time to fetch water — the other women came at dawn. She came alone, in the heat, when nobody would be there.','John 4:7'],
['येशूले उनीसँग पिउने पानी माग्नुभयो। उनी छक्क परिन् — तपाईं यहूदी, म सामरी स्त्री — तपाईंले मसँग कसरी केही माग्न सक्नुहुन्छ? एउटै वाक्यमा दुई पर्खाल ढले।','Yeshule unisanga piune paani maagnubhayo. Uni chhakka parin — tapaain yahudi, ma saamari strii — tapaainle masanga kasari kehi maagna saknuhunchha? Eutai waakyamaa dui parkhaal dhale.','Jesus asked her for a drink. She was astonished: you are a Jew and I am a Samaritan woman — how can you ask me for anything? Two walls fell in a single sentence.','John 4:7–9'],
['उहाँले उनलाई त्यस्तो पानीको कुरा गर्नुभयो जसले तिर्खा सधैंको लागि मेटाउँछ — मानिसभित्रैको मूल, जुन कहिल्यै नसकिने जीवनसम्म उम्रन्छ। उनले भनिन् — प्रभु, मलाई त्यही पानी दिनुहोस्।','Uhaanle unlaai tyasto paaniko kuraa garnubhayo jasle tirkhaa sadhainko laagi metaaunchha — maanisbhitraiko mool, jun kahilyai nasakine jeewansamma umranchha. Unle bhanin — Prabhu, malaai tyahi paani dinuhos.','He told her about water that ends thirst for good — a spring inside a person, welling up to life that never ends. She said: sir, give me that water.','John 4:10–15'],
['अनि उहाँले भन्नुभयो — गएर आफ्नो श्रीमान्लाई बोलाऊ। उनले भनिन् — मेरो श्रीमान् छैन। उहाँले नरम भई उनको जीवन नै भन्नुभयो — पाँच जना श्रीमान्, र अहिले जोसँग छ्यौ, त्यो तिम्रो श्रीमान् होइन। उहाँलाई सबै थाहा थियो, र उहाँ गइहाल्नुभएन।','Ani uhaanle bhannubhayo — gaera aaphno shreemaanlaai bolaau. Unle bhanin — mero shreemaan chhaina. Uhaanle naram bhai unko jeewan nai bhannubhayo — paanch janaa shreemaan, ra ahile josanga chhyau, tyo timro shreemaan hoina. Uhaanlaai sabai thaahaa thiyo, ra uhaan gaihaalnubhaena.','Then he said: go and call your husband. She said she had none. Gently he named her life — five husbands, and the man she was with now was not her husband. He knew everything, and he had not left.','John 4:16–18'],
['उनले आफ्नो गाग्री छोडेर सहरतिर दौडिन् — आऊ, हेर, एक जना मानिस जसले मैले गरेका सबै कुरा मलाई भने। उनकै कारण धेरैले विश्वास गरे। येशूले आफू मसीह हुँ भनी खुलेर बताउनुभएको पहिलो मानिस एउटी स्त्री थिइन् — विदेशी, र नाम बिग्रेकी।','Unle aaphno gaagri chhodera sahartira daudin — aau, her, ek janaa maanis jasle maile garekaa sabai kuraa malaai bhane. Unkai kaaran dheraile wishwaas gare. Yeshule aaphu Maseeh hun bhani khulera bataaunubhaeko pahilo maanis euti strii thiin — wideshi, ra naam bigreki.','She left her water jar and ran into the town — come and see a man who told me everything I ever did. Many believed because of her. The first person Jesus openly told that he was the Messiah was a woman, a foreigner, with a reputation.','John 4:25–30, 39']]},
{id:'stones',t:'The woman they came to stone',ne:'ढुङ्गा हान्न ल्याइएकी स्त्री',art:FNE_ART.stones,
note:['उनले गरेको कुरालाई उहाँले सफाइ दिनुभएन — उहाँले भन्नुभयो, त्यो जीवन छोड। तर उनले सुन्ने पहिलो शब्द दोष होइन भन्ने कुरा उहाँले पक्का गर्नुभयो।','Unle gareko kuraalaai uhaanle saphaai dinubhaena — uhaanle bhannubhayo, tyo jeewan chhod. Tara unle sunne pahilo shabda dosh hoina bhanne kuraa uhaanle pakkaa garnubhayo.','He did not excuse what she had done — he told her to leave that life. But he made sure the first words she heard were not condemnation.'],
paras:[
['बिहान सबेरै येशू मन्दिरको चोकमा सिकाउँदै हुनुहुन्थ्यो, त्यत्तिकैमा धार्मिक अगुवाहरूले एउटी स्त्रीलाई भीडको बीचमा धकेले। उनी व्यभिचारमा पक्राउ परेकी थिइन्।','Bihaan saberai Yeshu mandirko chokmaa sikaaundai hunuhunthyo, tyattikaimaa dhaarmik aguwaaharule euti striilaai bheedko beechmaa dhakele. Uni byabhichaarmaa pakraau parekee thiin.','Jesus was teaching in the temple courts at dawn when the religious leaders pushed a woman into the middle of the crowd. She had been caught in adultery.','John 8:2–3'],
['त्यो पासो थियो। तिनीहरूले भने — व्यवस्थाले भन्छ, ढुङ्गाले हान्नू। तपाईं के भन्नुहुन्छ? उहाँले छोडिदेऊ भन्नुभयो भने मोशाको व्यवस्था तोडिन्थ्यो; ढुङ्गाले हान भन्नुभयो भने उहाँकै दयाको सन्देश तोडिन्थ्यो।','Tyo paaso thiyo. Tiniharule bhane — byawasthaale bhanchha, dhungaale haannu. Tapaain ke bhannuhunchha? Uhaanle chhodideu bhannubhayo bhane Moshaako byawasthaa todinthyo; dhungaale haan bhannubhayo bhane uhaankai dayaako sandesh todinthyo.','It was a trap. The law says stone her, they said. What do you say? If he said let her go, he broke the law of Moses; if he said stone her, he broke his own message of mercy.','John 8:4–6'],
['येशूले केही भन्नुभएन। उहाँ निहुरनुभयो र औंलाले धूलोमा लेख्न थाल्नुभयो। भीड पर्खिरह्यो। उहाँ लेखिरहनुभयो।','Yeshule kehi bhannubhaena. Uhaan nihuranubhayo ra aunlaale dhoolomaa lekhna thaalnubhayo. Bheed parkhirahyo. Uhaan lekhirahanubhayo.','Jesus said nothing. He bent down and wrote in the dust with his finger. The crowd waited. He kept writing.','John 8:6'],
['अनि उहाँ सीधा हुनुभयो र एउटै वाक्य भन्नुभयो — तिमीहरूमध्ये जसले कहिल्यै पाप गरेको छैन, उसैले पहिलो ढुङ्गा हानोस्। अनि उहाँ फेरि निहुरेर लेख्न थाल्नुभयो।','Ani uhaan seedhaa hunubhayo ra eutai waakya bhannubhayo — timiharumadhye jasle kahilyai paap gareko chhaina, usaile pahilo dhungaa haanos. Ani uhaan pheri nihurera lekhna thaalnubhayo.','Then he straightened up and said one sentence: let whichever of you has never sinned throw the first stone. And he bent down and wrote again.','John 8:7–8'],
['एक-एक गर्दै तिनीहरू गए, सबभन्दा वृद्धबाट सुरु भयो। कोही पनि बहस गर्न बसेनन्। ढुङ्गा हातमै रह्यो, र हातहरू तल झरे।','Ek-ek gardai tiniharu gae, sabbhandaa wriddhabaata suru bhayo. Kohi pani bahas garna basenan. Dhungaa haatmai rahyo, ra haatharu tala jhare.','One by one they left, beginning with the oldest. Nobody stayed to argue. The stones stayed in their hands, and the hands went down.','John 8:9'],
['उनीहरू दुई जना मात्र बाँकी रहे। नारी, तिनीहरू कहाँ छन्? कसैले तिमीलाई दोषी ठहराएन? कसैले पनि होइन, प्रभु। त्यसो भए म पनि तिमीलाई दोषी ठहराउँदिनँ, येशूले भन्नुभयो। जाऊ, र यो जीवन पछाडि छोड।','Uniharu dui janaa maatra baanki rahe. Naari, tiniharu kahaan chhan? Kasaile timilaai doshi thahraaena? Kasaile pani hoina, Prabhu. Tyaso bhae ma pani timilaai doshi thahraaundinan, Yeshule bhannubhayo. Jaau, ra yo jeewan pachhaadi chhod.','Only the two of them were left. Woman, where are they? Has no one condemned you? No one, sir. Then neither do I condemn you, said Jesus. Go, and leave this life behind.','John 8:10–11']]},
{id:'zacchaeus',t:'Zacchaeus — the man in the tree',ne:'जक्कै — रूखमा चढेको मानिस',art:FNE_ART.zacchaeus,
note:['सबैले टार्ने घरमा येशू आफैले खाना खान जान्छु भन्नुभयो। भीडले गनगन गर्‍यो — र त्यही घरभित्र एक जना मानिसले चोरेको चार गुणा फिर्ता दिए।','Sabaile taarne gharmaa Yeshu aaphaile khaanaa khaana jaanchhu bhannubhayo. Bheedle gangan garyo — ra tyahi gharbhitra ek janaa maanisle choreko chaar gunaa phirtaa die.','Jesus invited himself to dinner at the one house everyone else avoided. The crowd grumbled about it — and inside that house a man gave back four times what he had stolen.'],
paras:[
['यरीहोमा जक्कै नाम गरेका एक जना मानिस बस्थे — मुख्य कर उठाउने, र धनी। कर उठाउनेहरू कब्जा गर्ने रोमीहरूका लागि काम गर्थे र आफ्नो लागि थप असुल्थे। आफ्नै मानिसहरूले तिनीहरूलाई गद्दार ठान्थे।','Yareehomaa Jakkai naam garekaa ek janaa maanis basthe — mukhya kar uthaaune, ra dhani. Kar uthaauneharu kabjaa garne Romiharukaa laagi kaam garthe ra aaphno laagi thap asulthe. Aaphnai maanisharule tiniharulaai gaddaar thaanthe.','In Jericho lived a man named Zacchaeus — the chief tax collector, and rich. Tax collectors worked for the occupying Romans and skimmed extra for themselves. Their own people counted them as traitors.','Luke 19:1–2'],
['येशू त्यही बाटो जाँदै हुनुहुन्थ्यो, र जक्कैलाई उहाँलाई हेर्ने रहर थियो। तर उनी होचा थिए र भीड बाक्लो थियो, त्यसैले उनी अगाडि दौडेर अञ्जीरको रूखमा चढे — एक धनी अधिकारी, रूखमाथि, सारा सहरको सामु।','Yeshu tyahi baato jaandai hunuhunthyo, ra Jakkailaai uhaanlaai herne rahar thiyo. Tara uni hochaa thie ra bheed baaklo thiyo, tyasaile uni agaadi daudera anjeerko rukhmaa chadhe — ek dhani adhikaari, rukhmaathi, saaraa saharko saamu.','Jesus was passing through, and Zacchaeus wanted to see him. But he was a short man and the crowd was deep, so he ran ahead and climbed a sycamore tree — a rich official, up a tree, in front of the whole town.','Luke 19:3–4'],
['येशू रूखनेर पुग्नुभयो, माथि हेर्नुभयो, र उनको नाम लिनुभयो — जक्कै, चाँडो ओर्ल। आज म तिम्रो घरमा बस्नैपर्छ।','Yeshu rukhner pugnubhayo, maathi hernubhayo, ra unko naam linubhayo — Jakkai, chaando orla. Aaja ma timro gharmaa basnaiparchha.','Jesus reached the tree, looked up, and used his name: Zacchaeus, come down quickly. I must stay at your house today.','Luke 19:5'],
['उनी तुरुन्तै खुसी हुँदै ओर्ले। अनि भीडले गनगन सुरु गर्‍यो — उहाँ त पापीको पाहुना बन्न जानुभयो।','Uni turuntai khusi hundai orle. Ani bheedle gangan suru garyo — uhaan ta paapeeko paahunaa banna jaanubhayo.','He came down at once, delighted. And the crowd began to mutter — he has gone to be the guest of a sinner.','Luke 19:6–7'],
['तर टेबलमा जक्कै उठे — प्रभु, मेरो सम्पत्तिको आधा म गरिबहरूलाई दिन्छु, र मैले कसैलाई ठगेको छु भने चार गुणा फिर्ता गर्छु। कसैले उनलाई भनेको थिएन।','Tara teblamaa Jakkai uthe — Prabhu, mero sampattiko aadhaa ma garibharulaai dinchhu, ra maile kasailaai thageko chhu bhane chaar gunaa phirtaa garchhu. Kasaile unlaai bhaneko thiena.','But at the table Zacchaeus stood up: Lord, I give half of everything I own to the poor, and if I have cheated anyone I will pay back four times as much. Nobody had asked him to.','Luke 19:8'],
['येशूले भन्नुभयो — आज यस घरमा मुक्ति आएको छ। मानिसको पुत्र हराएकोलाई खोज्न र बचाउन आउनुभएको हो।','Yeshule bhannubhayo — aaja yas gharmaa mukti aaeko chha. Maanisko Putra haraaekolaai khojna ra bachaauna aaunubhaeko ho.','Jesus said: today salvation has come to this house. The Son of Man came to seek and to save what was lost.','Luke 19:9–10']]},
{id:'bartimaeus',t:'Bartimaeus — what do you want?',ne:'बारतिमाइ — तिमी के चाहन्छौ?',art:FNE_ART.bartimaeus,
note:['येशूले एक दृष्टिविहीन भिखारीलाई सोध्नुभयो — तिमी के चाहन्छौ? मानौं त्यो स्पष्ट थिएन। उहाँ मानिसलाई समाधान गर्नुपर्ने समस्या ठान्नुहुन्न — उहाँ सोध्नुहुन्छ।','Yeshule ek drishtiwiheen bhikhaareelaai sodhnubhayo — timi ke chaahanchhau? Maanaun tyo spashta thiena. Uhaan maanislaai samaadhaan garnuparne samasyaa thaannuhunna — uhaan sodhnuhunchha.','Jesus asked a blind beggar what he wanted, as if it were not obvious. He does not treat people as problems to be solved — he asks them.'],
paras:[
['यरीहोबाहिर बारतिमाइ नाम गरेका एक दृष्टिविहीन मानिस बाटोको छेउमा भीख माग्दै बसेका थिए। येशू त्यही बाटो जाँदै हुनुहुन्छ भन्ने सुनेर उनी कराउन थाले — येशू, दाऊदका पुत्र, ममाथि दया गर्नुहोस्!','Yareehobaahir Baartimaai naam garekaa ek drishtiwiheen maanis baatoko chheumaa bheekh maagdai basekaa thie. Yeshu tyahi baato jaandai hunuhunchha bhanne sunera uni karaauna thaale — Yeshu, Daaudkaa Putra, mamaathi dayaa garnuhos!','Outside Jericho a blind man named Bartimaeus sat begging beside the road. He heard that Jesus was going past and began to shout: Jesus, Son of David, have mercy on me!','Mark 10:46–47'],
['वरिपरिका मानिसहरूले उनलाई चुप लाग् भने। त्यसैले उनी झन् चर्को कराए। उनीसँग जोगाउनुपर्ने कुनै मान बाँकी थिएन, र यो मौका जान दिने उनको इच्छा थिएन।','Wariparikaa maanisharule unlaai chup laag bhane. Tyasaile uni jhan charko karaae. Unisanga jogaaunuparne kunai maan baanki thiena, ra yo maukaa jaana dine unko ichchhaa thiena.','The people around him told him to be quiet. So he shouted louder. He had no dignity left to protect, and he was not going to let this pass.','Mark 10:48'],
['येशू रोकिनुभयो र भन्नुभयो — उसलाई बोलाऊ। एकैछिनमा ती नै मानिसहरूको स्वर फेरियो — खुसी होऊ, उठ, उहाँले तिमीलाई बोलाउँदै हुनुहुन्छ।','Yeshu rokinubhayo ra bhannubhayo — uslaai bolaau. Ekaichhinmaa tee nai maanisharuko swar pheriyo — khusi hou, utha, uhaanle timilaai bolaaundai hunuhunchha.','Jesus stopped and said: call him. Suddenly the same people changed their tone — cheer up, get up, he is calling you.','Mark 10:49'],
['बारतिमाइ ले आफ्नो खास्टो फ्याँके — भिखारीको खास्टो नै त्यो ठाउँ थियो जहाँ सिक्का खस्थ्यो, उनीसँग भएको एक मात्र चीज — उफ्रेर उठे, र आए।','Baartimaaile aaphno khaasto phyaanke — bhikhaareeko khaasto nai tyo thaaun thiyo jahaan sikkaa khasthyo, unisanga bhaeko ek maatra cheej — uphrera uthe, ra aae.','Bartimaeus threw off his cloak — a beggar’s cloak was where the coins landed, the only thing he owned — jumped up, and came.','Mark 10:50'],
['येशूले उनलाई सोध्नुभयो — म तिम्रो लागि के गरूँ भन्ने चाहन्छौ? एक दृष्टिविहीन भिखारीलाई। उहाँले अनुमान गर्नुभएन, सोध्नुभयो।','Yeshule unlaai sodhnubhayo — ma timro laagi ke garun bhanne chaahanchhau? Ek drishtiwiheen bhikhaareelaai. Uhaanle anumaan garnubhaena, sodhnubhayo.','Jesus asked him: what do you want me to do for you? To a blind beggar. He asked instead of assuming.','Mark 10:51'],
['गुरुज्यू, म देख्न चाहन्छु। जाऊ, येशूले भन्नुभयो, तिम्रो विश्वासले तिमीलाई निको पार्‍यो। तुरुन्तै उनले देख्न सके — र उनी बाटैभरि येशूको पछि लागे।','Gurujyu, ma dekhna chaahanchhu. Jaau, Yeshule bhannubhayo, timro wishwaasle timilaai niko paaryo. Turuntai unle dekhna sake — ra uni baataibhari Yeshuko pachhi laage.','Teacher, I want to see. Go, said Jesus, your faith has healed you. Immediately he could see — and he followed Jesus down the road.','Mark 10:51–52']]},
{id:'lostsheep',t:'The one that went missing',ne:'हराएको एउटा',art:FNE_ART.lostsheep,
note:['उनान्सय राम्रो सङ्ख्या हो। येशू भन्नुहुन्छ, परमेश्वरले उनान्सयमै छोड्न सक्नुहुन्न — र स्वर्गले आफ्नो सबैभन्दा ठूलो उत्सव फर्केर आउने एउटैका लागि राख्छ।','Unaansaya raamro sankhyaa ho. Yeshu bhannuhunchha, Parameshwarle unaansayamai chhodna saknuhunna — ra swargale aaphno sabaibhandaa thulo utsaw pharkera aaune eutaikaa laagi raakhchha.','Ninety-nine is a good number. Jesus says God cannot leave it at ninety-nine — and heaven saves its loudest celebrations for the one that comes back.'],
paras:[
['धार्मिक अगुवाहरूले गुनासो गरे — येशूले गलत मानिसहरूलाई स्वागत गर्नुहुन्छ र तिनीहरूसँगै खानुहुन्छ। त्यसैले उहाँले हराउने कुराहरूका बारेमा लगातार तीन कथा भन्नुभयो।','Dhaarmik aguwaaharule gunaaso gare — Yeshule galat maanisharulaai swaagat garnuhunchha ra tiniharusangai khaanuhunchha. Tyasaile uhaanle haraaune kuraaharukaa baaremaa lagaataar teen kathaa bhannubhayo.','The religious leaders complained that Jesus welcomed the wrong people and ate with them. So he told them three stories in a row about things that get lost.','Luke 15:1–3'],
['मानौं तिमीसँग सय वटा भेडा छन् र एउटा हरायो। उनान्सय त छँदैछ भनेर तिमी पन्छिन्छौ? पर्दैन — तिमी उनान्सय छोडेर नभेटुन्जेल खोज्न जान्छौ।','Maanaun timisanga saya wataa bhedaa chhan ra eutaa haraayo. Unaansaya ta chhandaichha bhanera timi panchhinchhau? Pardaina — timi unaansaya chhodera nabhetunjel khojna jaanchhau.','Suppose you have a hundred sheep and lose one. Do you shrug because you still have ninety-nine? No — you leave the ninety-nine and go looking until you find it.','Luke 15:4'],
['अनि भेट्दा तिमी त्यसलाई गाली गर्दैनौ। तिमी त्यसलाई काँधमा बोकेर घर ल्याउँछौ, र छिमेकीहरूलाई बोलाउँछौ — मसँगै रमाऊ, मैले मेरो भेडा भेट्टाएँ।','Ani bhetdaa timi tyaslaai gaali gardainau. Timi tyaslaai kaandhmaa bokera ghar lyaaunchhau, ra chhimekiharulaai bolaaunchhau — masangai ramaau, maile mero bhedaa bhettaaen.','And when you find it, you do not scold it. You lift it onto your shoulders and carry it home, and call your neighbours: celebrate with me, I found my sheep.','Luke 15:5–6'],
['त्यसै गरी, येशूले भन्नुभयो, परमेश्वरतिर फर्कने एक जनाको लागि स्वर्ग कहिल्यै नभड्किएका उनान्सयको भन्दा बढी खुसी हुन्छ।','Tyasai gari, Yeshule bhannubhayo, Parameshwartira pharkane ek janaako laagi swarga kahilyai nabhadkiekaa unaansayako bhandaa badhi khusi hunchha.','In the same way, Jesus said, heaven is happier over one person who turns back to God than over ninety-nine who never wandered off.','Luke 15:7'],
['अनि दोस्रो कथा — एउटी स्त्रीले दस चाँदीका सिक्कामध्ये एउटा हराउँछिन्। उनी बत्ती बाल्छिन्, सारा घर बढार्छिन् र नभेटुन्जेल हरेक कुना खोज्छिन् — अनि साथीहरूलाई रमाउन बोलाउँछिन्।','Ani dosro kathaa — euti striile das chaandeekaa sikkaamadhye eutaa haraaunchhin. Uni batti baalchhin, saaraa ghar badhaarchhin ra nabhetunjel harek kunaa khojchhin — ani saatheeharulaai ramaauna bolaaunchhin.','Then a second story: a woman loses one silver coin out of ten. She lights a lamp, sweeps the whole house and searches every corner until she finds it — and calls her friends to celebrate.','Luke 15:8–9'],
['भेडा आफै भड्कियो; सिक्का त धूलोमा त्यसै लडिरह्यो, केही गर्नै नसक्ने। दुवैलाई खोजिन्छ। कुनै पनि छोडिँदैन।','Bhedaa aaphai bhadkiyo; sikkaa ta dhoolomaa tyasai ladirahyo, kehi garnai nasakne. Duwailaai khojinchha. Kunai pani chhodindaina.','The sheep wandered off; the coin just lay there in the dust, unable to do anything at all. Both are hunted for. Neither is left.','Luke 15:10']]},
{id:'twoprayers',t:'Two men praying',ne:'प्रार्थना गर्ने दुई जना',art:FNE_ART.twoprayers,
note:['एउटाले परमेश्वरलाई आफू कति असल छु भने; अर्कोले आँखा उठाउनसम्म सकेन। तीमध्ये एक जना मात्र परमेश्वरसँग ठीक भएर घर फर्के — र त्यो प्रभावशाली मानिस थिएन।','Eutaale Parameshwarlaai aaphu kati asal chhu bhane; arkole aankhaa uthaaunasamma sakena. Teemadhye ek janaa maatra Parameshwarsanga theek bhaera ghar pharke — ra tyo prabhaawshaali maanis thiena.','One man told God how good he was; the other could not even lift his eyes. Only one of them went home right with God — and it was not the impressive one.'],
paras:[
['केही मानिसहरू आफ्नो असलपनमा पूरै ढुक्क थिए र अरू सबैलाई होच्याउँथे। त्यसैले येशूले तिनीहरूलाई मन्दिरमा प्रार्थना गर्न गएका दुई जना मानिसको कथा भन्नुभयो।','Kehi maanisharu aaphno asalpanmaa purai dhukka thie ra aru sabailaai hochyaaunthe. Tyasaile Yeshule tiniharulaai mandirmaa praarthanaa garna gaekaa dui janaa maanisko kathaa bhannubhayo.','Some people were quite sure of their own goodness and looked down on everyone else. So Jesus told them about two men who went up to the temple to pray.','Luke 18:9–10'],
['एक जना फरिसी थिए — कडा, धार्मिक, साँच्चै अनुशासित मानिस। अर्को कर उठाउने थिए, त्यस्तो मानिस जसलाई टार्न पहिलोले बाटो नै काट्थे।','Ek janaa Pharisee thie — kadaa, dhaarmik, saanchchai anushaasit maanis. Arko kar uthaaune thie, tyasto maanis jaslaai taarna pahilole baato nai kaatthe.','One was a Pharisee — a strict, religious, genuinely disciplined man. The other was a tax collector, the kind of man the first would cross the street to avoid.','Luke 18:10'],
['फरिसी उभिएर प्रार्थना गरे — हे परमेश्वर, म अरू मानिसहरूजस्तो छैनँ भनेर धन्यवाद दिन्छु — चोर, ठग, वा यो कर उठाउनेजस्तो। म हप्तामा दुई पटक उपवास बस्छु र सबै कुराको दशांश दिन्छु।','Pharisee ubhiera praarthanaa gare — he Parameshwar, ma aru maanisharujasto chhainan bhanera dhanyabaad dinchhu — chor, thag, waa yo kar uthaaunejasto. Ma haptaamaa dui patak upawaas baschhu ra sabai kuraako dashaansha dinchhu.','The Pharisee stood and prayed: God, I thank you that I am not like other people — thieves, cheats, or like this tax collector here. I fast twice a week and give a tenth of everything.','Luke 18:11–12'],
['त्यसको हरेक शब्द सत्य थियो। उनले साँच्चै उपवास बस्थे; साँच्चै दिन्थे। उनले बिर्सेका थिए — ती दुईमध्ये कुनचाहिँ केही पाउन आएको हो।','Tyasko harek shabda satya thiyo. Unle saanchchai upawaas basthe; saanchchai dinthe. Unle birsekaa thie — tee duimadhye kunchaahin kehi paauna aaeko ho.','Every word of it was true. He really did fast; he really did give. He had simply forgotten which of the two of them had come to receive anything.','Luke 18:11–12'],
['कर उठाउने टाढै उभिए। उनले आँखा उठाउन सकेनन्। छाती पिट्दै उनले भने — हे परमेश्वर, म पापीमाथि दया गर्नुहोस्।','Kar uthaaune taadhai ubhie. Unle aankhaa uthaauna sakenan. Chhaati pitdai unle bhane — he Parameshwar, ma paapeemaathi dayaa garnuhos.','The tax collector stood far off. He could not lift his eyes. He struck his chest and said seven words: God, have mercy on me, a sinner.','Luke 18:13'],
['येशूले भन्नुभयो — परमेश्वरसँग ठीक भएर घर फर्कने त्यही मानिस थिए, अर्को होइन। जसले आफूलाई उचाल्छ, ऊ तल झारिनेछ; र जसले आफूलाई होच्याउँछ, ऊ उचालिनेछ।','Yeshule bhannubhayo — Parameshwarsanga theek bhaera ghar pharkane tyahi maanis thie, arko hoina. Jasle aaphulaai uchaalchha, u tala jhaarinechha; ra jasle aaphulaai hochyaaunchha, u uchaalinechha.','Jesus said: it was that man who went home right with God, not the other. Anyone who lifts himself up will be brought down, and anyone who lowers himself will be lifted up.','Luke 18:14']]},
{id:'sower',t:'The farmer and the soil',ne:'किसान र माटो',art:FNE_ART.sower,
note:['बीउ हरेक पटक उही थियो। फरक त्यो माटोमा थियो जहाँ त्यो खस्यो — अर्थात् प्रश्न परमेश्वर बोल्नुहुन्छ कि हुन्न भन्ने होइन, हामी कस्तो माटो हौं भन्ने हो।','Beeu harek patak uhi thiyo. Pharak tyo maatomaa thiyo jahaan tyo khasyo — arthaat prashna Parameshwar bolnuhunchha ki hunna bhanne hoina, haami kasto maato haun bhanne ho.','The seed was the same every time. The difference was the ground it fell on — which means the question is not whether God is speaking, but what kind of soil we are.'],
paras:[
['यति ठूलो भीड जम्मा भयो कि येशू डुङ्गामा चढेर किनारबाट अलिकति पर जानुभयो, र किनारमा उभिएका मानिसहरूलाई सिकाउनुभयो। उहाँले तिनीहरूलाई बीउ छर्ने किसानको कुरा भन्नुभयो।','Yati thulo bheed jammaa bhayo ki Yeshu dungaamaa chadhera kinaarbaata alikati para jaanubhayo, ra kinaarmaa ubhiekaa maanisharulaai sikaaunubhayo. Uhaanle tiniharulaai beeu chharne kisaanko kuraa bhannubhayo.','A crowd so large gathered that Jesus got into a boat and pushed out a little from the shore, and taught the people standing on the beach. He told them about a farmer sowing seed.','Mark 4:1–3'],
['केही बीउ कडा बाटोमा खस्यो। चराहरू आए र त्यसले केही गर्न पाउनुअघि नै खाइदिए।','Kehi beeu kadaa baatomaa khasyo. Charaaharu aae ra tyasle kehi garna paaunuaghi nai khaaidie.','Some seed fell on the hard path. The birds came and ate it before it could do anything at all.','Mark 4:4'],
['केही ढुङ्गेनी जमिनमा खस्यो, जहाँ माटोको पातलो तह मात्र थियो। त्यो छिट्टै उम्रियो — र घाम लाग्दा ओइलायो, किनकि त्यसको जरा थिएन।','Kehi dhungeni jaminmaa khasyo, jahaan maatoko paatalo taha maatra thiyo. Tyo chhittai umriyo — ra ghaam laagdaa oilaayo, kinaki tyasko jaraa thiena.','Some fell on rocky ground with only a thin layer of soil. It sprang up fast — and when the sun rose it withered, because it had no root.','Mark 4:5–6'],
['केही काँडाहरूका बीचमा खस्यो, र काँडा बढेर त्यसलाई निसासिदिए, त्यसैले त्यसले केही फलाएन।','Kehi kaandaaharukaa beechmaa khasyo, ra kaandaa badhera tyaslaai nisaasidie, tyasaile tyasle kehi phalaaena.','Some fell among thorns, and the thorns grew up and choked it, so it produced nothing.','Mark 4:7'],
['अनि केही असल माटोमा खस्यो र फल दियो — छरेको भन्दा तीस, साठी, सय गुणा।','Ani kehi asal maatomaa khasyo ra phal diyo — chhareko bhandaa tees, saathi, saya gunaa.','And some fell on good soil and produced a crop — thirty, sixty, a hundred times what was sown.','Mark 4:8'],
['पछि उहाँले बुझाउनुभयो — बीउ परमेश्वरको वचन हो। बाटो त्यो हृदय हो जहाँ त्यो कहिल्यै भित्र पस्दैन; ढुङ्गेनी जमिन गहिराइविनाको छिटो जोश हो, पहिलो दुःखमै हराउने; काँडाहरू चिन्ता, पैसा र चाहना हुन्; र असल माटोले सुन्छ, समातेर राख्छ, अनि एउटा जीवन उम्रन्छ।','Pachhi uhaanle bujhaaunubhayo — beeu Parameshwarko wachan ho. Baato tyo hriday ho jahaan tyo kahilyai bhitra pasdaina; dhungeni jamin gahiraaiwinaako chhito josh ho, pahilo dukhmai haraaune; kaandaaharu chintaa, paisaa ra chaahanaa hun; ra asal maatole sunchha, samaatera raakhchha, ani eutaa jeewan umranchha.','Later he explained it: the seed is God’s word. The path is a heart it never gets into; the rocky ground is quick enthusiasm with no depth, gone at the first trouble; the thorns are worries and money and wanting; and the good soil hears it, holds on to it, and a life grows.','Mark 4:14–20']]},
{id:'servant',t:'The servant who was forgiven',ne:'क्षमा पाएको नोकर',art:FNE_ART.servant,
note:['पहिलो ऋण तिर्नै नसकिने थियो; दोस्रो सानो थियो। येशूले हाम्रो क्षमाले परमेश्वरको क्षमा कमाउँछ भन्नुभएको होइन — उहाँले भन्नुभएको हो, जसले साँच्चै त्यति धेरै पाएको छ, उसले त्यति सानो कुरा समातिरहन सक्दैन।','Pahilo rin tirnai nasakine thiyo; dosro saano thiyo. Yeshule haamro kshamaale Parameshwarko kshamaa kamaaunchha bhannubhaeko hoina — uhaanle bhannubhaeko ho, jasle saanchchai tyati dherai paaeko chha, usle tyati saano kuraa samaatirahana sakdaina.','The first debt was unpayable; the second was small. Jesus is not saying our forgiving earns God’s — he is saying that anyone who has really received that much cannot hold on to that little.'],
paras:[
['पत्रुसले येशूलाई सोधे — मलाई बारम्बार अन्याय गर्ने मानिसलाई मैले कति पटक क्षमा गर्नुपर्छ? सात पटक? सात नै उदार लाग्थ्यो।','Patrusle Yeshulaai sodhe — malaai baarambaar anyaaya garne maanislaai maile kati patak kshamaa garnuparchha? Saat patak? Saat nai udaar laagthyo.','Peter asked Jesus: how many times should I forgive someone who keeps wronging me? Seven times? Seven already felt generous.','Matthew 18:21'],
['सात पटक होइन, येशूले भन्नुभयो — सत्तरी गुणा सात। अर्थात् — गन्न छोड। अनि उहाँले एउटा कथा भन्नुभयो।','Saat patak hoina, Yeshule bhannubhayo — sattari gunaa saat. Arthaat — ganna chhod. Ani uhaanle eutaa kathaa bhannubhayo.','Not seven times, Jesus said — seventy times seven. In other words: stop counting. Then he told a story.','Matthew 18:22'],
['एक राजाले आफ्ना नोकरहरूसँग हिसाब मिलाए। एक जनाले तिर्नै नसकिने रकम तिर्नुपर्थ्यो — धेरै जुनीमा कमाउन नसकिने। उनले तिर्न सकेनन्, र राजाले सबै बेच्ने आदेश दिए।','Ek raajaale aaphnaa nokarharusanga hisaab milaae. Ek janaale tirnai nasakine rakam tirnuparthyo — dherai junimaa kamaauna nasakine. Unle tirna sakenan, ra raajaale sabai bechne aadesh die.','A king settled accounts with his servants. One owed him an impossible sum — more than a man could earn in many lifetimes. He could not pay, and the king ordered everything sold.','Matthew 18:23–25'],
['नोकर घुँडा टेकेर परे — मसँग धैर्य गर्नुहोस्, म सबै तिर्नेछु। उनले कहिल्यै तिर्न सक्दैनथे। राजाले दया गरे, सम्पूर्ण ऋण मिनाहा गरिदिए, र उनलाई जान दिए।','Nokar ghundaa tekera pare — masanga dhairya garnuhos, ma sabai tirnechhu. Unle kahilyai tirna sakdainathe. Raajaale dayaa gare, sampurna rin minaahaa garidie, ra unlaai jaana die.','The servant fell on his knees: be patient with me and I will pay it all. He never could have. The king took pity, cancelled the whole debt, and let him go.','Matthew 18:26–27'],
['त्यही नोकर बाहिर गए र आफूलाई सानो रकम तिर्नुपर्ने एक जना मानिस भेट्टाए — करिब सय दिनको ज्याला। उनले उसको घाँटी समाते — तैंले तिर्नुपर्ने तिर्। त्यो मानिसले ठ्याक्कै उनैले प्रयोग गरेका शब्दले बिन्ती गर्‍यो। उनले मानेनन्, र उसलाई झ्यालखानामा हालिदिए।','Tyahi nokar baahir gae ra aaphulaai saano rakam tirnuparne ek janaa maanis bhettaae — karib saya dinko jyaalaa. Unle usko ghaanti samaate — tainle tirnuparne tir. Tyo maanisle thyakkai unaile prayog garekaa shabdale binti garyo. Unle maanenan, ra uslaai jhyaalkhaanaamaa haalidie.','That same servant went out and found a man who owed him a small amount — about a hundred days’ wages. He grabbed him by the throat: pay me what you owe. The man begged with the very same words he himself had used. He refused, and had him thrown into prison.','Matthew 18:28–30'],
['राजाले थाहा पाएपछि उनलाई फर्काएर बोलाए — तैंले बिन्ती गरेकैले मैले त्यत्रो ऋण मिनाहा गरिदिएँ — मैले तँमाथि गरेजस्तै तैंले उसमाथि दया गर्नुपर्दैनथ्यो र? हृदयबाटै क्षमा गर, येशूले भन्नुभयो।','Raajaale thaahaa paaepachhi unlaai pharkaaera bolaae — tainle binti garekaaile maile tyatro rin minaahaa garidien — maile tanmaathi garejastai tainle usmaathi dayaa garnupardainathyo ra? Hridaybaatai kshamaa gar, Yeshule bhannubhayo.','When the king heard, he called him back: I cancelled all that debt because you begged me — should you not have had mercy on him as I had on you? Forgive from the heart, Jesus said.','Matthew 18:31–35']]},
{id:'banquet',t:'The invitation nobody wanted',ne:'कसैले नचाहेको निम्तो',art:FNE_ART.banquet,
note:['भोज गुमाउनेहरू दुष्ट थिएनन् — तिनीहरू व्यस्त थिए। र कोठा जसरी भए पनि भरियो — तिनीहरूले जसको अरू केही काम थिएन।','Bhoj gumaauneharu dushta thienan — tiniharu byasta thie. Ra kothaa jasari bhae pani bhariyo — tiniharule jasko aru kehi kaam thiena.','The people who missed the feast were not wicked — they were busy. And the room filled up anyway, with the people who had nothing else on.'],
paras:[
['एउटा भोजमा कसैले धार्मिक स्वरमा भन्यो — परमेश्वरको भोजमा खाने मानिस कति धन्य! येशूले एक जना मानिसको कथाले जवाफ दिनुभयो, जसले ठूलो भोज तयार पारे र धेरै पाहुनालाई निम्त्याए।','Eutaa bhojmaa kasaile dhaarmik swarmaa bhanyo — Parameshwarko bhojmaa khaane maanis kati dhanya! Yeshule ek janaa maanisko kathaale jawaaph dinubhayo, jasle thulo bhoj tayaar paare ra dherai paahunaalaai nimtyaae.','At a dinner someone said piously: how blessed is the person who will eat at God’s feast. Jesus answered with a story about a man who prepared a great banquet and invited many guests.','Luke 14:15–16'],
['सबै तयार भएपछि उनले आफ्नो नोकर पठाए — आउनुहोस्, अब सबै तयार छ। अनि तीमध्ये हरेकले बहाना बनाउन थाले।','Sabai tayaar bhaepachhi unle aaphno nokar pathaae — aaunuhos, aba sabai tayaar chha. Ani teemadhye harekle bahaanaa banaauna thaale.','When everything was ready he sent his servant to say: come, it is all ready now. And every one of them began to make excuses.','Luke 14:17–18'],
['मैले खेत किनेको छु, गएर हेर्नैपर्छ। मैले पाँच हल गोरु किनेको छु, जाँच्नैपर्छ। मैले भर्खर बिहे गरेको छु, त्यसैले आउन सक्दिनँ। जमिन, काम, परिवार — कुनै पनि खराब होइन, तर सबै निम्तोभन्दा जरुरी।','Maile khet kineko chhu, gaera hernaiparchha. Maile paanch hal goru kineko chhu, jaanchnaiparchha. Maile bharkhar bihe gareko chhu, tyasaile aauna sakdinan. Jamin, kaam, pariwaar — kunai pani kharaab hoina, tara sabai nimtobhandaa jaruri.','I have bought a field and must go and see it. I have bought five pairs of oxen and must try them out. I have just got married, so I cannot come. Land, work, family — none of it evil, all of it more urgent than the invitation.','Luke 14:18–20'],
['नोकरले खबर ल्यायो। मालिक रिसाए — अनि उनले त्यस्तो काम गरे जुन कुनै पनि घरधनीले गर्दैनथ्यो। छिटो गएर सडक र गल्लीहरूमा जाऊ, र गरिब, अपाङ्ग, दृष्टिविहीन र लङ्गडालाई भित्र ल्याऊ।','Nokarle khabar lyaayo. Maalik risaae — ani unle tyasto kaam gare jun kunai pani ghardhaneele gardainathyo. Chhito gaera sadak ra galleeharumaa jaau, ra garib, apaang, drishtiwiheen ra langadaalaai bhitra lyaau.','The servant reported back. The master was angry — and then he did something no host would do. Go out quickly into the streets and alleys and bring in the poor, the crippled, the blind and the lame.','Luke 14:21'],
['नोकरले त्यसै गर्‍यो र भन्यो — मालिक, भयो, तर अझै ठाउँ छ। त्यसैले मालिकले भने — गाउँका बाटा र बारका छेउमा जाऊ, र तिनीहरूलाई भित्र ल्याऊ — मेरो घर भरिएको चाहन्छु।','Nokarle tyasai garyo ra bhanyo — maalik, bhayo, tara ajhai thaaun chha. Tyasaile maalikle bhane — gaaunkaa baataa ra baarkaa chheumaa jaau, ra tiniharulaai bhitra lyaau — mero ghar bharieko chaahanchhu.','The servant did it and said: it is done, sir, and there is still room. So the master said: go out to the country roads and the hedges and make them come in — I want my house full.','Luke 14:22–23'],
['निम्तो पूरै खुला छ, र सधैंभरि खुला रहँदैन। आफ्नो ठाउँ पक्का छ भन्ने ढुक्क हुनेहरूले नै गुमाए; निम्तोको आशै नगर्नेहरू भित्र बसेर खाइरहेका छन्।','Nimto purai khulaa chha, ra sadhainbhari khulaa rahandaina. Aaphno thaaun pakkaa chha bhanne dhukka huneharule nai gumaae; nimtoko aashai nagarneharu bhitra basera khaairahekaa chhan.','The invitation is wide open, and it is not open forever. The ones who were sure they had a seat were the ones who missed it; the ones who never expected an invitation are inside, eating.','Luke 14:24']]}
]}
]});
